{"artifact_digest":"sha256:6bf0d8fb1eb949a35beee69708896ad4a1d299de756e8394998864980fab69cc","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/6b/6bf0d8fb1eb949a35beee69708896ad4a1d299de756e8394998864980fab69cc.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:2a3526a069e58eb54d8f0027118c05c057248309b1d4530b297c337872e45f59","bundle_entry_key":"2510-00214-lemma-11-log","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s0_060","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-v2-20260907/bundle_s0_060.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2510-00214-lemma-11-log","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: Define $\gamma_t(x) = (2\pi t)^{-1/2}\exp\{ -x^2/(2t)\}$
	for all $t>0$ and $x\in\mathbb{R}$,
	and recall that
	$G_t(x\,,y)=\sum_{n=-\infty}^{\infty} \{
	\gamma_t(x-y-2n)-\gamma_t(x+y+2n)\}$, valid for all $t>0$ and $x,y\in[0\,,1]$;
	see for example Dalang and Sanz-Sol\'e 
	[bookDS]. Thus, we may proceed as follows:
	\begin{align*}
		&\int_0^1\left| G_{t}(x\,,y)-G_{s}(x\,,y)\right|\,\mathrm{d} y
			\leq \int_0^1 \sum_{n=-\infty}^{\infty} \vert \gamma_t(x-y-2n)-
			\gamma_s(x-y-2n)\vert \, \mathrm{d} y\\
		&\hskip1.8in+
			\int_0^1 \sum_{n=-\infty}^{\infty} \vert \gamma_t(x+y+2n)-
			\gamma_s(x+y+2n)\vert\, \mathrm{d} y\\
