body:
[Theorem 13 (Predictive stability for GPs) of arXiv:2608.25706, 'Fast rates in Bayesian online learning with approximate posteriors'] Let $P$ and $Q$ be Gaussian process laws on $L^2(\bP_X)$. Then there exists an absolute constant $L_{\cM}>0$ such that
    \begin{equation}
    \cM_t(Q)-\cM_t(P)
    \le  L_{\cM}\cbr{ \W(P,\delta_{f^\star})\W(P,Q)+\W(P,Q)^2+\overline v(P,Q)\W(P,\delta_{f^\star})^2 }
\end{equation}
with $\overline v(P,Q):=\sup_{x\in\cX}\{v_P(x)+v_Q(x)\}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

