[Corollary eq:mgf-comparison of arXiv:2607.14087, 'Stochastic Domination of Gaussian Maxima: A Resolution of the Weak Simplex Conjecture'] \label[corollary]{cor:mgf}
Let $G$ be any $m\times m$ correlation matrix, let
$\xi\sim\mathcal N(0,G)$, and let
$\xi^\triangle\sim\mathcal N(0,G_\triangle)$.  Then
\begin{equation}
  \mathbb E\exp\!\left\{\lambda\max_i\xi_i\right\}
  \leq
  \mathbb E\exp\!\left\{\lambda\max_i\xi_i^\triangle\right\}
  \qquad(\lambda>0).
\end{equation}
If $G\neq G_\triangle$, then (equation eq:mgf-comparison of the paper) is strict for every
$\lambda>0$.  Equivalently, equality for any one $\lambda>0$ holds if and
only if $G=G_\triangle$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

