[Lemma prop:good_annulus_macroscopic_scale of arXiv:2609.04140, 'The conformally invariant metric on $\CLE_4$ III:\\ uniqueness'] There exist universal constants $\alpha>2$ and $R_0 > 1$ such that for all $R \geq R_0$,  there exists a constant $c_R>0$ depending only on $R$ such that the following is true.  Suppose that we have the same setup as in (prop:conformal_rectangles of the paper) and let $U_1,\ldots,U_N$ denote the connected components of the complement in $A$ of the union of the crossings of $A$ made by loops in $\overline{\Gamma}$ with height in $\{-\lambda,\lambda\}$ together with the interiors of the excursions into $A$ from the inner and outer boundary of $A$ made by such loops,  as in (rem:crossings_general_case of the paper) with $n=0$.  In the case that no loop in $\overline{\Gamma}$ with height in $\{-\lambda,\lambda\}$ crosses $A$,  we instead set $N=1$ and let $U_1$ be as in (rem:no_crossings of the paper). Let $E(\Psi)$ denote the event that the following hold.
	\begin{enumerate}
		\item 
		There are at most four crossings of $A$ made by loops in $\overline{\Gamma}$ with height in $\{-\lambda,\lambda\}$.
		\item 
		For every $j \in \{1,\ldots,N\}$ such that the boundary conditions of $\Psi|_{U_j}$ are given by the zero function,  we have that (recall the definitions of $\phi_j$,  $V_j$ and $L_j$ from (subsec:conformal_rectangles of the paper))
		\begin{align*}
			D^{V_j}_{\phi_j(\Gamma|_{U_j})}((0,L_j) \times \{0\} ,  (0,L_j) \times \{1\}) \geq c_R,
		\end{align*}
		and in the case where there is no crossing of $A$ by loops with height in $\{-\lambda, \lambda\}$, we have for all $\gamma \in \SP_A$,
		\begin{align*}
				D^{V_\gamma}_{\phi_\gamma(\Gamma|_{U_\gamma})}((0,L_\gamma) \times \{0\} ,  (0,L_\gamma) \times \{1\}) \geq c_R.
		\end{align*}

		Moreover,  in the case that there are exactly four crossings of $A$ made by loops in $\overline{\Gamma}$ with height in $\{-\lambda,\lambda\}$,  there exists for each such $j$ a collection of conformal rectangles $R_{j,m} \subseteq U_j$ for $1 \leq m \leq 8$ for which properties~(equation it:disconnecting_conformal_rectangles of the paper) and~(equation it:left_to_right_crossings_shorter_than_top_to_bottom of the paper) in the statement of (prop:conformal_rectangles of the paper) hold,  with $B$ the universal constant appearing there.
	\end{enumerate}
	Then,  we have that $\BP[E(\Psi)] \geq 1 - 2^{-\alpha R}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Corollary 32 (Global single-coordinate branching criterion) of arXiv:2604.10792, 'Variable-Length Markov Chains on Finite Quivers: Boundary-Window Identifiability, Exact De'] Fix $m<r$ and assume exact depth $r$ at $\theta_0$ together with \cref{ass:regularity}. Let $T\subset T_{\theta_0}\Theta$ be a tangent block. Suppose there exist a visible state $y\in\cS_m$ and an admissible appended edge $a$ such that, writing $y_a:=U_m(y,a)$,
\begin{enumerate}[label=\textup{(\alph*)}]
\item \begin{equation}
\Ker\bigl(Dq_{y,y_a}^{(m)}(\theta_0)|_T\bigr) \subset \Ker\bigl(Dq_{\cQ}^{(m)}(\theta_0)|_T\bigr),
\end{equation}
\item \begin{equation}
Dq_{y,y_a}^{(m)}(\theta_0)|_T\neq0,
\end{equation}
\item \begin{equation}
\rank\bigl(Dq_{\cQ}^{(r)}(\theta_0)|_T\bigr)\ge2.
\end{equation}
\end{enumerate}
Then the depth-$m$ window is not first-order locally sufficient relative to depth $r$ on $T$.

