body:
[Theorem th:EW-SHF of arXiv:2511.08479, '\Large From disordered systems to the Critical 2D Stochastic Heat Flow'] As $\vartheta\to-\infty$ we have the convergence in distribution, for any $\varphi \in C_c(\mathbb{R}^2)$,
\begin{equation}
	\sqrt{|\vartheta|} \,
	\big\{ \mathscr{Z}_t^{\vartheta}(\varphi) - {\ensuremath{\mathbb E}} [\mathscr{Z}_t^{\vartheta}(\varphi)] \big\}
	\xrightarrow[\vartheta\to -\infty]{d} \, \mathcal{N} \big( 0 \,, v_{t,\varphi}\big)\,,
\end{equation}
where $v_{t,\varphi} :=
	\int_{\mathbb{R}^2 \times \mathbb{R}^2} \varphi(x) \, K_t(x,x') \, \varphi(x') \, \mathrm{d}x \, \mathrm{d}x'$
with
$K_t(x,x') := \int_{0}^{t} \frac{1}{2u} \, e^{-\frac{|x-x'|^2}{2u}} \, \mathrm{d}u$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

