[Lemma lem:C=G of arXiv:2605.15545, 'Crossover from subcritical to critical decay: \\ random walk, self-avoiding walk, percolat'] Let $\Lambda$ be symmetric and positive-definite,
and let $x,\eta \in \mathbb{R}^d$.
Define $a^2= \eta\cdot \Lambda^{-1} \eta$.
Then
\begin{equation} 
\mathbb{C}(x;\eta,\Lambda)
=  \frac 1 {\sqrt{\det \Lambda}}
\mathbb{G}_{a}( \Lambda^{-1/2} x) e^{x\cdot \Lambda^{-1} \eta}
=  \frac {1} { \abs x^{d-2} \sqrt{\det \Lambda}}
\mathbb{G}_{a\abs x}(   \Lambda^{-1/2} \hat x )
	e^{x\cdot \Lambda^{-1} \eta} .
\end{equation}

