[Proposition prop:overlap-sde of arXiv:2507.12502, 'Quantitative Edge Eigenvector Universality for Random Regular Graphs: Berry-Esseen Bounds '] For indices $i$ with $|\lambda_i - 2| \leq N^{-2/3+\varepsilon/2}$, the overlap satisfies
\begin{equation}
\mathrm{d} X_i^{(\mathbf{q})} = \sum_{j \neq i} \frac{X_j^{(\mathbf{q})} - X_i^{(\mathbf{q})}}{\lambda_i - \lambda_j}\mathrm{d} B_{ij} - \frac{1}{2}X_i^{(\mathbf{q})}\mathrm{d} t + \mathcal{E}_i(t)\mathrm{d} t
\end{equation}
where $B_{ij} = \sqrt{N}\langle \mathbf{u}_j, \mathrm{d} W_t\mathbf{u}_i\rangle$ are martingales with $\mathrm{d}\langle B_{ij}, B_{k\ell}\rangle = \delta_{ik}\delta_{j\ell}\mathrm{d} t$, and the error satisfies
\begin{equation}
|\mathcal{E}_i(t)| \leq \frac{C_1}{N^{5/6-\varepsilon}}\left(\sum_{j \geq 2} |X_j^{(\mathbf{q})}|^2\right)^{1/2}
\end{equation}
with $C_1 = 12d^3\varepsilon^{-2}$.

