[Lemma lem:unifboundlambda of arXiv:2607.09946, 'Statistics on Yau's conjecture: Variance asymptotics'] There exists a constant $\mathfrak{K}(n,M,g;B,\varepsilon)>0$, depending on the geometry $n,M,g$ and on an additional real parameters $B,\varepsilon>0$, decreasing in $\varepsilon$, such that the following holds.
 Assume that $f$ is a $\mathcal{C}^3$ Gaussian field on $M$ satisfying (eq:assjet of the paper), with covariance $C$ such that
\begin{equation} 
\sup_{\substack{x,y\in M,
\\
\mathrm{dist}(x,y)\le  r}}
\|j^{3,3}_{x,y}C\|_{g^{\lambda}}
\le B,
\end{equation}

for some $r \le \mathrm{diam}(M,g)$, and some $\lambda>0$. Then, for any $M'\subset M$ Borel subset, we have that
\begin{equation} 

\frac{\lambda^{-2}}{r^n}
\int_{M'}\int_{B_{r}(x)} \mathbb{E} \left\{  \mathcal{L}_f(dx)\cdot \mathcal{L}_f(dy)\right\} < \mathfrak{K}(n,M,g;B,\lambda r)\mathrm{Vol}^{n}(M').
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2604.26549, 'Existence and uniqueness results of a stochastic nonlinear heat equation with a constraint'] Let $f\in \Vp$ be fixed. Let us consider the map, see \eqref{eqn-def-Nn},
		\begin{align}
			\Vp \ni v \mapsto \Nn(v):= f - (f,v)v \in \Vp.
		\end{align}
		Then, for all $v_1,v_2\in \Vp$, the map $\Nn$ is locally Lipschitz, i.e.,
		\begin{equation*}
			\|\Nn(v_1) -\Nn(v_2)\|_{\Vp} \leq \bigg(\frac{1}{\sqrt{\lambda_1}} \|f\|_{L^2(\bO)}\left(\|v_1\|_{H_0^1(\bO)} + \|v_2\|_{\Vp}\right) + \|f\|_{L^2(\bO)} \|v_1\|_{L^p(\bO)} \bigg) \|v_1-v_2\|_{\Vp},
		\end{equation*}
	where $\lambda_1$ is the first eigenvalue of the Dirichlet Laplacian.

