body:
[Theorem 29 of arXiv:2609.03070, 'Variants of order semicontinuity in Banach lattices'] The following conditions are equivalent:
\item[(i)] $F$ is monotonically complete;
\item[(ii)] Every directed norm bounded dominable subset of $F$ has a supremum in $F$;
\item[(iii)] $F$ is norm complete and every disjoint $D\subset F_{+}$ such that $D^{\vee}\subset\Ba_{F}$ has a supremum in $F$;
\item[(iv)] The order adherence of $\Ba_{F}$ in $F^{u}$ is contained in $F$;
\item[(v)] Every uo-Cauchy net in $\Ba_{F}$ has a uo-limit.

