[Lemma lem1 of arXiv:2411.01731, '$L^2$-Wasserstein contraction of modified Euler schemes for SDEs with high diffusivity and'] Under $({\bf A}_0)$, $({\bf A}_2)$ and $({\bf A}_3)$, for  $b^{(\delta)}$ given in (equation EY- of the paper) and $\pi^{(\delta)}={\mbox Id}$,
$({\bf H}_1)$ holds  with
\begin{align*}
R=R^*,~ C_R= (L_0+ L_1 )(1+R^{\ell_0})^2,~ K_R=L_0+L_1,~   K_R^*=(L_{2 }/2)\wedge L_{4 },
\end{align*}
$\theta=\gamma$ and $ \delta_R=(L_{2}/(2L_{3}))^{\frac{1}{\gamma}}\wedge1$.
Moreover,  under $({\bf A}_0)$ and  $({\bf A}_4)$,  for  $b^{(\delta)}=b$  and  $\pi^{(\delta)} $ defined in (equation ET- of the paper),
$({\bf H}_1)$ is satisfied  with
\begin{align*}
R=R_*, ~ C_R=2L_0\varphi(R),~K_R=2L_0, ~ K_R^*=L_5,~\theta=\gamma,~\delta_R=\varphi(R)^{-\frac{1}{\gamma}}.
\end{align*}

