[Theorem thm:decorrelation of arXiv:2507.12502, 'Quantitative Edge Eigenvector Universality for Random Regular Graphs: Berry-Esseen Bounds '] For distinct indices $i \neq j$ with $|\lambda_i - 2|, |\lambda_j - 2| \leq N^{-2/3+\varepsilon/2}$ and $t \leq t_* = N^{-1/3+\varepsilon}$:
\begin{equation}
|\mathbb{E}[X_i^{(\mathbf{q})}(t)X_j^{(\mathbf{q})}(t)]| \leq C_4 N^{-1/2+\varepsilon}
\end{equation}
where $C_4 = 8d\varepsilon^{-6}$. Consequently, $X_i^{(\mathbf{q})}(t)$ and $X_j^{(\mathbf{q})}(t)$ are asymptotically independent as $N \to \infty$.

