body:
[Theorem eq:rec fixed of arXiv:2608.19050, 'Online Permutation Embedding: \\ Optimal Stopping and Scaling Laws'] Set $\beta(\emptyset) = 0$. Then,
            \begin{equation}
        \beta(\pi)
        =
        \min_{0 \le a < b \le 1}
        \cb{
            \frac{1}{b-a}
            +
            \frac{1}{b-a}
            \int_{a}^{b}
                \frac{\beta(L(\pi))}{x}
                +
                \frac{\beta(R(\pi))}{1-x}
            \, dx
        }.
    \end{equation}
    Here, $\beta(\emptyset)/0 := 0$ by convention. That is, terms from empty subpermutations are omitted from the integrand. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Corollary cor:oco-games of arXiv:2608.25182, 'Minimax Alternating Regret \\for the Experts Problem and Online Convex Optimization'] Consider a two-player game with action sets $\mathcal{X}$ and $\mathcal{Y}$ of dimensions $d_x$ and $d_y$, respectively, and losses in $[-1,1]$ that are convex in each player's own action. Suppose both players use Option I of Algorithm~(alg:continuous-althedge of the paper) with $\eta=1/10$ in the alternating learning dynamic of [hait2025alternating]. Then the empirical distribution assigning mass $1/(2T)$ to each of the $2T$ indexed profiles $\{(x_t,y_t),(x_{t+1},y_t)\}_{t\in[T]}$ is an $\varepsilon_{\mathrm{CCE}}$-approximate coarse correlated equilibrium with
\begin{align*}
  \varepsilon_{\mathrm{CCE}}
  =
  \mathcal{O}\left(
    \frac{
        d_x\log(1+\frac{T}{d_x})+
        d_y\log(1+\frac{T}{d_y})
    }{T}
  \right).
\end{align*}
If the game is convex-concave and zero-sum, the time-averaged strategies form an $\varepsilon_{\mathrm{NE}}$-approximate Nash equilibrium with
\begin{align*}
  \varepsilon_{\mathrm{NE}}
  =
  \mathcal{O}\left(
    \frac{
      d_x\log(1+\frac{T}{d_x})
      +
      d_y\log(1+\frac{T}{d_y})
    }{T}
  \right).
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lem e:Phix01 of arXiv:2504.07255, 'A Tail-Respecting Splitting Numerical Scheme\\ for L\'evy-Driven SDEs With Superlinear Dri'] Let assumptions $\mathbf{H}^{\mathrm{Lip}_+}_A$ and
$\mathbf{H}_{A_x,A_{xx}}$ hold. Then, for $t\in [0,1]$,
\begin{align}

\|\Phi_x(t,x)\|&\leq_C 1,\\

\|\Phi_x(t,x)-\mathrm{Id}\|&\leq_C   t (1+\|x\|^\chi).
\end{align}

