[Prop 4. prop: improved lower bound for point probability of arXiv:2412.08236, 'Aging and sub-aging for Bouchaud trap models on resistance metric spaces'] For any $x \in F$, $t \geq 0$, and $\varepsilon > 0$,
  \begin{equation}
    P_{x}(X(t) = x) 
    \geq 
    \frac{\mu(\{x\})}{\mu(D_{R}(x, \varepsilon))}
    - 
    P_{x}(\tau_{B_{R}(x, \varepsilon)} \leq t).
  \end{equation}

[Lemma lem:VolumeGrowthEstimate of arXiv:2609.01825, 'On everywhere locally soluble varieties \\ in families over toric bases'] Let $A_0 \subset A_1 \subset A_2 = \mathbb R^s$ be affine subspaces of dimension $d_0 < d_1$ and $d_2 = s$ equipped with the Euclidean distance. Let $X_i \subset A_i$ be compact subsets with $\operatorname{diam}(X_0) \leq \delta_0$ and $\operatorname{dist}(X_{i-1}, X_i) \leq \delta_i$ for $i = 1, 2$. Then
	\begin{equation*}
		\operatorname{vol}(X_2) \ll_{d_0, d_1, d_2} (\delta_0 + \delta_1 + \delta_2)^{d_0} (\delta_1 + \delta_2)^{d_1 - d_0} \delta_2^{d_2 - d_1}. 
	\end{equation*}
	When $\delta_0 \geq \delta_1 \geq \delta_2$, this simplifies to $\operatorname{vol}(X_2) \ll_{d_0, d_1, d_2} \delta_0^{d_0} \delta_1^{d_1 - d_0} \delta_2^{d_2 - d_1}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

