body:
[Thm Kolmogorov of arXiv:2601.19145, 'Stochastic Persistence in Infinite Dimensions'] Let $(X_t)_{t\in[0, T]}$ be a stochastic process on $\mathbb{R}^n$ for some $T > 0$. Suppose there exist constants $\alpha, \beta, \gamma, K, C > 0$ such that:
    \begin{itemize}
        \item $\mathbb{E}[|X_t - X_s|^\alpha] \leq K|t-s|^{1 + \beta}$ for all $t,s \in [0,T]$.
        \item $\mathbb{E}[\sup_{t \in [0,T] \cap D} |X_t|] \leq C$, where $D$ denotes the dyadic numbers $\frac{k}{2^n}$.
        \item $\gamma < \beta / \alpha$.
    \end{itemize}

    Then there is a modification $\tilde{X_t}$ of $X_t$ with almost surely $\gamma$-H\"{o}lder continuous sample paths. Additionally, there is a function $A: [0,\infty) \to [0,1]$ which depends only on $T,\alpha,\beta,\gamma,K,C$ (not on $X$) and satisfies: \begin{itemize}
        \item $\lim_{M \to \infty} A(M) = 0$.
        \item $\mathbb{P}(\|\tilde{X}\|_\gamma > M) \leq A(M)$, where $$\|\tilde{X}\|_\gamma \coloneqq |\tilde{X}_0| + \sup_{0 \leq s < t \leq T} \frac{|\tilde{X}_t - \tilde{X}_s|}{t-s} \,.$$
    \end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem:proplo of arXiv:2505.12187, 'Speeding up quantum Markov processes through lifting'] Under (assump:overdp of the paper), $\sigma_o$ is the reduced state of $\sigma$ on $\mathcal{F}(\mathcal{L}_S)$. Moreover, the fixed-point algebra $\mathcal{F}(\mathcal{L}_O)$ of $\mathcal{L}_O$ defined on $\mathcal{F}(\mathcal{L}_S)$ is characterized by 
    \begin{align} 
        \mathcal{F}(\mathcal{L}_O) = \{X \in \mathcal{F}(\mathcal{L}_S)\,;\ \mathcal{L}_A (X) = 0\} = \mathcal{F}(\mathcal{L}_\gamma)\,,
    \end{align}
    where the operators $\mathcal{L}_S$ and $\mathcal{L}_A$ satisfy (asspA of the paper).

