[Lem 46 of arXiv:2510.23423, 'One-arm exponents of the high-dimensional Ising model'] Let $d\geq 2$ and $G=(V,E)\subset H=(V',E')$ be two subgraphs of $\mathbb Z^d$. For every $\beta\geq 0$, and every $x,y \in V'$,
\begin{equation}
	\langle \sigma_x\sigma_y\rangle_{H,\beta}-\langle \sigma_x\sigma_y\rangle_{G,\beta}\leq \sum_{u\in \partial V}\langle \sigma_x\sigma_u\rangle_{G,\beta}\langle \sigma_u\sigma_y\rangle_{H,\beta},
\end{equation}
where $\p V:= \{ x\in V : \exists x'\in V' \setminus V \text{ with } xx' \in E' \}$.

