[Lem convexbifurcation of arXiv:2608.30031, 'Ziggurats, taut foliations, and contact structures'] After some arbitrarily $C^\infty$-small perturbation of $\xi$, there exists finitely many times $0 < t_1 < \dots < t_N < 1$ such that 
    \begin{itemize}
        \item If $t \neq t_i$, then $S_t$ is $\xi$-convex ,
        \item At $t=t_i$, a pair of parallel closed characteristics of $\xi|_{S_t}$ is born or dies.
    \end{itemize}
    Moreover, when a pair of characteristics is born (in forwards time), a $\flat$ annulus appears between them, and when a pair of characteristics dies, a $\sharp$ annulus disappears between them (see \zcref{fig:birthdeath}). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

