[Thm mainresult of arXiv:2607.28817, 'Limiting spectral distribution for the adjacency matrix of the Watts--Strogatz random grap'] Let $(K_n)_{n\ge1}$ be a sequence of even integers satisfying $0< K_n < n$ for all sufficiently large values of $n$, and let $(p_n)_{n\ge1}$ be a sequence in $(0,1]$. Let $A_n$ denote the adjacency matrix of $WS_n(K_n, p_n)$. If
\begin{equation}
    p_nK_n\;\xrightarrow[n\to\infty]{}\;\infty
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
    \frac{K_n}{n}\;\xrightarrow[n\to\infty]{}\;0
\end{equation}
then the empirical spectral distribution $\mu_{\frac{A_n}{\sqrt{K_n p_n(2- p_n)}}}$ of the normalized adjacency matrix $\frac{A_n}{\sqrt{K_n p_n(2- p_n)}}$ converges weakly in probability to the semicircle law $\mu_{\mathrm{SC}}$ as $n \to \infty$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem RPD_Uniformity of arXiv:2607.12061, 'Models for species evolution with random deaths'] Let $f^\dagger_c=\frac{qr}{p}$. Then for any $f^\dagger_c\le a<b\le1$,
\[
\frac{L_n(b)-L_n(a)}{n}
\stackrel{\mathbb{P}}{\to}
(p-q)\left(\frac{b-a}{1-f^\dagger_c}\right), \qquad \text{as } n \to \infty.
\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

