[Lemma 21 (Estimate of \(\mathcal P\) and \(\mathcal P'\)) of arXiv:2609.01436, '2609.01436'] The series in \eqref{eq:Pcal} converges uniformly on
$[t_0,\infty)$ and defines a bounded, nondecreasing, locally absolutely
continuous function.  It satisfies
\begin{equation}
 0\leq\mathcal P(t)\leq\Theta_j(h),
 \qquad t\geq t_0,
\end{equation}
and, for almost every $t\geq t_0$,
\begin{equation}
 \mathcal P'(t)
 =
 \sum_{\substack{k\geq j\\
                  Z_k(t)<\Lambda_k(h)}}
 \frac{\omega_k(h)}{\Lambda_k(h)}Z_k'(t)\geq \sum_{\substack{k\geq j\\
                  Z_k(t)<\Lambda_k(h)}}
 \frac{A_k(t)^2}{\omega_k(h)}.
\end{equation}

