[Definition 11 of arXiv:2608.29157, 'Dilator-based analysis of $\KP$'] We define $\psi(D)\subseteq \psi^+(D)$ recursively as follows:
    \begin{equation*}
        \psi(\sigma)\in \psi(D)\iff \supp^D_{\psi^+(D)}(\sigma)\subseteq \psi(D) \land D\bigl(\psi^+(D)\bigr)\vDash \hat\sfK^D(\sigma) < \sigma.
    \end{equation*}
    Here $X<\sigma$ denotes ``For every $x\in X$, $x<\sigma$.''

[Conjecture conj:profile of arXiv:2412.05491, 'Near-critical and finite-size scaling for \\ high-dimensional lattice trees and animals'] Let $d>8$.
For lattice trees or lattice
animals on $\mathbb{T}_r^d$, there are positive constants $\lambda_1,\lambda_2$ such that,
for all $x\in \mathbb{T}_r^d$ and all $s \in \mathbb{R}$,
\begin{equation}
    G_{p_c +sV^{-1/2}}^\mathbb{T}(x) - G_{p_c}(x)
    \sim
    \lambda_1 I_0(\lambda_2 s) \frac{1}{V^{3/4}}
\end{equation}
as $V \to \infty$.
By summation over all $x \in \mathbb{T}_r^d$,
\begin{equation}

    \chi^\mathbb{T}(p_c+sV^{-1/2}) \sim  \lambda_1 I_0(\lambda_2 s) V^{1/4}.
\end{equation} (Stated as a conjecture by the paper; open unless the paper says otherwise.)

[Prop mass of arXiv:2607.01877, 'Coupling some conditioned L\'evy trees with the Kesten tree'] Assume~(equation eq:hyp-param of the paper)-(equation eq:decroissant of the paper) hold (in particular the branching meachnism $\psi$  is
  critical, that is $\psi'(0)=0$). Let $F$ be bounded nonnegative measurable
  function on ${\mathbb T}$. We have:
 \begin{equation}

\lim_{r\rightarrow \infty } {\mathbb N}^\psi_r\left[  
 F( {\mathrm R}_h({\mathcal T}^{\mathbf{\mathrm{mass}}}_r)) \right]  
=\lim_{r\rightarrow \infty } {\mathbb E}^{\varphi, r}\left[  
 F( {\mathrm R}_h({\mathcal K}^{\mathbf{\mathrm{mass}}}_r)) \right]  
={\mathbb E}^\psi\left[  F({\mathrm R}_h( {\mathcal K})) \right].
\end{equation}

