body:
[Proposition prop:jump-correction of arXiv:2606.28869, '\bfseries A General Theory of Paths:\\ \large Signatures, Jump Lifts, and Expected Signatu'] For every finite-variation c\`adl\`ag{} path,
\begin{equation}
\mathbb X^{M}_{s,t}-\mathbb X^{I}_{s,t}
=\frac12\sum_{s<u\le t}\Delta X_u\otimes\Delta X_u.
\end{equation}
The Marcus lift satisfies the geometric shuffle identity; the forward It\^o{} lift satisfies it if and only if the total jump-square correction vanishes at level two.

