\begin{equs}
     \mathbb{E} \big( \widetilde{B}^{s,1}_{t, T}\widetilde{B}^{s,1}_{u, v} \big)=  \mathbb{E} \big(B^1_{t, T}B^1_{u, v} \big)-  \mathbb{E} \big( \widebar{B}^{s,1}_{t, T} \widebar{B}^{s,1}_{u, v} \big).
\end{equs}
It follows from the covariance of $B$ (see also [friz2006]) that $|\mathbb{E} \big( B^1_{t, T}B^1_{u, v} \big)| \lesssim |v-u|^{2H}$ so we only focus on bounding the second term on the right hand side of the above equality. 
    We have 
