  If $s \in W^{k-1, p}\Gamma(f^*TX)$, then $f^*T\iota(s)\in W^{k-1, p}(M, \bR^N)$. This means that there is a sequence $(a_l)\in C^\infty(M, \bR^N)^\bN$ with 
  \begin{equation}
    a_l  \to f^*T\iota(s) \quad \text{ in } W^{k-1, p}(M, \bR^N).
  \end{equation}
  Now, for every $l \in \bN$, define $h_l \in ...","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:2cfbe5a6805a0d4dd8ae6e5109d6551723f79032036467e2b70ee03cacb3565d","revision_digest":"sha256:07fe7d87994b94f6e8409930c6b9cccf7b5f931685363ba85d7056013dc56df4","source_id":"arxiv:2608.26803","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-07","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

