 \mathsf{ord}_{\mathrm{loc}} (W , \| \cdot \|_p ) = \mathsf{ord}_{\mathrm{loc}} (W , \| \cdot \|_\infty )
\end{equation}
and,  in particular,  that the order spectrum is universal across $L^p$-norms on $\Omega$ ? (Stated as a question by the paper; open unless the paper says otherwise.)

[Lemma 9 of arXiv:2609.02790, 'Full-Model Optimality for Tunable Linear Generative Priors in Compressed Sensing'] Under the same assumptions as Lemma \ref{Under_E(k)}, for fixed $m \in [1,n]$, $k \in [m+1,n]$, let $T_1(k)=\big\langle G_k^2,P_{G_k^TA_k^T} \big\rangle=\big\langle G_k^2,P_{M_k^T} \big\rangle$  ,
\begin{equation}
T_1(k)-T_1(k-1) = \sum_{i=1}^{k-1}\big(\sigma_i^2-\sigma_k^2\big)\big(P_{M_k^T}-P_{M_{k-1}^T}\big)_{ii} \leq 0 
\end{equation}
and $T_1(k)$ is decreasing monotonically. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

