[Proposition prop:mellin-mapping-comp of arXiv:2609.00698, 'Kinetic Wedge Layers and Diffusive Limit of Neutron Transport in Polygonal Domains'] Fix $\Omega$, its sector charts, the ray-lifting convention of Section~(subsec:harmonic-lifts-comp of the paper), and finite power-logarithmic index sets $I_{\ell,i}$ at every $V_\ell$, $1\le \ell\leN_{\rm v}$, $i=1,2$. Assume that the following hypothesis hold:

\begin{enumerate}[label=\textup{(A\arabic*)},leftmargin=*,itemsep=0.8em,
before={\let\fullwidthdisplay\relax}]

\item \emph{Vertex geometry and target weight.} Let $V_m$ be the selected vertex. After translation and rotation, $V_m=0$ and $\Omega\cap B_{\ell_{\mathrm{vtx}}}=K_{\omega_m}\cap B_{\ell_{\mathrm{vtx}}}$ with $0<\omega_m<2\pi$, $K_{\omega_m}$ the sector of (equation eq:wedge-sector-def of the paper). Convexity is not used in this proposition. 
Let $q\in\mathbb N$, $q\ge2$, $0<\gamma<1$, $B\in\mathbb N_0$, and $\sigma>0$ be noncritical for the Dirichlet pencil at $V_m$:
\begin{align}
 \sigma
 \neq
 \lambda_{m,n},
 \qquad n\in\mathbb N.

\end{align}
By the choice of $\ell_{\mathrm{vtx}}$, the singular-part cutoff may be taken with $\chi_m^{\rm sing}=1$ on $B_{\ell_{\mathrm{vtx}}}(V_m)$, all others vanishing there.

\item \emph{Ray germs at the selected vertex.} Assume the germ exponents at $V_m$ lie below the target weight, $I_{m,i}\subset\{(\lambda,b):\lambda<\sigma,\ b\in\mathbb N_0\}$ for $i=1,2$, and write the two incident-ray traces as
\begin{align}
