 \nm{h_{\rm rem}}_{H^{\frac{1}{2}}(\partial\Omega)}
 +
 \nm{f^{\rm cut}}_{C^{q-2,\gamma}(\overline\Omega)},

\end{align}
is finite. Two abbreviations used in the conclusions are then defined from it. The germ size 
\begin{align}
    \mathcal A_{\rm germ}(h):=\sum_{\ell=1}^{N_{\rm v}}\sum_{i=1}^2\sum_{(\lambda,b)\in I_{\ell,i}}\abs{a_{\ell,i,\lambda,b}}
\end{align}
is a finite quantity making the topology on the fixed germ class explicit. It sums over all vertices, since the data is global. The data size is
\begin{align}
    \mathcal A^{\rm ell}_{m,\sigma}(h):=\sum_{i=1}^2\nm{\mathcal R_{m,i}}_{\mathcal C_{\sigma,B}^{q,\gamma}(0,\ell_{\mathrm{vtx}})}+\mathcal N_{\rm far}+\mathcal A_{\rm germ}(h).
\end{align}
\end{enumerate}

Write $H_{{\rm ray},m}$ for the sum of the normalized local harmonic lifts of every displayed term of (equation eq:mellin-ray-data-comp of the paper), that is the degree-zero, zero-exponent logarithmic, nonresonant and normalized resonant lifts of Section~(subsec:harmonic-lifts-comp of the paper). Its coefficients are fixed locally and linearly by the $a_{m,i,\lambda,b}$. The conclusions are the following:
