body:
[Theorem thm1:srd of arXiv:2506.17168, '{\bf Scaling limits for sample autocovariance operators of Hilbert space-valued linear pro'] Let $\{X_n\}_{n \in \mathbb Z}$ be an $\mathbb{H}$-valued linear process (equation eq:linear_process of the paper), and consider its autocovariance operators $(\widehat \Gamma_{N,h}, h = 0,\dots,H)$ given in (equation eq:SampleAutoShort of the paper) with $\widehat \Gamma_{N,h} \in \operatorname{HS}(\mathbb{H})$ for all $h$ with a slight abuse of notation. Suppose (equation cond:srd-improved_1 of the paper) and 
\begin{equation} 
  \operatorname{E} \| \varepsilon_{0} \|^4_{\mathbb{H}}< \infty. 
\end{equation}
    Then,
    \begin{equation}
        \sqrt{N} \begin{pmatrix}
            \widehat \Gamma_{N,0} - \Gamma_{0} \\
            \vdots \\
            \widehat \Gamma_{N,H} - \Gamma_{H}
        \end{pmatrix} \xrightarrow{d} 
        G \doteq
        \begin{pmatrix}
            G_0 \\
            \vdots \\
            G_H
        \end{pmatrix} \in (\operatorname{HS}(\mathbb{H}))^{\times (H+1)},
    \end{equation}
    where the weak convergence holds in the topology of $(\operatorname{HS}(\mathbb{H}))^{\times (H+1)}$, and $G$ is the centered Gaussian element of $\operatorname{HS}(\mathbb{H})^{\otimes (H+1)}$ with covariance operator $\Sigma$ given in (equation eq:Sigma of the paper)--(equation def:def:Aq-C of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

