[Definition def:NSE_cutoff of arXiv:2607.15140, 'On the absence of blow-up in the 3D Navier-Stokes equations with transport noise'] Fix $R,\mu,\varepsilon>0$ and $q,p\in (2,\infty)$ satisfying (equation eq:condition_pq_subcritical_scaling_cutoff of the paper). Let $u_0\in \mathbb{B}^{1-2/p}_{q,p}(\mathbb{T}^3)$ and 
$$
w_{{\rm cut,d}} \in L^{2p}({\mathbb R}_+;\mathbb{L}^{2q}(\mathbb{T}^3))\cap L^2_{{\rm loc}}([0,\infty);\mathbb{H}^1(\mathbb{T}^3))\cap C([0,\infty);\mathbb{H}^{-\varepsilon}(\mathbb{T}^3)) .
$$
We say that $w_{{\rm cut,d}}$ is a weak $(p,q)$-solution to the {{\normalfont{3D NSEs}}} with cutoff (equation eq:navier_stokes_cutoff_det of the paper) if for all divergence-free vector fields $\varphi\in C^{\infty}(\mathbb{T}^3;{\mathbb R}^3)$ and all $t\in {\mathbb R}_+$, it holds that 
\begin{align*}
\langle w_{{\rm cut,d}}(t),\varphi\rangle
&=\int_{\mathbb{T}^3} \varphi\cdot (u_0-\overline{u}_0)
+\Big(1+\frac{3\mu}{5}\Big)\int_0^t\int_{\mathbb{T}^3}
\, w_{{\rm cut,d}}\cdot\Delta \varphi \,\mathrm{d} x \,\mathrm{d} s\\
&+\int_0^t\int_{\mathbb{T}^3}
\big[ (w_{{\rm cut,d}}\otimes \overline{u}_0)+ \phi_{p,q}^R(\cdot,w_{{\rm cut,d}})\,(w_{{\rm cut,d}}\otimes w_{{\rm cut,d}})\big] : \nabla \varphi\,\mathrm{d} x \,\mathrm{d} s.
\end{align*}

[Lem hq2 of arXiv:2411.04081, 'A Multi-level Monte Carlo simulation for invariant distribution of Markovian switching L\''] Under all assumptions of  Proposition (dinh ly 2 of the paper), for any $p \in [2;p_0]$,  there exists a positive constant $C_p$, which does not  on  $\Delta$, such that
	\begin{equation*}
		\sup_{t \geq 0} \mathbb{E} \left[  |\widehat{X}_t - \widehat{X}_{\underline{t}}|^p \big| \mathcal{F}_{\underline{t}}  \right] +
	\sup_{t \ge 0}\mathbb{E} \left[  |\widehat{X}_t - \widehat{X}_{\underline{t}}|^p \right] \le C_p\Delta.
	\end{equation*}

