[Thm mamporia of arXiv:2606.24385, 'Gradient Mean-Field Dynamics with Measure-Valued States: Well-Posedness, Chaos, and Long-T'] {mamporia2004}}]
Let $\phi\in {\mathcal H}_{Q}(L(({\mathscr{F}}(U),{\mathscr{F}}(U))))$, and $L_{\phi}: ({\mathscr{F}}(U))^{\ast}\rightarrow {\mathscr{F}}(U)$, $x^{\ast}\mapsto \int_{0}^{t}\int_{\Omega}\phi(s,w)Q\phi^{\ast}(s,\omega)x^{\ast}{\rm d} s{\mathbb{P}}(\omega)$ belongs to $\mathscr{R}_{2}({\mathscr{F}}(U))$. Then there exists the stochastic integral $\int_{0}^{t}\phi {\rm d} W_{s}^{Q}$, and
\begin{align}
  {\mathbb E}\norma{\int_{0}^{t}\phi {\rm d} W_{s}^{Q}}_{{\rm BL}}^{2}<+\infty.  
\end{align}
Furthermore, the process $\int_{0}^{t}\phi {\rm d} W_{s}^{Q}$ has a.s. continuous sample paths.

