[Proposition prop:discrete of arXiv:2603.28161, 'Boundary four-point connectivities of conformal loop ensembles'] Let $x_1<x_2<x_3<x_4$. There exist constants $C,C'\in(0,\infty)$ such that
\begin{align}
\lim_{\delta\to0}\delta^{-\frac{4}{3}}\mathbbm{P}^\delta[x_1^\delta\leftrightarrow x_2^\delta\leftrightarrow x_3^\delta\leftrightarrow x_4^\delta]=C G^{(1234)}(x_1,x_2,x_3,x_4),\\
\lim_{\delta\to0}\delta^{-\frac{4}{3}}\mathbbm{P}^\delta[x_1^\delta\leftrightarrow x_2^\delta\not\leftrightarrow x_3^\delta\leftrightarrow x_4^\delta]=C' G^{(12)(34)}(x_1,x_2,x_3,x_4).
\end{align}

[Cor of arXiv:2505.11700, 'Distribution of the cokernels of determinantal row-sparse matrices'] Suppose that the following hold: 
\begin{enumerate}
\item 
for every prime $p$, $p \nmid k_n$ for all sufficiently large $n$;
\item 
for every $\epsilon>0$, $k_n < n^{\epsilon}$ for all sufficiently large $n$;
\item 
for every $\delta >0$, $\delta \log\log n < k_n$ for all sufficiently large $n$. 
\end{enumerate}
Let $S$ be a finite set of primes and for each $p \in S$, let $G_p$ be a finite abelian $p$-group. Then
$$
\lim_{n \to \infty} \mathbb{P}\left(\bigoplus_{p\in S}\mathrm{cok}(A_n)_p \cong \bigoplus_{p\in S} G_p\right) = \prod_{p\in S} \frac{1}{|\mathrm{Aut}(G_p)|}\prod_{j=1}^{\infty}(1-p^{-j})=  \prod_{p \in S} \nu_{\mathrm{CL}, p}(G_p).
$$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 22 of arXiv:2603.28093, 'Random Stability of Random Variables'] Assume $\mathbb E[X] < \infty$. We can define $L$ as a complex-valued function on the half-plane $\mathbb H = \{z \in \mathbb C\mid \mathrm{Re}(z) > 0\}$. This function is analytic on $\mathbb H$, and we have: 
\begin{equation}

\frac{1 - L(z)}{z} \to \mathbb E[X],\quad z \to 0,\quad \mathrm{Re}(z) > 0.
\end{equation}

