[Lemma 15 of arXiv:2605.10150, 'Rough path theory and an introduction to rough partial differential equations'] Let $\beta \in (\frac{1}{3},\frac{1}{2}]$ and $\alpha \in (0,\beta)$ be arbitrary. Then for each rough path $\mathbf{X} = (X,\bbx) \in \scrc^{\beta}([0,T],V)$ we also have $\mathbf{X} \in \scrc^{\alpha}([0,T],V)$ and the estimate
\begin{align*}
\interleave \mathbf{X} \interleave_{\alpha} \leq \| X \|_{\beta} T^{\beta-\alpha} + \| \mathbb{X} \|_{2\beta} T^{2(\beta-\alpha)}.
\end{align*}

