[Lemma lemma2 of arXiv:2412.06086, 'Zeros of conditional Gaussian analytic functions, random sub-unitary matrices and q-series'] For every $q\in (0,1)$, $t\ge 0$ and $x\in \mathbb{C}\backslash\{0\}$,
\begin{align}
F(x,t;q)=\frac{(q;q)_\infty}{2\pi i}\oint_{\mathcal{C}}\frac{e^{-\log x\log z/\log q}}{(z;q)_\infty}e^{t(1-z)}dz
\end{align}
where ${\mathcal{C}}$ is a clockwise Hankel contour around the positive real axis from $\infty-i0$ to $\infty+i0$
that can be deformed to run along the straight line $(\rho-i\infty,\rho+i\infty)$ for $0<\rho<1$.

