[Lemma 19 of arXiv:2604.01978, 'Homogenized Transformers'] Under \eqref{eq: tformers.at.initialization}, we have  $b_{{\uprho_*}}[\mu]\equiv 0$ and
\begin{equation*}
    \mathsf{K}[\mu](x_i,x_j)=\frac1d\proj_{x_i} \E_\bA \< \mathsf{m}_{\upbeta,\bA}[\mu](x_i),\mathsf{m}_{\upbeta,\bA}[\mu](x_j)\>  I_d\,\proj_{x_j},
\end{equation*} 
where 
\begin{equation*} 
    \mathsf{m}_{\upbeta,\bA}[\mu](x):=\frac{1}{\mathscr{Z}_{\bA}[\mu](x)}\int e^{\upbeta\<\bA x,y\>}y\mu(\de y).
\end{equation*}
Here, $\mu=\mu_X$ is the empirical measure.

