body:
[Proposition prop_C of arXiv:2607.11469, 'Breuer-Major-Donsker invariance principle'] Suppose $\varphi\in L^2(\gamma)$ and the  processes $V_n$ 
and $\widetilde V_n$ are given as in (equation def_VN of the paper) and (equation def_VN2 of the paper).
Let $\{b_n\}_{n\geq 1}$ be a deterministic sequence of real numbers 
with $\liminf_{n\to+\infty} b_n > 0$.
Let $\mathcal{V}$ be a random element of  $\mathbf{C}([0,1])$. 
Then, the following equivalence holds:
\begin{align}
\frac{V_n}{b_n}  \Longrightarrow \mathcal{V}
\quad\text{in $\mathbf{D}([0,1])$}
\end{align}
if and only if
\begin{align}
\frac{\widetilde V_n}{b_n} \Longrightarrow  \mathcal{V}
\quad\text{in $\mathbf{C}([0,1])$}.
\end{align}
Consequently, the conclusions of Theorems~(thm_BMD1 of the paper) and (thm_BMD2 of the paper), 
and hence of Corollary (cor_FBM of the paper), 
also hold in $\mathbf{C}([0,1])$ after replacing $V_n$ by $\widetilde V_n$
and taking $b_n =1$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Definition plouf of arXiv:2603.17861, 'Gaussian concentration, integral probability metrics, and coupling functionals\\ for infin'] Let $\mu\in\mathscr{M}_\tau^1(\Omega)$ and let $C>0$. We say that $\mu$ satisfies the
\emph{weak thermodynamic Gaussian concentration bound with constant $C$} if
\begin{equation}

\bar{p}(f-\mu(f)|\mu)
:=
\limsup_{n\to\infty}
\frac{1}{|\ensuremath{\Lambda}_n|}
\log \int \e^{\sum_{i\in \ensuremath{\Lambda}_n}( \tau_i f -\mu(f))}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}\mu
\leq
\frac{\scaleto{C}{7pt}}{2} \|\delta f\|_1^2
\end{equation}
for every $f\in{\mathcal L}\!\!\mathrm{{\scriptscriptstyle oc}}(\Omega_{})$.

[Proposition 37 of arXiv:2609.02850, 'Canonical-row Chern flow on Bott--Samelson towers:\\ realizable-volume models for Schubert'] On the canonical-row tower,
\begin{equation}
 P_{u,\boldsymbol\kappa,\mu}(h,h_z)
 =\rho_*\!\left[
 \prod_{t=1}^{\ell}s_t^{\kappa_t}(q_t+h_z)
 \prod_{j=1}^n c_j(F_j^{(\ell)})^{d_j}
 \right].
\end{equation}

