where $s(t)$ is the unique solution to $h(s) := g'(f^{-1}(s),...,f^{-1}(s)) = t$. Solving for $s$ yields $h^{-1}(t) = s(t) =  f\bigg(\frac{(t-C)^{1/k}}{\left(\sum_i |a_i|\right)^{1/k}} \bigg)$.
