[Thm dle of arXiv:2411.14090, '{\bf Exponential Ergodicity in $\W_1$ for SDEs with Distribution Dependent Noise and Parti'] Assume {\bf(A2)} for
$$L_b^2\gamma^{-2}<\frac{3}{4}K_1.$$
Then there exists a constant $\delta_0>0$ such that when $\kappa<\delta_0$, (equation Langevin levy of the paper) has a unique invariant probability measure $\mu^\ast\in\mathscr P_1(\mathbb R^{2d})$ and there exist constants $c,\lambda>0$ such that
\begin{equation*}
  \mathbb W_1(P_t^*\eta, \mu^\ast)\leq ce^{-\lambda t}\mathbb W_1(\eta, \mu^\ast),\quad\eta\in\mathscr P_1(\mathbb R^{2d}),\, t\geq 0.
\end{equation*}

