body:
[Theorem thm:main of arXiv:2510.26960, 'Free energy fluctuations in SK and related spin glass models: \\ A literature survey'] Consider an MSK model with species density matrix $\Lambda=\Lambda_N+O(N^{-1})$ and variance profile matrix $\Delta^2$.Let $\beta_c$ be as given in (equation eq:bcrit_msk of the paper). If $\Delta^2$ is positive semi-definite, then the following statements hold for the free energy $F_N(\beta)$.
    \begin{enumerate}
    \item There exists a constant $C>0$ such that 
     \begin{equation} 
    	\Var\left(F_N(\beta_c)\right) \leq C \left( (\log N)^2 +1\right).
     \end{equation} 
    \item For fixed $\alpha>0$ and $d>0$, there is a constant $C>0$, depending only on $\alpha$ and $\delta$, such that
     \begin{equation} 
    	\Var\left(F_N(\sqrt{\beta_c^2+dN^{-\alpha}})\right) \leq C \left( (\log N)^2 + N^{1-\alpha}\right).
     \end{equation} 
    \end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

