body:
[Lemma 4 of arXiv:2608.24675, 'Towards Liouville Quantum Gravity on fractals'] For any $s>d_S/2$, the fractional Riesz kernel~\eqref{E:def_Riesz_kernel} admits the expansion
    \begin{equation*}
        k_s(x,y)=\sum_{k= 1}^\infty\lambda_{k}^{-s/2}\varphi_k(x)\varphi_k(y),\quad x,y\in K,
    \end{equation*}
   where the convergence of the series is understood in the $L^2(K\times K,\mu\otimes\mu)$-sense.

