[Prop 31 of arXiv:2511.10535, 'Eigenvalues of Brownian Motions on $\mathrm{GL}(N,\mathbb{C})$'] Given a $(\rho,\zeta)$-Brownian motion $B^N$, driven by $W^N$, there exists a constant $C_{\rho, T}$ such that for all $k\geq 0$ and $t\leq T$,
	\begin{align*}
		\E\left[\ts_N\left(\left|B^N(t) - I_N - W^N(t)\right|^{2k}\right)\right] \leq (t C_{\rho,T})^{2k} e^{C_{\rho,T} \frac{k^4}{N^2}}.
	\end{align*}

