body:
[Thm thm! of arXiv:2604.24061, 'A characterization of ruin-inducing probability measures in a renewal risk model'] The following assertions hold:
\begin{enumerate}
\item
for every  $Q{\,\in\,}\hyperlink{ms}{\mathcal M^{\mathcal H}_S}$ there exists an essentially unique pair $(\gamma,\delta){\,\in\,}\hyperlink{fp}{\mathcal F_P}{\,\times\,}\hyperlink{gp}{\mathcal G_P}$ so that the conditions 
\begin{gather}
\tag{$RM({\mathcal H})$}
\frac{dQ}{dP}{\upharpoonright}{\mathcal H}_t=e^{S_t^{(\gamma)}+T_{N_t+1}^{(\delta)}}=:L^{(\gamma,\delta)}_{t}\quad P{\upharpoonright}{\mathcal H}_t\text{-a.s.} 

\end{gather}
and 
\begin{gather}
\tag{$RM(\mathcal F)$}
\frac{dQ}{dP}{\upharpoonright}\mathcal F_t=e^{S_t^{(\gamma)}+T_{N_t}^{(\delta)}}\cdot\frac{\int_{J_t}^\infty e^{\delta(w)}\,P_{W_1}(dw)}{\int_{J_t}^\infty \,P_{W_1}(dw)}=:M^{(\gamma,\delta)}_{t}\quad P{\upharpoonright}\mathcal F_t\text{-a.s.}

\end{gather}
hold for all $t{\,\in\,}\mathbb R_+$, and  the processes $L^{(\gamma,\delta)}{\,:=\,}\{L^{(\gamma,\delta)}_{t}\}_{t\in\mathbb R_+}$ and $M^{(\gamma,\delta)}{\,:=\,}\{M^{(\gamma,\delta)}_{t}\}_{t\in\mathbb R_+}$ are  a.s. positive $(P,{\mathcal H})$- and $(P,\mathcal F)$-martingales, respectively, satisfying $\mathbb E_P\big[L^{(\gamma,\delta)}_{t}\big]{\,=\,}\mathbb E_P\big[M^{(\gamma,\delta)}_{t}\big]{\,=\,}1$; 
\item
conversely, for every pair $(\gamma,\delta){\,\in\,}\hyperlink{fp}{\mathcal F_P}{\,\times\,}\hyperlink{gp}{\mathcal G_P}$ there exists a unique probability measure $Q{\,:=\,}Q^{(\gamma,\delta)}{\,\in\,}\hyperlink{ms}{\mathcal M^{\mathcal H}_S}$ determined by 
\begin{gather}		
Q(A)=\mathbb E_P\big[\1_A\cdot L^{(\gamma,\delta)}_{t}\big]\,\,\text{ for every } t \in \mathbb R_+\text{ and } A \in {\mathcal H}_t

\tag{$\ast$}
\end{gather}
and satisfying condition (equation mart1 of the paper).
\end{enumerate}

