[Lemma 12 (Slow bridge sequence) of arXiv:2608.31157, 'Sharp Approximation Rates for Neural Networks with Affine Latent Parameterizations'] Let $f\in C([0,1]^d)$ and $K\in\N^+$.  There exist $2K^d$ samples
$y_0,\ldots,y_{2K^d-1}$ such that
\begin{equation}
 y_{\operatorname{addr}(\bmbeta)}=f(\bmbeta/K),\qquad
 \bmbeta\in\{0,\ldots,K-1\}^d,
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
 \lvert y_j-y_{j-1}\rvert
 \le\omega_f\bigl(\tfrac{\sqrt d}{K}\bigr),
 \qquad j=1,\ldots,2K^d-1.
\end{equation}

