body:
[Lemma lem:goodset_from_bigset of arXiv:2507.10531, 'Quantitative central limit theorems for exponential random graphs'] Suppose that $\Pi \subseteq \mathcal{B}_p^\eta$ with $\mathbb{P}[X \in \Pi] \geq 1 - \exp\mleft(-\Omega(n^\xi)\mright)$ for some $\xi \in (0,1)$.
Then there is a set $\Lambda \subseteq \Lambda^*$ (where $\Lambda^*$ is the set given in
Proposition (prop:goodset of the paper)) such that
\begin{equation}
    \mathbb{P}[X_t^x \in \Pi \text{ for all } 0 \leq t \leq n^3] \geq 1 - \exp\mleft(-\Omega(n^\xi)\mright)
\end{equation}
for all $x$ with $\mathbf{d}_\mathrm{Ham}(x,\Lambda) \leq 1$.
Moreover, there is some $z \in \Lambda$ for which
\begin{equation}
    \mathbb{P}[X_t^z \in \Lambda \text{ for all } 0 \leq t \leq n^3] \geq 1 - \exp\mleft(-\Omega(n^\xi)\mright).
\end{equation}

