body:
[Lemma lem:abstract-borel-submersion of arXiv:2608.02459, 'Response Calculus for Spectral Simplicity\\ and Joint Eigenvalue Densities'] Let $g=(g_1,\ldots,g_M)\in\mathcal Q^M$ and define
\begin{equation*}
 \Omega_{\nu,g}^{\rm sub}
 :=
 \left\{
 x\in\Omega_{\rm str}:
 \begin{array}{l}
 \Lambda_{n_1}^{\mu_x},\ldots,\Lambda_{n_M}^{\mu_x}
 \text{ are simple},\\[1mm]
 \det(\ell_{n_i}^{\mu_x}(g_j))_{i,j=1}^M\ne0
 \end{array}
 \right\}
\end{equation*}
Then $\Omega_{\nu,g}^{\rm sub}\in\mathcal B(X)$.

