[Lemma LemmaL2IncrementY of arXiv:2608.11178, 'A submartingale for the probability of avoiding the origin in one-point interaction ground'] Fix \(T,\gamma>0\) and \(x\in\mathbb R^3\setminus\{0\}\). Then
\begin{align}
\sup_{0<t\le T}
\int_{\mathbb R^3}
q_t^\gamma(x,y)
\left|
\mathbb Q_{T-t}^{\gamma}(y)-\mathbb Q_T^\gamma(x)
\right|^2
\,dy
<
\infty. \nonumber
\end{align}

