{"artifact_digest":"sha256:b9114f554ed1eade24bb129e57bc28af303f233ffd9b2d9eb4a485543b4fe8b1","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/b9/b9114f554ed1eade24bb129e57bc28af303f233ffd9b2d9eb4a485543b4fe8b1.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:d6e4f92136ac5073572898d3e60154ba2623e292172e163f39dac38e7c6984db","bundle_entry_key":"2609-02398-lemma-14-unimodality-of-the-sub-gaussia","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s3_150","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-20260907/bundle_s3_150.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2609-02398-lem-14-unimodality-of-the-sub-gaussia","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: \emph{Cumulant identities.} Write $q_s \coloneqq p e^{s}/(1 - p + p e^{s}) = (1 + e^{\beta_p - s})^{-1}$ for the mass that the exponential tilt of $Z_p$ at $s$ places on the upper atom. Direct differentiation of \eqref{eqn:gpsi} gives $q_s' = q_s(1-q_s)$ and
\begin{align}
&&
    g'(s) &= q_s - p, &
    g''(s) &= q_s(1 - q_s), &
    g'''(s) &= q_s(1 - q_s)(1 - 2q_s). &
& 
\end{align}
