[Lemma lem:bound_G of arXiv:2604.18558, 'Uniform analyticity of local observables in FK-percolation and analyticity of the Ising sp'] There exists $c_\epsilon>0$, going to 0 when $\epsilon$ tends to 0, such that for every $\epsilon > 0$ small enough, if $|z| < \epsilon$, then:
\begin{align*}
\sum_{\{\bar\gamma\} \in \mathfrak{I}\cap I(\Delta)} |G_z(\{\bar\gamma\})|\exp(-c_\epsilon |\mathsf{Tr}(\{ \bar\gamma \})|) \leq \phi_{\mathbb T_N,p}[F(\omega)].
\end{align*}

