[Proposition prop:mpinformal of arXiv:2411.09516, 'Sharp Matrix Empirical Bernstein Inequalities\footnote{NeurIPS 2025 Poster}'] Let $n$ be even and $ \mathbf{X} _1,\dots ,  \mathbf{X} _n$ be i.i.d.\ symmetric matrices with eigenvalues in $[0,1]$ and mean $ \mathbf{M} $. Let $ \mathbf{V} _n^*$ be the paired sample variance  $n^{-1}(( \mathbf{X} _1 -  \mathbf{X} _2 )^2+ ( \mathbf{X} _3 -  \mathbf{X} _4 )^2+ \dots + ( \mathbf{X} _{n-1} -  \mathbf{X} _n )^2)$. Then,
\begin{equation} 
     \mathbb P \left( \lambda_{\max} \left( \overline \mathbf{X} _n - \mathbf{M}  \right) \geqslant  \sqrt{  \frac{2  \|   \mathbf{V} ^*_n  \|  \log \frac{nd}{(n-1)\alpha}  }{n}}  + \mathcal{O}\left(\frac{ \log(nd/\alpha)}{ n
  }\right)\right) \leqslant \alpha.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

