[Lem perfectbounds of arXiv:2604.14122, 'The scaling limit of random walk and\\ the intrinsic metric on planar critical percolation'] Let $B\in\mathcal{B}^R_{k,n}$ and let $B^{(i)}$ be one of its superboxes. There exists a constant $c=c(\delta)>0$ such that for all $R$ sufficiently large, $k\geq 2$, $0\leq i<k$ and $n> R^k$,
\begin{equation}
    \begin{split}
        c\mathbf{P}(X_{R^{\kappa-k}} > \mathbf{q}_n) \mathbf{P}(B\textrm{ is $B^{(i)}$-important})\leq{}& \mathbf{P}(B\textrm{ is $B^{(i)}$-bad})\\
        \leq{}&\mathbf{P}(X_{R^{\kappa-k}} > \mathbf{q}_n) \mathbf{P}(B\textrm{ is $B^{(i)}$-important}) 
    \end{split}
\end{equation}

