[Defn 25 of arXiv:2607.03924, 'Tree Coordinates and Range Martingales for Positive Operator-Valued Measures'] The local variance of $X$ at $w$ is 
\begin{equation}
\Gamma_{w}\left(X\right)=\sum^{m-1}_{j=0}C^{*}_{wj}X^{2}_{wj}C_{wj}-X^{2}_{w}.
\end{equation}

[Proposition MMU2 of arXiv:2606.24304, 'Quantitative Homogenization of PDEs with Neumann boundary conditions: a probabilistic appr'] For any $h>0$ and $s \in[t, T-h]$, and { any } $\lambda \geqslant 1$, 
\begin{eqnarray*}
\mathbb{E} \Big[ e^{\lambda\left(s+\phi_s^{\varepsilon,t,x,y}\right)}\left|U_s^{\varepsilon, t, x, y}-U_{s+h}^{\varepsilon, t, x, y}\right|^2 \Big]
+\mathbb{E} \int_s^{s+h} e^{\lambda\left(r+\phi_r^{\varepsilon,t,x,y}\right)}\left|Z_r^{\varepsilon, t, x, y}\right|^2 d r 
\leqslant Ch^{\frac12}.
\end{eqnarray*}

