[Theorem thm:FP-pKP of arXiv:2608.02772, 'Non-Abelian Hirota-Miwa Equations for the KPZ Universality Class'] At every $(t, \mathbf{x}, \mathbf{a})$ with $t > 0$,
the dressed observable $\mathcal{A}$ satisfies
the matrix potential KP equation
\begin{equation}
\partial_{t,\mathbf{a}} \mathcal{A}
+ \tfrac{1}{4}\partial_{\mathbf{x}}^2 \mathcal{A}
+ \tfrac{1}{12}\partial_{\mathbf{a}}^4 \mathcal{A}
+ \tfrac{1}{2}\partial_{\mathbf{a}}
  (\partial_{\mathbf{a}}\mathcal{A})^2
+ \tfrac{1}{2}[\partial_{\mathbf{a}}\mathcal{A},
\partial_{\mathbf{x}}\mathcal{A}] = 0.
\end{equation}

[Theorem thm:observables of arXiv:2603.28936, 'Composition of random functions and word reconstruction'] For every $u\in [0,1]$ we have
\begin{align}
		\mathrm{Var}(Q_n^w(u)) &=  c(w,u)n + O(1),


\end{align}
where
	\begin{align}
		 c(w,u):= & g_k(u^2\eta_k)- g_k(u\eta_k)^2+ 2c_{\textrm{approx}}^1(w,u)g_k(u\eta_k)-c_{\textrm{approx}}^2(w,u)
+ c_{\textrm{int}}(w,u), 
	\end{align}
	where the constants $c_{\textrm{approx}}^1(w,u)$, $c_{\textrm{approx}}^2(w,u)$ and $c_{\textrm{int}}(w,u)$ are defined above and summarized altogether in Section~(subsec:def-cw-selfcontained of the paper) below.

