[Prop single-location master loop equation in the 't Hooft limit of arXiv:2411.11676, 'Surface sums for lattice Yang--Mills in the large-$N$ limit'] Let $\Lambda_N$ be an increasing sequence converging to $\mathbb{Z}^d$. Suppose that there exists a subsequence of $N$ such that $\phi_{\Lambda_N,N,\upbeta}(s)$ converges to $\phi_{\infty}(s)$ for all strings $s\in\mathcal{S}$.  Then, for every fixed non-empty string $s$ and every fixed edge $\mathbf{e}$ in $s$,
\begin{align}
	\phi_{\infty}(s) &= \sum_{s'\in \mathbb{S}_-(\mathbf{e},s)}\phi_{\infty}(s') - \sum_{s'\in \mathbb{S}_+(\mathbf{e},s)}\phi_{\infty}(s') \notag
	\\&+ \upbeta\sum_{s'\in \mathbb{D}_-(\mathbf{e},s)}\phi_{\infty}(s') - \upbeta\sum_{s'\in \mathbb{D}_+(\mathbf{e},s)}\phi_{\infty}(s').
\end{align}

[Lemma 14 (Local stability of irreducibility and visible positivity) of arXiv:2604.10792, 'Variable-Length Markov Chains on Finite Quivers: Boundary-Window Identifiability, Exact De'] Assume exact depth $r$ at $\theta_0$ together with \cref{ass:regularity}. Let $\mathcal A_r$ be the affine subspace of depth-$r$ transition arrays satisfying the forced-zero and row-sum constraints, and let $p_0=q_{\cQ}^{(r)}(\theta_0)\in\mathcal A_r$. Then there exists a relative neighborhood $\mathcal U_r\subset\mathcal A_r$ of $p_0$ such that every stochastic matrix represented by $p\in\mathcal U_r$ is irreducible on the fixed support, and for every visible state $y\in\cS_m$ used in the depth-$m$ informative map one has
\begin{equation}
\sum_{z\in\Pi_{r,m}^{-1}(y)}\pi(p)(z)>0,
\end{equation}
where $\pi(p)$ denotes the stationary law of the chain with transition matrix $p$.

[Proposition 24 of arXiv:2606.14443, 'SEMICLASSICAL LIMIT OF POLYAKOV-LIOUVILLE MEASURE and Q-Curvature Uniformization ON EVEN-D'] For all positive bounded functions $\varphi\colon M\to\R$ we have
	\begin{align*}
		\lim_{\gamma\to0}\E[\exp(-\frac1{\gamma^2}\scalar{\varphi}{\mu^{\gamma h}-1-\gamma h})]=\E[\exp(-\frac12\scalar{\varphi}{\wick{h^2}})].
	\end{align*}

