[Proposition 21 of arXiv:2609.03070, 'Variants of order semicontinuity in Banach lattices'] The following conditions are equivalent:
\item[(i)] $F$ is pointwise demicontinuous;
\item[(ii)] The common order and uo adherence of $\Ba_{F}$ in $F^{u}$ is radially bounded;
\item[(iii)] The common order and uo adherence of $\Ba_{F}$ in $F$ is radially bounded;
\item[(iv)] Every directed subset of $\Ba_{F_{+}}$ is dominable.

