[Prop 2 (The simplest Gaussian convex inequality) of arXiv:2603.25536, 'The $H^{2|2}$ monotonicity theorem revisited'] The integral
\begin{equation*}
    I=\int_{\mathbb{R}}f(x)e^{-\frac{w}{2}x^2}\frac{\sqrt{w}}{\sqrt{2\pi}}dx=\mathbb{E}[f(\mathcal{N})]
\end{equation*}
is non-increasing in $w>0$ if $f:\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R}$ is convex. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 23 of arXiv:2506.10817, 'On the Weak Error for Local Stochastic Volatility Models'] Let $Z_0,\eta$ be random variables such that $\Prob(\eta=0)=0$. Let $\Delta W$ be Gaussian with mean $0$ and variance $h$ such that $\Delta W$ is independent of $Z_0$ and $\eta$. Assume that 
    \begin{align*}
        Z_1=Z_0+\eta \Delta W.
    \end{align*} 
    Then $Z_{1}$ has a density given by a convolution-type formula: 
    \begin{align*}
        f_{Z_{1}}(x)=\E\Bigl[\varphi_{h\eta^2}\bigl(x-Z_0\bigr) \Bigr]
    \end{align*}

[Proposition prop_upper_bound_LSI_quadratic of arXiv:2503.24372, 'A criterion on the free energy for log-Sobolev inequalities in mean-field particle systems'] Let $V$ satisfy Assumption~(ass_doublewell of the paper). 
There is $C>0$ such that, for all $T > T_c$, one gets for  $N$  large enough 
\begin{equation}
\gamma^N_{\mathrm{LS}}(T)
\leq  C (T-T_c) .
\end{equation}

[Lemma lem: b3 connector relations of arXiv:2608.27771, 'A normal form for the Thin Flat Surfaces category'] The three relations involving  $b_3$ in Figure (Fig:b3-equivalences of the paper) hold in the $\mathbf{TFS}$ category.
