[Lemma lem:JordanLowerBoundLower of arXiv:2606.24465, 'History estimation in random recursive trees:\\Pointwise approach via iterated Jordan cent'] For the Jordan ordering $\widehat{\sigma}_J$, there exist positive constants $C, c^\prime$ and $c$ such that for any $n\geq 1$, any vertex $v\in[n/2]$ and any $S\in[1,c^\prime v]$

    \begin{equation}
        \mathbb{P}\left(\widehat{\sigma}_J(v)\leq \frac{v}{S}\right) \geq c e^{-CS}.
    \end{equation}

