[Proposition prop:Wellsforheight of arXiv:2604.24743, 'The impact of disorder and non-convex interactions on delocalisation of height functions'] For any $L \in \ensuremath{\mathbb{N}}$, any $x \in \Lambda_L$ and any $\beta \geq 0$, one has the inequality
\begin{equation*}
     \mathbb{E}_{\nu_{L , \beta}} \left[ \mathrm{Var}_{L, \beta , r}^{\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}-\mathrm{XY}}\left[ \varphi(x) \right] \right] \geq \mathrm{Var}_{L, \beta/4}^{\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}-\mathrm{XY}}\left[ \varphi(x) \right].
\end{equation*}
Similarly, for any $L \in \ensuremath{\mathbb{N}}$, any $n \geq 2$ and any $\beta_1 , \beta_2 \geq 0$,
\begin{equation*}
    \mathbb{E}_{\nu_{L , n , \beta_1, \beta_2}} \left[ \mathrm{Var}_{L, n , \beta_1, \beta_2 , r}^{\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}-\mathrm{XY}} \left[ \varphi(x) \right] \right] \geq \mathrm{Var}_{L , n , \beta_1/2, \beta_2}^{\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}-\mathrm{XY}}\left[ \varphi(x) \right].
\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem of arXiv:2411.05534, 'Inverse problems for stochastic partial differential equations'] Assume (eqDou2023Assumtion1 of the paper), (eqDou2023Assumtion2 of the paper), and that $ \alpha \in (0,1] $ is a constant.
For any given $\widehat{G} \subset \subset G$ and $\varepsilon \in (0, \frac{T}{2}) $, let $ \gamma \in (0,1) $ as stated in (thmProb9 of the paper).
Then there exists a constant $ \mathcal{C} > 0 $  such that  for all $ \delta \in (0,1) $,
\begin{align*}
|y_{\tau} - y^{*}|_{L^{2}_{\mathbb{F}}(\varepsilon,T-\varepsilon;H^{1}(\widehat{G}))}
\leq
\mathcal{C} (1 + |y^{*}|_{L^{2}_{\mathbb{F}}(0,T;H^{2}(G))}) \delta^{\alpha \gamma}
,
\end{align*}
where $ y_{\tau} $ is the minimizer of the functional (eqDou2023Fucntional of the paper) with the regularization parameter  $ \tau = \delta^{2 \alpha} $.

