body:
[Prop 57 of arXiv:2507.08909, 'Annealed almost periodic entropy'] Let $\rho$ be a separable unital representation whose support is a perfect subset of $\hat{\A}$ for the Fell topology: that is, it has no isolated points.
\begin{enumerate}
\item[a.] If another separable unital representation $\pi$ weakly contains $\rho$, then $\pi \gtrsim_\rm{a} \rho$.
\item[b.] If another separable unital representation $\pi$ is weakly equivalent to $\rho$, then ${\pi \simeq_\rm{a} \rho}$.
\item[c.] If a sequence $(\pi_n)_{n\ge 1}$ converges to $\rho$ strongly, then $\t{\pi_n}$ sq-converges to $\t{\rho}$.
\end{enumerate}

[Corollary co:clttozero of arXiv:2411.09058, 'Time-dependent averages of a critical long-range stochastic heat equation'] For any $0<\kappa<\frac{d-2}{2}$,
