\frac{1}{\sqrt{t_R/R^2}} [u_{t_R/R^2}(B_1) -\omega_d]\to \mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^2) \quad \text{in law},
    \end{equation*}
    as $R \to \infty$, with $\sigma^2$ as defined in (equation eq:1stvar of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem:cpts-length of arXiv:2509.04333, 'The limiting law of the Discrete Gaussian level lines'] Fix $\varepsilon, \delta \in (0, 1)$, and $A, B$ with $B \in \ensuremath{\mathcal Y}_\delta^\blacktriangleleft(A)\setminus \{A\}$. Let $V$ be an $\varepsilon$-nice domain, and $U$ any domain. There exists $\beta_0, v_0, \delta_0, c > 0$ such that uniformly over $n$, $\beta \geq \beta_0$, and $r \geq 1 + 2\varepsilon$, we have
