[Corollary 5 (Fluctuation-Dissipation Relation) of arXiv:2606.07096, 'Non-Selection of Lagrangian Trajectories in the Zero-Noise Limit for a Class of Stochastic'] Let $W^\beta$, $u$ be as in Theorem~\ref{thm:SWP_stable} and additionally assume that $u$ is divergence-free. Then for any $\rho_0\in L^2$ and any $\kappa>0$, the associated solution $\rho^\kappa$ to the PDE~\eqref{eq:FP_PDE_stable_v2} satisfies
    \begin{equation}
        \| \rho_0\|_{L^2}^2-\|\rho^\kappa_t\|_{L^2}^2 = 2\kappa ^\beta\int_0^t \big\| |\nabla|^\beta \rho^\kappa_s\big\|_{L^2}^2 \dd s = \int_{\T^d} Var\big[ \rho_0((X^\kappa_{0,t})^{-1}(x))\big] \dd x
    \end{equation}

