[Definition of arXiv:2609.03532, 'Airy limit for the Jack process and topological expansion'] The \emph{Jack--Plancherel process}
$(\lambda^{(N)}(s))_{s\geq0}$ starts from the empty partition
$\varnothing$ and has transition kernel
\begin{equation*}
  \mathbb P\bigl(
    \lambda^{(N)}(t)=\mu\mid\lambda^{(N)}(s)=\lambda
  \bigr)
  =\mathsf P_{N,t-s}^{(\theta)}(\lambda,\mu),
  \qquad 0\leq s\leq t.
\end{equation*}

