[Theorem ContDensL of arXiv:2412.04973, 'On the Laplace equation with non-local dynamical boundary conditions'] Let $\Lambda=0$, $l > 0$, $k \in \mathbb{R}$ and $\alpha \in (0,1]$.  Let assume  $\lambda_1\geq 0.$ Let $w$ be the solution to (equation EsolVVw of the paper). Then, the solution (equation uAlfa of the paper) can be written as 
\begin{align*}
u(t,x) = \int_0^\infty w(s,x) \mathbf{P}_0(L_t \in ds)
\end{align*}
where 
\begin{align}
\int_0^\infty e^{-\lambda t} \mathbf{P}_0(L_t \in ds) = E_\alpha(-\lambda t^\alpha), \quad t \geq 0,\; \lambda \geq 0.

\end{align}

