[Theorem th:detCLT of arXiv:2604.20327, 'Persistent Homology of the Wiener Sausage II: A Central Limit Theorem for Drifted Planar B'] Let $\psi$ be a bounded Borel function supported in a compact interval
  $[r_0, r_1] \subset (0,\infty)$. Then
  \begin{equation}
    \frac{\Phi_\psi(t) - \rho_\psi t}{\sqrt{t}}
    \xrightarrow{d}_{t \to \infty}
    \mathcal{N}(0, \sigma_\psi^2),
  \end{equation}
  where
  \begin{equation}
    \sigma_\psi^2
    = \frac{1}{\mathbb{E}[\eta_0]}
      \bigl(\operatorname{Var}(Y_0) + 2\operatorname{Cov}(Y_0, Y_1)\bigr).
  \end{equation}

