[Lemma lem:apriori of arXiv:2412.05142, 'Strong convergence of the Euler scheme for singular kinetic SDEs driven by $\alpha$-stable'] Let $p\geqslant 1$ and $\epsilon>0$. Suppose that  Assumption (ass:main1 of the paper) holds. Let $M$ be as (equation def:noise of the paper) and let $Z=(X,V)$ and $Z^n=(X^n,V^n)$ satisfy (equation eq:SDE of the paper) and (equation eq:SDE-EM of the paper) correspondingly. Then for $Y:=Z-M, Y^n:=Z^n-M$ there exists a constant $C=C(d,\beta,\|b\|_{{\mathbb C}_{\boldsymbol{a}}^{\beta}},\alpha,\epsilon,p)$ so that
    \begin{align}
   \|Y_t-{\mathbb E}^sY_t  \|_{L_p(\Omega)|{\mathcal F}_s}  \leqslant C|t-s|^{1+(\frac{\beta}{\alpha}\wedge\frac{1}{p})-\epsilon},\\
         \|Y_t^n-{\mathbb E}^sY_t^n  \|_{L_p(\Omega)|{\mathcal F}_s}  \leqslant C|t-s|^{1+(\frac{\beta}{\alpha}\wedge\frac{1}{p})-\epsilon}.  
    \end{align}

