This is clearly true since $b$ is bounded and continuous.  We proceed now inductively on $m$.
We apply (equation est:two-random-norms-1 of the paper) with taking ${\mathscr G}:={\mathcal F}_s$ and $\tilde Y:=Y_t, \hat{Y}:=\Gamma_{t-s}Y_s+\int_s^tB(\Gamma_{r-s}M_s+{\mathbb E}^sY_r)dr\in{\mathscr G}$ where $B(x,v):=\left(\begin{smallmatrix} v\\beta(x,v)
    \end{smallmatrix}\right)$, $(x,v)\in{\mathbb R}^{d}\times{\mathbb R}^{d}$. By the fact that $Z=(X,V)$ ...","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:5df0ec3477560a50bd246e9c0c20352d732b1b931b590c35d988ac52f79321ba","revision_digest":"sha256:17eac0f8fcb6c81097fdb37f70ffe8c983c6d5fd00f45f4a674fada3a7ad0e30","source_id":"arxiv:2412.05142","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-08","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

