[Definition def:alpha_profile of arXiv:2604.20215, '\bf Edge Universality for Inhomogeneous Random Matrices II: Markov Chain Comparison and Cr'] Let  $f_{\alpha}(x)$ denote  the  density of $d$-dimensional   $\alpha$-stable distribution    whose characteristic function is given  by
    \begin{equation}
     \phi(t)=\begin{cases}  e^{-\frac{\sigma^2 }{2}\|t\|^2}, &\alpha=2,\\
     e^{-c_{\alpha}\|t\|^\alpha}, &0<\alpha<2, \end{cases}
 \end{equation}
 for $t\in \mathbb{R}^d$, where $c_{\alpha}>0$ and  $\sigma>0$ are fixed. With   the scaling notation
 \begin{equation}
     f_{\alpha}(x, \tau)=\tau^{-\frac{d}{\alpha}}f_\alpha( \tau^{-\frac{1}{\alpha}} {x}),
 \end{equation}
the corresponding $\alpha$-stable theta function is
\begin{equation} 
    \theta_\alpha (x,\tau)=\sum_{k\in \mathbb{Z}^d} f_{\alpha}(x+k, \tau).
\end{equation}

