[Theorem 5 of arXiv:2608.13732, '\textbf{On the First Hitting Time Problems \\ for Diffusion Processes: \\ Local Time-Space'] Assume the kernel $k(t,u)$ and the solution $\tilde f(t)$ of \eqref{VIE-1-standard1} are 
\begin{enumerate}
    \item twice continuously differentiable;
    \item  derivatives $\tilde f^{(3)}$, $\partial^3 k/\partial u^3$, and $\partial^3 k/\partial t \partial u^2$ are bounded on the domain $0 \le u \le t \le T$.
\end{enumerate}
Then, the error of the product trapezoidal rule  for VIE \eqref{VIE-1-standard1} satisfies
\begin{equation}
\max_{0 \le i \le m} |\tilde f(t_i) - \hat f_i| = \mathcal O\left(\Delta t^{3/2} \right).
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

