[Lem 23 of arXiv:2609.01358, 'Regularized spectral expansion of a Rankin--Selberg period and moments'] Let $\varphi\in\1_{n-2}\boxplus\1_1\boxplus\1_1$ be $(s,z)$-independent. Then there exists $\beta_\varphi\in\1_{n-1}\boxplus\1_1$ so that
		\begin{equation*}
			\Res_{z=\frac{n-1}{2}-\frac{n}{2}s}\Eis(\varphi,\lambda_{\mathrm{C}}(s,z))=\Eis(\beta_\varphi,\lambda_{\mathrm{E}}(s-\tfrac{1}{2})),
		\end{equation*}
		where $\lambda_{\mathrm{E}}$ is as in \eqref{eq:def-lambda-E},
		for $s$ in general position.

