[Corollary 15 of arXiv:2607.07022, 'Coordinate-wise Elephant Random Walk'] $s_n^2:=\E\left[ \langle M^{(f)}\rangle_n\right]$, $n \ge 1$ satisfies $\lim_{n\to \infty} s_n^2 / n = \sigma^2_f$.  If $\sigma_f^2>0,$ then  
    \begin{equation*}
\frac{\langle M^{(f)}\rangle_n}{s_n^2} =\dfrac{\langle M^{(f)}\rangle_n/n}{s_n^2/n} \xrightarrow[n \to \infty]{\PP} 1.
    \end{equation*}

[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2606.29131, '2606.29131'] Let $\Lambda_\e^4 f(x,y)$ be defined in \eqref{e3-3a}.
