[Lemma lem:M3 of arXiv:2608.26765, 'Beyond Client Averaging: A Client-Independent Second-Order Stationary-Bias Component in St'] There exists $C_H<\infty$ such that
\begin{equation}

  |M_3|:=|\mathbb{E}[x^3]|\le C_Hr_{\gamma,N}.
\end{equation}
In fact, the proof below yields the stronger internal estimate
\begin{equation}

  |M_3|\le C_Hv_{\gamma,N}.
\end{equation}
Only Equation~(equation eq:M3-target of the paper) is needed for the main theorem.

