body:
[Prop quadrisk of arXiv:2412.03560, 'Non-asymptotic entropic bounds for non-linear kinetic Langevin sampler with second-order s'] Let $f:\mathbb R^d\rightarrow \mathbb R$ be a bounded measurable function and, for $N,n\in\mathbb N$. Then,
\begin{equation}
      \mathfrak{R}(f,n,N,h)  \leqslant 4 \|f\|_{\infty}^2 \left( \frac1N   +   \sqrt{2\mathcal H(\mu_n^N |  \mu_\infty^N)} + \mathrm{TV} (\mu_\infty^{2,N},\bar{\mu}_*^{\otimes 2})  \right)  \, .
\end{equation}
Alternatively, if we assume that there exists $R>0$ and $(\eta_N)_{N\in\mathbb N}\in\mathbb R_+^{\mathbb N}$ such that, for all $N\in\mathbb N$ and $\mu \in \mathcal P_2(\mathbb X^N)$,
\begin{equation}

\mathcal H\left( \mu|\bar{\mu}_*^{\otimes N}\right) \leqslant R \mathcal H\left( \mu|\mu_\infty^N\right) + \eta_N\,, 
\end{equation}
  then
    \begin{equation}
    \mathfrak{R}(f,n,N,h)  \leqslant   4 \|f\|_{\infty}^2 \left( \frac1N  +   2\sqrt{\frac{\eta_N + R    \mathcal H(\mu_n^N | \mu_\infty^N)}{N} } \right)  \, . 
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

