[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2604.25336, 'Central limit theorem for slow-fast system under mixed fractional Brownian motion'] Let \(p\ge 2\) and \(\alpha\in(0,H)\). Under \textbf{H1}--\textbf{H3}. Then for all \(\epsilon\in(0,1]\),
\begin{eqnarray}
\mathbb{E}[\|x^\epsilon\|^p_{\alpha}] \le C_{x_0,T}, \quad \|\bar x\|_{\alpha}\le C_{x_0,T}
\end{eqnarray} 
where the constant \(C_{x_0,T}>0\) only depends on \(x_0\) and \(T\). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem 4 of arXiv:2608.22595, 'Sparse Additive Off-Policy Evaluation for Reinforcement Learning with Potentially Limited '] Under Assumption \ref{sparseQ}-\ref{a3}, we have 
    \begin{equation}
        ||{\widehat{\boldsymbol{\kappa}} }||_{1} \lesssim \frac{\log(nT \vee d)}{\sqrt{nT}}*d_0L,
        \end{equation}
        and \begin{equation}||\widehat{\boldsymbol{\kappa}}||_{2} \lesssim  \frac{\log(nT \vee d)}{\sqrt{nT}}*\sqrt{d_0L},
    \end{equation}
    with probability at least $1- \exp\{-c\log(nT \vee d)\}$ for some constant $c>0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem 30 (Maximal local solution and blow-up criterion) of arXiv:2606.15425, 'Well-posedness of stochastic parabolic equations with gradient nonlinearities and applicat'] Assume the conditions of Theorem \ref{thm:localexistence}. Then there exists a unique maximal local solution $(z,\tau_{\max})$ of \eqref{eq:FullNoiseSPDE} in the following sense:
\begin{enumerate}
\item (Maximality) If $(\widetilde {\bm z},\widetilde\tau)$ is any other local solution, then $\widetilde\tau\leq \tau_{\max}$ a.s. and
$\widetilde {\bm z}_t={\bm z}_t$ for all $t<\widetilde\tau$ a.s.
\item (Blow-up criterion) Let $\Xi_\sigma(t,{\bm z})$ be defined as in \eqref{eq:blowupfunctional}. Then, for any stopping time $\sigma \leq \tau_{\mathrm{max}}$, 
\begin{equation}
\limsup_{t\nearrow \tau_{\max}} \Xi_\sigma(t,{\bm z}) =\infty.
\end{equation}
almost surely on the event $\{\sigma < \tau_{\max}<T\}$,
\end{enumerate}

