[Definition cubfreeliedef of arXiv:2411.13707, 'High-degree cubature on Wiener space \\ through unshuffle expansions'] Letting $\ell_j \coloneqq \widetilde \pi_m(\log S(\omega_j))$, we say that the discrete probability $Q=\sum_{j=1}^{n}\lambda
_{j}\delta_{\ell_{j}}$ measure on $\mathcal L(\mathbb R^{1+d})$ is a \emph{degree-$m$ cubature measure on $d$-dimensional Wiener space with drift} if
\begin{equation*}
\mathbb{E}[\widetilde \pi_{m}( S_{0,1}(\circ \widehat B))] = \mathbb E_{Q}[\widetilde\pi_{m}\exp(\ell)].
\end{equation*}

