[Theorem thm1 of arXiv:2508.09291, '1+O(1) asymptotics for loop percolation in five and higher dimensions'] Recall that ${\mathcal C }_0$ is the open cluster at the origin and always contains the origin itself. For all $\alpha<\alpha_\#$ and $d\ge 5$, as $n\to\infty$
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbb{P}_\alpha\left(0\longleftrightarrow \partial B_n\right)=\alpha\frac{C_d\mathbb{E}_\alpha\ek{\mathrm{Cap}\left({\mathcal C }_0\right)}}{n^{d-2}}\left(1+o(1)\right)\, .
    \end{equation}
Furthermore
    \begin{equation}
        \lim_{k\to\infty}\lim_{n\to\infty }  \mathbb{P}_\alpha\rk{\exists \omega\colon {\mathcal C }_0\left(\eta\setminus \omega\right)\subseteq B_k\textnormal{ and }{\mathcal C }_0\left(\eta\setminus \omega\right)\xleftrightarrow{\,\,{\omega}\,\,}\partial B_n\mid 0\longleftrightarrow \partial B_n}=1\, .
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

