[Definition of arXiv:2607.18635, 'Remainders of generalised Taylor expansions and a priori bounds for rough differential equ'] For $\tau,\tau'\in{\mathcal T}$ we set
		\begin{equation*}
			\tau\curvearrowright_{\rm CK}\tau':=\sum_{\tau''\in{\mathcal T}}m(\tau,\tau';\tau'')\,\tau''\,,
		\end{equation*}
		where $m(\tau,\tau';\tau'')$ denotes the number of edges of $\tau''$ that, once removed, produce $\tau'$ as the subtree that contains the root of $\tau''$ and $\tau$ as the remaining part.

