[Lem lem311 of arXiv:2609.02795, 'Global smooth behavior in Kuznetsov and Westervelt type\\ viscous wave equations:\\ A unif'] Let $p\ge 2$ and $r\ge p$ satisfy $r\le\frac{np}{(n-2)_+}$.
  Then there exists $C(p,r)>0$ such that for each $\varphi\in C^2(\overline{\Omega})$ fulfilling $\varphi=0$ on $\partial\Omega$,
  \begin{eqnarray}\label{311.1}
	\|\nabla\varphi\|_{L^r(\Omega)}^p
	&\le& C(p,r)\cdot\bigg\{ \int_\Omega |\nabla\varphi|^{p-2} |D^2\varphi|^2 \bigg\}^\frac{1+\frac{n}{2}-\frac{n}{r}}{1+\frac{n}{2}-\frac{n-2}{p}}
		\cdot \bigg\{ \int_\Omega \varphi^2 \bigg\}^\frac{1-\frac{n}{2}+\frac{np}{2r}}{1+\frac{n}{2}-\frac{n-2}{p}} \nonumber\\
	& & + C(p,r)\cdot\bigg\{ \int_\Omega |\nabla\varphi|^{p-2} |D^2\varphi|^2 \bigg\}^\frac{1+\frac{n}{2}-\frac{n}{p}}{1+\frac{n}{2}-\frac{n-2}{p}}
		\cdot \bigg\{ \int_\Omega \varphi^2 \bigg\}^\frac{1}{1+\frac{n}{2}-\frac{n-2}{p}}.
  \end{eqnarray} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

