[Lemma 4 of arXiv:2609.01774, 'Hypoellipticity on time-periodic space-times'] Let $\alpha \in \mathbb{R}$ be an irrational number which is not a Liouville number.  Let $\nu>\mu(\alpha)$. Then there exists $C>0$ such that 
    \begin{equation}
        \ltwo{u-\bar u} \leq C \nm{(\p_t^2-\alpha\p_x^2) u}_{H^{2(\nu-1)}_x L^2_t},
    \end{equation}
    where $\bar u$ denotes the average of $u$ over the torus.

