[Lemma lem:basicboundaryint of arXiv:2609.01825, 'On everywhere locally soluble varieties \\ in families over toric bases'] Let $\vec\ell$ be of convergent type for the face $\cal F$ and $1\leq j_0\leq s$. Then there exists $\epsilon >0$ such that for $0<Y<1$ we have the bounds

\begin{align*}
\int_{\substack{\cal F\\ |t_{j_0}|\leq Y}} \prod_{i=1}^s t_i^{\ell_i} d\mu \ll_{\epsilon} Y^{\epsilon} \quad \mbox{ and }\quad \int_{\substack{\cal F\\ |t_{j_0}|\leq Y}} \prod_{i=1}^s \left(t_i+Y\right)^{\ell_i} d\mu \ll_{\epsilon} Y^{\epsilon}.
\end{align*}

