body:
[Lemma Inductive step of arXiv:2601.07808, 'Supercritical long-range percolation on graphs of polynomial growth: the truncated one-arm'] \label[lemma]{lem:f_connectivity}
    Let $G$ be a transitive graph of polynomial growth with $d \geq 2$, and suppose that $J : V \times V \to \mathbf{R}_+$ is a transitive kernel with $J(x,y) = O(d_G(x,y)^{-d \alpha})$ with $\alpha > 1$.

    For $k \in \mathbf{N}$, $b \in \mathbf{N}, \mathbf{m} \in \mathcal{M}(b,k)$, and $\mathbf{f} \in \mathcal{F}(b)$,

    \begin{equation}
        \sum_{\mathbf{B} \in \mathcal{A}(b,\mathbf{m})}
        \mathbf{P}_{\beta}
        \left(
            \mathcal{H}(\mathbf{B})
            \text{ is }
            \mathbf{f} \text{-connected}
        \right)
        \leq 
        \mathbf{E}_{\beta,J^{\star}}
        \left[
            \mathrm{length}(o)
        \right]^{b-1}
        \prod_{i = 0}^{b-1}
        m_i^{f_{i}}
        \exp
        \left(
            c_{\mathrm{pei}} m_i
        \right).
    \end{equation}

