[Thm 78 ({\cite[Theorem 2.7.1) of arXiv:2605.23308, 'Convergence rate estimates for semigroups and heat kernels associated with resistance form'] {VWJ96}}]
  Let $I\subseteq \R$ be a bounded interval with Lebesgue measure $|I|>0$ and $\kappa\in (0,1]$.
  Then there exists a constant $C=C(\kappa)$ such that
  \begin{align*}
    \log N(C^{\kappa}_1(I),\|\cdot\|_{\sup},\varepsilon)\leq C(|I|+2)\varepsilon^{-\frac{1}{\kappa}},\qquad\varepsilon>0,
  \end{align*} 
  where 
  \begin{align*}
    C^{\kappa}_1(I)=\{f:I\to\R:\|f\|_{\BL^{\kappa}}\le 1\}.
  \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

