[Lemma limit-points-drift:fixed-path of arXiv:2605.14149, 'The mean-field limit of online stochastic vector balancing'] For each $n$, let $\bm{a}^n:[0,1]\to{\mathbb R}^n$ be such that $a_i^n\in H_0^1$ and for almost every $t\in[0,1]$
	\begin{equation}
		n^{-1}\dot{\bm{a}}^n(t) \in \big\{{\mathbb E}[g(\bm{Z}^n) \bm{Z}^n] : \sqrt{n}\bm{Z}^n\sim \nu^{\otimes n},\ g:{\mathbb R}^n\to\{\pm 1\}\text{ measurable}\big\}.
	\end{equation}
	Then, any limit point $\mu\in{\mathcal P}({\mathcal C})$ of the sequence
    \begin{equation*}
        \mu_n = \frac{1}{n} \sum_{i=1}^n \delta_{a_i^n}\in{\mathcal P}({\mathcal C})
    \end{equation*}
    is contained in $\mathcal{K}_{2/\pi}$.

