[Theorem lem:full_supp_meas_full_supp_cop of arXiv:2411.07113, '\begin{LARGE}On differentiability and mass distributions of topologically typical multivar'] Let $C \in \mathcal{C}_{ar}^d$ and let $\gamma \in \mathcal{P}_{\mathcal{W}_d}$ be its corresponding Williamson measure. Then the following assertions hold
    \begin{itemize}
     \item[(i)] If $\gamma^{abs}$ has full support, then $\mu_C^{abs}$ has full support.
        \item[(ii)] If $\gamma^{dis}$ has full support, then $\mu_C^{dis}$ has full support.
         \item[(iii)] If $\gamma^{sing}$ has full support, then $\mu_C^{sing}$ has full support.
    \end{itemize}

[Corollary 151 of arXiv:2605.03236, 'Stochastic It\^o Equations and Parabolic Second-Order Equations with singular Drift'] Assume that $a,b$ are smooth and bounded. Take
$R\leq 1$, smooth $f$, and let $u$ be the classical solution of
\begin{equation} 

\cL u+f=0
\end{equation}
in $C_{R}$ with zero boundary condition
on $\partial' C_{R}$.   Then
\begin{equation} 

|u|\leq NR^{2-\beta }\|I_{C_{R}}f\|_{E_{q,p,\beta }},
\end{equation}
where $N$ depends only on $d,\delta,q ,p ,\beta ,\rho_{a} $. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theo thm:unif-rsw of arXiv:2509.08928, 'The near critical random bond Ising model via embedding deformation'] Fix $m>0$, a proper $s$-embedding $\mathcal{S}^{\delta}$ of a graph $(S, (x_e)_{e\in E})$ satisfying {\mbox{\textsc{Unif(}$\delta,r_0,\theta_0$\textsc{)}}}\,, and a collection of masses $(m_{e})_{e\in E}$ all bounded by $m$. Fix a square $\Lambda^{\delta}_{\rho}$  of width $\rho>0$ drawn over $\mathcal{S}^{\delta}$. Consider the FK-Ising model on $\Lambda^{\delta}_{\rho}$, where the coupling constant on the edge $e\in \Lambda^{\delta}_{\rho}$ is $x^{(\delta)}_e=x_e + \delta m_e$, and denote by $\mathbb{P}^{\textnormal{free}}_{\textnormal{FK}}$ the measure with $\textnormal{free}$ boundary conditions on the annulus $\Lambda^{\delta}_{\rho}$. Then, there exists $c(m,r_0,\theta_0)>0$, only depending on $m,r_0,\theta_0$, such that
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{P}^{\textnormal{free}}_{\textnormal{FK}} \big( \textnormal{There exist an open circuit in } \mathrm{A}_{\frac{\rho}{2},\rho} \big) > c(m,r_0,\theta_0).		
\end{equation}
A similar estimate holds for the dual model. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Corollary 24 of arXiv:2608.12291, 'When should one stop the most exciting game?\\ {\tiny Sequential Inference for win-marting'] For every $\mathcal{I}=[t_1,t_2]\subset[0,\infty)$ and $\mathcal{J}=[\underline{a},\overline{a}]\subset(0,1)$ it holds that
    \begin{equation*}
        V_T\to V_\infty
    \end{equation*}
    uniformly on $\mathcal{I}\times\mathcal{J}$ for $T\to\infty$.

