[Lemma lemma_G_large_2 of arXiv:2504.00512, 'Localization-delocalization transition for a random block matrix model at the edge'] In the setting of (mix of the paper), let $z=E+\mathrm{i} \eta$ with $\eta\gtrsim N^{-1/3+\tau_e}$ and $\eta/\im m (z) \sim N^{-\varepsilon_g}$ for some small constants $\tau_e,{\varepsilon}_g>0$. If $\varepsilon_g<({1/8})\wedge ({\delta_A/4})$, then for any $z_1,z_2\in\ha{z,\overline{z}}$, we have that
    \begin{equation}
        \begin{aligned}
            \max_{a\in [\![{D}]\!]}\absa{\mathbb{E}\avga{\left({G (z) -M (z) }\right)E_a}}\prec N^{-1}\left({\im m (z) }\right)^{-1},
        \end{aligned}
    \end{equation}
    \begin{equation}
        \begin{aligned}
            \left\|\mathbb{E} L_{(1,2)}-K_{(1,2)}\right\|_2\prec N^{-1}\eta^{-2}\pa{N^{-\tau_e\wedge \varepsilon_g}}.
