[Cor concentration_meso of arXiv:2510.18856, 'Evolution of recursive trees with limited memory'] Fix $\beta \in (0,1)$. For any $\epsilon,\delta>0$ and $T < T_\beta = 2(1-\beta)^{-1}$ there exist constants $C=C(\delta,T)>0$ and $\xi=\xi(\epsilon)>0$ such that
    \begin{align*}
        \mathbb{P}\left(\exists\;\;v \in [\delta n, n]: \sup_{t\leqslant T }\left|\frac{1}{v}L_v(\lfloor tv^{1-\beta} \rfloor)-f_{\beta}(t)\right|>v^{\frac{-1+\beta}{2}+\epsilon}\right)\leqslant \exp(-Cn^{\xi}).
    \end{align*}

