\begin{align*}
    \lim_{n\to\infty} \frac{1}{\rho_{n+1}-\rho_1} \sum_{u=\rho_1}^{\rho_{n+1}-1} f(\theta_u\mvgo) = \E[f(\mvgo)] \quad \text{a.s.}
\end{align*}
On the other hand, since the blocks are i.i.d., the strong law of large numbers implies
\begin{align*}
