[Definition def:zero of arXiv:2604.21142, 'Gaussian fluctuations for Internal DLA on cylinders'] A function $f : V_N \times {\ensuremath{\mathbb Z}}  \to {\ensuremath{\mathbb R}} $ has the zero horizontal average property if
	\begin{equation}
	\sum_{x \in V_N} f(x, y) = 0 \qquad \text{for every } y \in {\ensuremath{\mathbb Z}} \,.
	\end{equation}

[Lemma h-cof-compute-po-unbased of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] Let $G$ be a compact Lie group, and let
    \begin{equation}
       \begin{tikzcd}
            A\arrow[r,"i"]\arrow[d,"f"']\arrow[dr,phantom,"\ulcorner"{very near end}] & B\arrow[d]\\
            C\arrow[r] & D
        \end{tikzcd}
    \end{equation}
    be any pushout in $\cat{$\bm{G}$-Top}$ such that $i$ is an h-cofibration. Then $((diag:po-along-hcof of the paper))$ is a homotopy pushout in the ${\mathcal{F}}$-model structure for any collection ${\mathcal{F}}$ of subgroups.
    \begin{proof}
        It suffices to factor $f$ into a cofibration $A\to C_0$ followed by a weak equivalence, and to observe that the induced map $B\amalg_AC_0\to B\amalg_AC=D$ is an ${\mathcal{F}}$-weak equivalence by [schwede2018global]*{Proposition~B.6}.
    \end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem:contourintegral of arXiv:2510.26960, 'Free energy fluctuations in SK and related spin glass models: \\ A literature survey'] Given a symmetric matrix $M$ with eigenvalues $\lambda_1\geq\cdots\geq\lambda_N$, the partition function $Z_N$ with the corresponding Hamiltonian $H(\sigma) =\frac12\sigma^TM\sigma$ can be expressed as
 \begin{equation} 
Z_N=C_N\int_{\gamma-\mathrm{i}\infty}^{\gamma+\mathrm{i}\infty}e^{\frac{N}{2}\mathcal{G}(z)}\mathrm{d} z
 \end{equation} 
where the contour is a vertical line crossing the real axis at any $\gamma>\lambda_1$ and
 \begin{equation} 
\mathcal{G}(z)=\beta z-\frac1N\sum_{i=1}^N\log(z-\lambda_i),\qquad C_N=\frac{\Gamma(N/2)}{2\pi\mathrm{i}(N\beta/2)^{N/2-1}}.
 \end{equation}

