body:
[Unnumberedtheorem eq:smoothing_formula of arXiv:2412.00279, 'Optimal local storage policy based on stochastic intensities and its large scale behavior'] Let $\Phi$ be a simple point process in $\mathbb{R}$ with history $\mathcal{F}_t,$ and $\lambda(t)$ an $\mathcal{F}_t$-adapted and a.s. integrable process. Then: $\lambda(t)$ is an $\mathcal{F}_t$-stochastic intensity of $\Phi$ if and only if 
  \begin{equation}
    \mathrm{E}\left[ \int Z(t)\Phi(dt) \right] = \mathrm{E}\left[ \int Z(t)\lambda(t)dt \right]
  \end{equation}
 holds for all $\mathcal{F}_t$-predictable processes $Z(t)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

