{"artifact_digest":"sha256:f39337870da524dde0a555bc14564e975a3a243dcd5061fd3d80d185b8f06194","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/f3/f39337870da524dde0a555bc14564e975a3a243dcd5061fd3d80d185b8f06194.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:29c0e7a62458907f8fb6723d1a6de96eecf665ca28ebed4d87ab4ac1f0b0bb8e","bundle_entry_key":"2607-13302-lemma-7-lema-pomocna-dzamic","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s1_043","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-v2-20260907/bundle_s1_043.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2607-13302-lemma-7-lema-pomocna-dzamic","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: We use the standard generating function for Stirling numbers of the second kind [kesidis2018generating]:
   \begin{align*}
       \sum_{t\geq -1}\genfrac{\{}{\}}{0pt}{}{m+t+1}{m+i}x^{t+1}
&= x^{-m}\sum_{t\geq -1}\genfrac{\{}{\}}{0pt}{}{m+t+1}{m+i}x^{m+t+1} \\
&= x^{-m}\frac{x^{m+i}}{(1-x)(1-2x)\cdots(1-(m+i)x)} \\
&= \frac{x^i}{(1-x)(1-2x)\cdots(1-(m+i)x)}
   \end{align*}

It follows that
\begin{align*}
\sum_{t\geq -1} A_m^N(t)x^{t+1}
&=\sum_{i=0}^{N-m}
\frac{(m+i-1)!}{(m-1)!}\binom{N-m}{i}
\frac{x^{i}}{\prod_{q=1}^{m+i}(1-qx)}. 
\end{align*}

Since
\[
