	\end{enumerate}

Differential terms which add a marking will always satisfy ({\ttfamily b2}).  Differential terms which contract an edge preserve the number of markings, hence preserve property ({\ttfamily b2}).  It thus remains to examine the impact of contracting an edge of a graph satisfying properties ({\ttfamily b1}) or ...","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:89d216e5439fce16368718bdee2b9ff8901861155a9a021df138ff2a7e3a5a1c","revision_digest":"sha256:217f3771a887e6716e3337b822a96e86e79d49a8171f8dfebfdb6e3b70b38fe8","source_id":"arxiv:2609.04033","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-07","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

