The above equation means that there exists $N \subseteq \mathcal{S}$ such that $\overline{I}({\bf 1}_N)=0$ and $\overline{I}_{\rho(S)}(|f-g|)(S)= 0 $ for all $ S \in N^C \equiv \mathcal{S} \setminus N$. Therefore for all $S\in N^C$ we have
\begin{equation} \nonumber
 f =g~\mbox{holds}~ \overline{I}_{(S, \rho(S))}-a.e. ~\mbox{on}~\mathcal{S}_{(S, \rho(S))}~(\mbox{i.e., the equality holds a.e. in } \mathcal{S}_{(S, \rho(S))}).
 \end{equation}
