		As $K_{n,v}\ni k$ is compact we can replace $\varphi,f,\Phi$ by their corresponding $k$-average, which has no effect on convergence. \forlater{\rn{I actually never understood this phrase... DO you mean chang eeach individual function by its k average? that sounds odd to me. Or do you mean k ...","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:d3038bbb6429700df35b2ba9975767832df9ae6cee979a5d8a2348b2ca9e1251","revision_digest":"sha256:21ea5439be92ea5827109cf638e698c21d41cd2c3fd1addf45e3e24af3215507","source_id":"arxiv:2609.01358","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-07","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

