[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2609.02392, 'Large values of cubic and quartic Dirichlet $L$-functions of prime moduli'] With the notation as above and the truth of GRH, we have, for sufficiently large $X$, 
\begin{equation} 
  \max_{\substack{X< p \le 2X \\\chi \bmod{p} \\ \chi^3 = \chi_0 }}\Big|L(\tfrac 12, \chi)\Big |  \geq \exp\left(\left(\frac {\sqrt{2}}{\pi} +o(1) \right)\frac {\log_{3} X}{\log_{2} X}\sqrt{\log X}\right),  \\
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation} 
 \max_{\substack{X< p \le 2X \\\chi \bmod{p} \\ \chi^4 = \chi_0 }}\Big|L(\tfrac 12, \chi)\Big |   \geq \exp\left(\left(\frac {\sqrt{3/2}}{\pi} +o(1) \right)\frac {\log_{3} X}{\log_{2} X}\sqrt{\log X}\right).
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

