[Proposition thm:Neumann of arXiv:2606.01866, 'Phase Transition of a Semiflexible Membrane in Two Dimensions'] In (equation eq:beforeNeumann of the paper), the $L^2$ matrix norm of $\Gamma_N\Delta_N$ is less than $1$, if $N$ is large enough. In particular, the series
    \begin{equation}
        G_N=\sum_{n\ge0} (\Gamma_N \Delta_N)^n \Gamma_N=\sum_{n\ge0} \Gamma_N (\Delta_N \Gamma_N)^n
    \end{equation}
    converges in operator norm.

