[Lemma 10 of arXiv:2512.08595, 'Small time asymptotics of spectral heat content of isotropic processes'] Suppose that $f\in C^{1,\kappa}(\R^d)$ with $|\nabla f(x)-\nabla f(y)|\le L|x-y|^\kappa$ for all $x,y\in\R^d$, and $t>0$. Then,
		\begin{align*}
			\left|\inf_{0\le s\le t} f(X_s)-f(x)-\inf_{0\le s\le t} \langle X_s-x,\nabla f(x)\rangle\right|\le \frac{L}{1+\kappa}\sup_{0\le s\le t} |X_s-x|^{1+\kappa}
		\end{align*}

