[Question universal-parameter of arXiv:2609.03856, 'Consensus time for asynchronous $\ell^p$ relaxation: graph dependence'] For fixed $p\in(1,\infty)\setminus\{2\}$, is there an intrinsic graph
quantity that characterizes $\mathsf T_p(G,1/2)$ on every finite connected
graph, up to constants and logarithmic factors?  In particular, does
\begin{equation}
  \mathfrak C_p(G)
  :=n\kappa_p(G)^{-1}

\end{equation}
have this property? (Stated as a question by the paper; open unless the paper says otherwise.)

[Lem 7 of arXiv:2607.27535, 'Universal topological statistics on \\ triangulated singular spaces'] Let $\phi: K \rightarrow M \subset \RR^D$ be a purely $d$-dimensional $C^2$ triangulation, and let $\hausmeas^d$ be the $d$-dimensional Hausdorff measure. Then for some $b_\phi^{\pm} > 0$ and small enough $r>0$,
    \begin{align*}
        b_\phi^- \cdot r \le \hausmeas^d \big( \ball ( \partial_\phi M, r) \cap M \big) \le b_\phi^+ \cdot r.
    \end{align*}

