[Lemma lem:semi-good2 of arXiv:2512.12124, 'A discontinuous percolation phase transition on the hierarchical lattice'] Let $a,\delta>0, n \in \mathbb{N}$, and let $J : \mathbb{H}_L \to \mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}$ be a kernel such that $J\left(L^j\right) \geq \frac{(a+\delta)L \log (j)}{L^{2j}}$ for every $j\geq n$. Then, for all $k\in \mathbb{N}$ for which $(a+\delta)( 1 - L^{-k} ) \geq a$ and for all subsets $A\subset \Lambda_{n,n+k}$ of size $|A|=\gamma L^k$ one has
    \begin{align}
	&\mathbb{P}_{J} \left( A \nsim \Lambda_{n,n+2k} \setminus \Lambda_{n,n+k} \right) \leq n^{-\gamma a}.
	\end{align}

