[Lemma lem: JordansLemma of arXiv:2606.19583, 'Power-law hypothesis and (un)fairness of PageRank on undirected multi-type PAMs'] For $n \in \mathbb{N}$, let $A_n$ and $B_n$ be random variables taking non-negative values, $\xi_n,R_n$ random variables taking real values, and $a$ and $b$ positive constants such that
\[B_{n+1}-B_n=\frac{1}{n}(A_n-bB_n+\xi_n)+R_{n+1},\]
where 
\begin{enumerate}
    \item $A_n \stackrel{n \to \infty}{\rightarrow} a$ almost surely;
    \item $\sum_{n=1}^\infty R_n<\infty;
    $
    \item $\mathbb{E}[\xi_n]=0$ and $(\xi_n)_{n \in \mathbb{N}}$ is bounded. 
\end{enumerate}
Then $B_n \stackrel{n \to \infty}{\rightarrow} a/b$ almost surely. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

