\begin{equation}
\{s<t_1<\cdots<t_k<t\}
\end{equation}
according to the number $j$ of integration variables lying in $[s,u]$. This gives
\begin{equation}
\inner{\mathrm{Sig}(x)_{s,t}}{w}
=
\sum_{j=0}^k
\inner{\mathrm{Sig}(x)_{s,u}}{i_1\cdots i_j}
