			Next, notice that, since $(M_t)_{t \leq T}$ is a finite variation martingale, and using the definition of the defaultable process $(H_t)_{t \leq T}$, we get $d\left[M,M\right]_s=d\left[M\right]_s=\left(\Delta H_s\right)^2=\Delta H_s=dH_s$, hence: For all $\nu \in \mathcal{T}_{[0,T]}$, we ...","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:67f0fb96acf95f77b99ab7623ccfdf33a3c99c543aef3c4a2766e5dd3459267a","revision_digest":"sha256:2444c98fdb8dbb3d83a08335e55516286398de0e0b0a829d4a76849e5055caaa","source_id":"arxiv:2605.04359","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-07","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

