[Theorem thm-all-or-nothing-transition of arXiv:2607.22324, 'The conclave process'] {}
    Define $\lambda_0=+\infty$ and define $\lambda_k= 2^{1/k}$ for each $k \geq 1$. Then for any $k \geq 1$ and $\alpha \in (\lambda_k,\lambda_{k-1})$, we have
    \begin{align*}
        \mathbb P_n^{\alpha}\big( \mathcal W \in \mathfrak L_k \big)=1-o(1) \mbox{ and } \mathbb P_n^{\alpha}\big( \mathcal W \in \mathfrak L_{k-1} \big) = o(1) \,.
    \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

