[Lemma lem:estimate_small_ht_unif_tree of arXiv:2512.17747, 'On exponentially height-penalized random trees'] Let $\mathbb T_n$ be a uniformly sampled tree. Then for any $k=k_n$ satisfying $\frac{k^2}{n} \to 0$ and $k \to \infty$, 
    \begin{align*}
        \frac{k^2}{n}\log\Big(\mathbb{P}\left(h(\mathbb T_n)<k\big.\right)\Big) \longrightarrow -\pi^2. 
    \end{align*}

