[Thm CT Hldr of arXiv:2608.25471, 'Exact Hausdorff measures and fine geometry of collisions of independent Markov processes'] There exists a deterministic function 
  $c \colon (0,\infty) \to (0,\infty)$ such that, $\hat{P}_{\bm{\rho}}$-a.s., 
  \begin{equation}
    \limsup_{\delta \downarrow 0}
    \sup_{\substack{0 \leq s < t \leq T\\ t-s \leq \delta}} 
    \frac{C_t - C_s}{\lambda_1(t-s)} \leq c(T),
    \qquad 
    \forall T \in (0, \infty).
  \end{equation}

