body:
[Definition def:XYheightfunction of arXiv:2604.24743, 'The impact of disorder and non-convex interactions on delocalisation of height functions'] Given a finite subset $\Lambda \subseteq \ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}^2$, an integer $n \in \ensuremath{\mathbb{N}}^*$, and a collection of conductances $\left( J_{xy,k} \right)_{xy \in E(\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}^2), 1 \leq k \leq n} \in [0, \infty)^{E(\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}^2) \times \{1 , \ldots, n \}}$, we define the XY height function to be the probability distribution on the set $\Omega_\Lambda^{\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}}$ given by the identity
\begin{equation*}
    \mu_{\Lambda , J}^{\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}-\mathrm{XY}} (\left\{ \varphi \right\}) := \frac{1}{Z_{\Lambda,J}^{\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}-\mathrm{XY}}} \prod_{x \sim y} \prod_{1 \leq k \leq n}  I_{\left(\varphi(x) - \varphi(y)\right)} \left( J_{xy,k} \right) .
\end{equation*}
We denote by $\mathrm{Var}_{\Lambda , J}^{\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}-\mathrm{XY}}$ the variance with respect to the measure $\mu_{\Lambda , J}^{\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}-\mathrm{XY}}$ and write $\mathrm{Var}_{L , J}^{\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}-\mathrm{XY}}$ when $\Lambda = \Lambda_L$.

[Theorem 34 (asymptotic) of arXiv:2606.22611, 'Upper and Lower Bounds on Expected Soft Maxima\\of Gaussian Processes'] Using the same notation as in Theorem~\ref{thm:one-shot},
  for any subgaussian $(X_t)$, we have
  \begin{align*}
  \Ex{X_\tau} \lesssim \int_0^\Delta 
  \sqrt{R_\nu(\epsilon^2)\wedge I(X ; \tau)} \dif \epsilon.
  \end{align*}
  If $(X_t)$ is a Gaussian process,
  \begin{align*}
    \Ex{X_{\uptau_\beta^*}} 
    \gtrsim \sup_{\nu\in \eP(T)} 
    \int_0^\Delta \sqrt{R_{\nu}(\epsilon^2)\wedge I(X ; \uptau_\beta^*)} 
    \dif \epsilon.
  \end{align*}

