[Lemma apx_lemma: random_walk_expected_hitting_size_lower_bound of arXiv:2608.00399, 'The Heavy-tailed Frog Model'] Let $Q \in \mathcal{H}_{\alpha, K}$ for some $\alpha, K > 0$. Fix $K_0 \ge 1$ and $\varepsilon \in (0, 1)$.
    Then, there exists positive constants $C = C(Q)$ and $c = c(Q, K_0)$ such that the following holds:
    for any $r, L \in \mathbb N^+$ and
    any subset $D \subseteq B_x(K_0 r)$ with $|D| \ge \varepsilon r^d$, we have

        \vspace{2mm}

        \begin{align}
            \varepsilon c f(r) \le \sum_{y \in \widecheck{D}} \mathbf P_y \left( \tau_{\widecheck{x}} \le \ell(r) \right) \le \sum_{y \in D} \mathbf P^L_y \left( \tau_x \le \ell(r) \right) \le C f(r),
        \end{align}
        where $\widecheck{D} := \{ \widecheck{y} : y \in D \}$ and $f(r)$ is defined as follows:
        \begin{align*}
            f(r) := \begin{cases}
                \ell(r) & \text{if } d \ge 3 \text{ or } (d = 2 \text{ and } \alpha < 2), \\
                \ell(r) / \log \log \ell(r) & \text{if } d = 2 \text{ and } \alpha = 2, \\
                \ell(r) / \log \ell(r) & \text{if } d = 2 \text{ and } \alpha > 2.
            \end{cases}
        \end{align*}

