[Lemma 20 of arXiv:2607.08536, 'Soft edge limit of the Laguerre beta-ensemble at the lower edge'] Suppose that $0<h$, $0<x$. Then
\begin{align}
    \gamma(\sqrt{h})\log(4+ \tfrac{x}{h}+3 |\log \sqrt{h}|)\le c (1+h) \log(\max(x,2)) 
\end{align}
with an absolute constant $c>0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem:cascade of arXiv:2603.28161, 'Boundary four-point connectivities of conformal loop ensembles'] Consider the measure $\widetilde\mu_{\mathcal{U}(\eta_{12}),x_3,x_4}(d\eta_{34})\mu_{\mathbbm{H},x_1,x_2}(d\eta_{12})$. Then its total mass
\begin{equation}
\int H_{\mathcal{U}(\eta_{12})}(x_3,x_4)^h\mu_{\mathbbm{H},x_1,x_2}(d\eta_{12})=\int H_{\mathcal{U}(\eta)}(x_1,x_2)^b\tau ^{2b}f(1-\tau)\widetilde\mu_{\mathbbm{H},x_3,x_4}(d\eta).
\end{equation}
Here $\tau\in(0,1)$ is such that the $(\mathcal{U}(\eta),x_1,x_2,x_3,x_4)$ is conformally equivalent to $(\mathbbm{H},0,\tau,1,\infty)$.

