[Lem lemma:convergenceL of arXiv:2411.12717, 'Excursion theory for Markov processes indexed by Lévy trees'] Fix $r\geq 0$. Under $\mathbf{N}_{x,r}$ and for every $\varepsilon>0$, let  $ {\textbf{\emph{m}}} ( \widetilde{H}  , \varepsilon )$ be the number of connected components of $\mathcal{T}_{\widetilde{H}}\setminus\{ 0 \}$ having  at least a point  at distance  $\varepsilon$ from the root $p_{\widetilde{H}}(0)$.  Then the following convergence holds 
\begin{equation}
L_\sigma(\rho,W)=\lim \limits_{\varepsilon \rightarrow 0} \frac{ {\textbf{\emph{m}}} (\widetilde{H}  , \varepsilon )}{\widetilde{v}(\varepsilon)}, \quad \mathbf{N}_{x,r}\text{-a.e.} 
\end{equation}

[Lem ComLem of arXiv:2506.18207, 'Cartan's Path Development, the Logarithmic Signature and a Conjecture of Lyons-Sidorova'] Let $0\leqslant s\leqslant R$ be given fixed and
let $\{c_{k}\}_{1\leqslant k\leqslant R+1}$ be a given sequence of
numbers. Then one has 
\begin{equation}
\sum_{\eta\in{\cal T}(s,R-s)}\frac{1}{c_{\eta^{-1}(2)}^{\eta^{-1}(2)}c_{\eta^{-1}(2)}^{\eta^{-1}(3)}\cdots c_{\eta^{-1}(2)}^{\eta^{-1}(R+1)}}=\big(\prod_{k=1}^{s}c_{k}^{s}\big)^{-1}\big(\prod_{k=s+2}^{R+1}c_{s+2}^{k}\big)^{-1}.
\end{equation}
Here ${\cal T}(s,R-s)$ denotes the collection of permutations $\eta\in{\cal S}_{R+1}$
such that 
\begin{equation}
\eta(s+1)=1;\ \eta(s)<\cdots<\eta(1);\ \eta(s+2)<\cdots<\eta(R+1).
\end{equation}
We also denote 
\begin{equation}
c_{\eta^{-1}(2)}^{\eta^{-1}(k)}\triangleq c_{\eta^{-1}(2)}+c_{\eta^{-1}(3)}+\cdots+c_{\eta^{-1}(k)},\ c_{p}^{q}\triangleq c_{p}+c_{p+1}+\cdots+c_{q},
\end{equation}
and conventionally we set $c_{1}^{0}=c_{R+2}^{R+1}=1$.

