[Lemma eq:loc_contbd of arXiv:2607.05671, 'Bi-infinite systems of singularly interacting Brownian particles and the KPZ equation'] Let $g^* = \max\{g_-,g_+,0\}$. Fix $m,n,j,\ell\in \mathbb{N}$ with $M_m \leq j \leq \ell \leq N_n-1$. There exists $m_0 = m_0(\omega) \in \mathbb{N}$ such that if $m \geq m_0$ and $0 \leq s \leq t < \infty$,
\begin{equation} 
\begin{split}
L_{(j,j+1)}^{[m,n]}(t) - L_{(j,j+1)}^{[m,n]}(s) & \leq \frac{q^{-1}(g^* - g_*)(t - s)}{1-r} + \frac{q^{-1}(L_{(\ell,\ell+1)}^0(t) - L_{(\ell,\ell+1)}^0(s))}{1 - r} \\
& \quad + q^{-1}\sum_{k = -\infty}^j r^{j - k}(B_k(t) - B_k(s) - \mathcal{B}^-_{\ell - k + 1}(k,[s,t])).
\end{split}
\end{equation}

