[Lem 60 of arXiv:2510.22783, 'Universality of Cutoff for Riffle Shuffling'] As $N\to\infty$, we have $|H(\vec\bn)|\geq N^{1/2}$ and $|\partial H(\vec\bn)|\leq 2|H(\vec\bn)|^{\frac{1}{2}}$. More precisely,
		\begin{equation}
		    |H(\vec\bn)|=N^{1+\sum_{(i,l)\in T} \alpha_l^{(i)}(\log(p_l^{(i)})\pm O(\chi))+\alpha_{\tot}\sum_{i=0}^{z}h_iH(\{\alpha_l^{(i)}\}_{l:(i,l)\in T})-o(\delta)}\geq N^{1/2}.
		\end{equation}

