[Proposition 6 of arXiv:2604.15753, 'The truncation property and continuity for \\ the long-range contact process on $\mathbb{Z'] Let $\lambda \in \Lambda$  be symmetric and satisfy  $\lambda_{o,y} \simeq \|y\|^{-\alpha}$ for some $\alpha>d$, and let $\delta >0$ so that $\phi(\lambda,\delta)>0$. Then, for any  $\epsilon > 0$, there exists $A \subset \bZ^d$ and $L, T \in [0,\infty)$   such that
\begin{align}

 \P_{\lambda,\delta} \left(\exists (y,t) \in D \colon A(y)  \subset \leftidx{_{5L}}{A}{_{6T-s}^{A(x)}} \right)> (1-\epsilon) \quad \text{ for any } (x,s)\in B_{L,T},
 \end{align}
 where $D \coloneqq  [L,3L] \times [-L,L]^{d-1} \times [5T,6T]$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem:vandermonde of arXiv:2609.04092, 'Short character sums of inhomogeneous polynomials'] Let $m,n$ be positive integers and  consider the Vandermonde matrix
    \begin{align*}
        \begin{bmatrix}
            1&a_1&a_1^2&\cdots&a_1^n\\
            \vdots &&&&\vdots\\
            1&a_m&a_m^2&\cdots&a_m^n
        \end{bmatrix}.
    \end{align*}
    If $m\leq n+1$, then this has rank $m$ if and only if all $a_i$'s are distinct. If $m>n+1$, then this has rank $n+1$ if and only if $n+1$ of the $a_i$'s are distinct.

