[Lemma 38 of arXiv:2607.29495, 'Fast Mixing for Low-Temperature Potts Models via Poisson Trees'] For $\ell \geq 0$, let $Z_\ell \coloneqq |\cT^\dom_\ell|$ be the total number of vertices in the branching process after $\ell$ generations. Then, \(Z_\ell\) has a probability generating function, defined recursively by
    \[
    f_\ell(t) \coloneqq \E[t^{Z_\ell}] = \begin{cases}
        t & \text{if } \ell = 0 \\
        t f(f_{\ell-1}(t)) & \text{otherwise}
    \end{cases}
    \]
    The function \(f_0\) is defined for all \(t\geq 0\), and \(f_\ell\) is defined for all \(t\geq 0\) small enough so that \(f_{\ell-1}(t)\leq (\frac{\emm^{dp_\bad-1}}{dp_\bad})^{1/D}\).

