[Proposition Prop: LB_main of arXiv:2608.00399, 'The Heavy-tailed Frog Model'] Let $d \geq 1$, $\lambda > 0$, $\ell \in \mathbb N^+$, $\alpha \in (0, d)$, and $Q \in \mathcal{H}_{\alpha, K}$.
    There exist positive constants $C_1$, $C_2$, and $M$ (depending on $d, \alpha, K, \lambda, \ell$) such that, for all $m \ge M$ and all $x \in \mathbb Z^d$ with $x \neq o$, we have
    \begin{align}
        \mathbb P(\mathrm{D}_{\ell}(o, x) \le m) \le \frac{C_1}{|x|^{d + \alpha}} e^{C_2 m^{1/\Delta}}. 
    \end{align}

