body:
[Lemma lem:symmetric-radial of arXiv:2608.30904, 'Entire monotone solutions of the anisotropic Allen--Cahn equation in dimension 5'] Under the assumptions of (lem:radial-Bregman of the paper),
\begin{equation}
 [a(\alpha n+\xi)-a(\alpha n)]\cdot\xi
 \ge
 \frac12(b\cdot\xi)^2+\frac{\lambda}{2}|\xi|^2.
\end{equation}

[Lemma 14 of arXiv:2506.15159, 'Conditional central limit theorems for exponential random graphs'] In the compact subset $B$ of the subcritical region, we have
\begin{align}
    f_{d,A} =O_{r} (\|A\|_2),
\end{align}
where $\|A\|_2$ is the Euclidean norm of the tensor $A$ when viewed as a vector. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem.sym-exit of arXiv:2605.26082, 'Quantitative Einstein relation for reversible diffusions in a random environment'] Fix an environment $\omega$. Let $Z_t$ be a Feller diffusion with generator $\tfrac12\nabla\cdot(\mathbf{a}\nabla)$, where $\mathbf{a}$ is symmetric, uniformly elliptic, and Lipschitz with constants $(\Lambda^{-1},\Lambda)$. There exist constants $c,C>0$ depending only on $(d,\Lambda)$ such that, for every $R>0$ and $T>0$ and every $x\in\mathbb{R}^d$,
		\begin{equation}
			P_x^{0,\omega} \left(\sup_{0\le s\le T}|Z_s-x|\ge R\right)\le C\exp \left(-c\frac{R^2}{T}\right)\, .
		\end{equation}

