[Thm equiv_entropies of arXiv:2509.08659, 'Gap metrics for stationary point processes and quantitative convexity of the free energy'] For a stationary point process $\mathsf{P}\in \mathcal P_{s,1}(\Gamma)$ \begin{align*}
        \mathcal{E}(\mathsf{P})=\mathcal{E}^*( \mathsf{gap}(\mathsf{P})).
    \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition 7 (Reflection, scaling, and L\'evy time) of arXiv:2609.02590, 'Directional Optimal Sub-Gamma Scales for Infinitely Divisible Laws'] For $b>0$ and $s>0$,
\begin{align}
 \cplus(-X)&=\cminus(X), & \cminus(-X)&=\cplus(X),
 \\
 \cplus(bX)&=b\cplus(X), & \cminus(bX)&=b\cminus(X).

\end{align}
If $X_s$ is the time-$s$ marginal of a L\'evy process whose time-one marginal
is $X$, then
\begin{equation}
 \cplus(X_s)=\cplus(X),
 \qquad
 \cminus(X_s)=\cminus(X).

\end{equation}

[Prop of arXiv:2509.08659, 'Gap metrics for stationary point processes and quantitative convexity of the free energy'] Let $\mathsf{P}_i\in \mathcal P_{s,1}(\Gamma)$, $i=0,1$ with $\mathcal E(\mathsf{P}_1)<\infty$.  Then the HWI inequality holds  \begin{align}
     \mathcal E(\mathsf{P}_0)-\mathcal E(\mathsf{P}_1)\leq \mathscr W_{2}\left(\mathsf{P}_0,\mathsf{P}_1\right) \sqrt{\mathcal I^*\left( \mathsf{gap}(\mathsf{P}_0)\right)}.
    \end{align}

