[Lemma eqn:asymptotics_T_mapsto_g_k1(T) of arXiv:2604.09509, 'An Improved Bipartition Cover Bound for the Multispecies Coalescent Model'] The function $T \mapsto g_{k,1}(T)$ has asymptotics
\begin{equation}
     \begin{cases} 1 - g_{k,1}(T) \sim \frac{3(k-1)}{k+1} \exp(-T), & T \uparrow \infty, \\ 
 g_{k,1}(T) \sim \frac{k!}{2^{k-1}} T_k^{k-1}, &  k^2T_k = o(1).
\end{cases}

\end{equation}
\noindent Moreover, for fixed $T$, we have $g_{k,1}(T) \downarrow \mathbb{P}(S_\infty \leqslant T) =: s(T)$ where $S_\infty := \sum_{i=2}^\infty \tau_i$ for $\tau_i \sim \mathrm{Exp}\left({i \choose 2}\right)$ independent. Furthermore, the gap $\Delta_k(T) := g_{k,1}(T) - s(T)$ satisfies

\[\Delta_k(T) = \frac{2f_{S_\infty}(T)}{k} + o\left(\frac{1}{k}\right) \sim \frac{2f_{S_\infty}(T)}{k}.\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

