[Lemma 10 of arXiv:2608.27433, 'Scalar curvature on K\"ahler blow-ups and systolic inequalities'] Let $x$ satisfy $2\eps\le d(x)=\rho\le r_\eps$, and let $B_x$ be a ball of radius comparable to $\rho$ as in \eqref{eq:weighted-norm}. Then
\begin{equation}
  \norm{S(\omega_\eps)}
  _{C^{2,\alpha}(B_x,\rho^{-2}\omega_\eps)}
  \le C\left(1+\eps^2\rho^{-3}\right).
\end{equation}

