[Lemma lem.vn.1lip of arXiv:2605.14149, 'The mean-field limit of online stochastic vector balancing'] For each $n \in {\mathbb N}$ and $k \in \{0,1,\dots,n\}$, $\mathcal{V}^n(k,\cdot)$ is $1$-Lipschitz with respect to $|\cdot|_{\infty}$, i.e., for all $\bm{x},\bm{y}\in{\mathbb R}^n$
    \begin{align*}
        |\mathcal{V}^n(k,\bm{x}) - \mathcal{V}^n(k,\bm{y})| \leq |\bm{x} - \bm{y}|_{\infty}.
    \end{align*}

