[Proposition prop:unif_prob_bound of arXiv:2609.04045, 'Heat content and spectrum for subordinated sub-Laplacians'] Let $(B_t)_{t\geqslant 0}$ denote the hypoelliptic Brownian motion on $\mathbb{G}$. If $\Omega\subset \mathbb{G}$ is a bounded, open set satisfying the intrinsic exterior cone condition, there exists a constant $c=c(\Omega)\in (0,1)$ such that 
        \begin{align}
            \mathbb{P}_x(B_t\in \Omega)\leqslant c \text{ for all } x\in\Omega^c, \ t>0.
        \end{align}

