[Definition 7 (Branching capacity from escape probabilities) of arXiv:2608.30668, 'Recurrence and capacity of stable branching random walks'] The branching capacity (associated with a \(\Tree\)-walk) of a finite
subset \(A \subset \Z^d\) is defined as

\begin{equation*}{
\bcp(A) = \sum_{a \in A} \P(\Tree_{+}^{a} \cap A = \emptyset).
}\end{equation*}
It implicitly depends on \(\mu\) and \(\theta\).

