[Lem head-randomization of arXiv:2608.29018, 'Sharp Restricted Isometry Thresholds for\\ Global Minima of Rank-Restricted Matrix LASSO'] One has \begin{subequations}
\begin{align}
\mathbb{E}[\sigma_{\bm{T}}] & =\frac{\alpha}{r_{\star}}\sigma_{\mathrm{head}},\\
\mathbb{E}\normtwo{\sigma_{\bm{T}}}^{2} & =\frac{\alpha}{r_{\star}}\mathsf{H}^{2},
\end{align}
\end{subequations} and 
\begin{align}
\mathbb{E}\normtwo{A\sigma_{\bm{T}}}^{2}={} & \frac{\alpha(\alpha-1)}{r_{\star}(r_{\star}-1)}\normtwo{A\sigma_{\mathrm{head}}}^{2}\nonumber \\[-1mm]
 & +\frac{\alpha(r_{\star}-\alpha)}{r_{\star}(r_{\star}-1)}\sum_{j\ler_{\star}}\sigma_{j}^{2}\normtwo{A\mathrm{e}_{j}}^{2}.
\end{align}
Moreover, $\normzero{\sigma_{\bm{T}}}\le\alpha$ almost surely. The
analogous identities hold with $(\bm{T},\alpha)$ replaced by $(\bm{S},\beta)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

