[Theorem informal_thm1 of arXiv:2606.28575, 'Global smooth solutions by high mode Lie-Transport noise for Logarithmically Hyperdissipat'] Let $T, R>0,\ \varepsilon\in (0,1)$. There exist $\nu>0,\ \theta\in \ell^2(\mathbb{Z}^3_0)$ such that for all zero mean, divergence-free vector field $\omega_0$ such that
    \begin{align*}
        \|\omega_0\|_{L^2(\mathbb{T}^3;\mathbb{R}^3)}\leq R,
    \end{align*}
    there exists a unique smooth solution to the (equation main_strat of the paper) that does not blow-up before time $T$ with probability larger than $1-\varepsilon$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 9 of arXiv:2609.03386, 'Twisted Gradient Flow Approach to Vegetation-Rainfall-Bushfire Interactions Model'] There exists a constant $C_5>0$, which depends on the following values:

\begin{equation*}
\delta,\quad T, \quad \|v_0\|_{H^1(\Omega)},\quad \int_0^T \|\tilde{z}'(t)\|_{L^2(\Omega)}dt, 
\quad \int_0^T \|\tilde{g}(t)\|_{L^2(\Omega)}^2dt,
\end{equation*}
such that the following boundedness estimates hold for all $\nu \in (0,1)$:

\begin{align*}
&\int_0^T \|(S_{\text{{\tiny $1,\!\delta,\!\nu$}}}(\tilde{z},\tilde{g}))'(t)\|_{L^2(\Omega)}^2dt
+\sup_{0 \le t \le T} \Phi_\nu ((S_{\text{{\tiny $1,\!\delta,\!\nu$}}}(\tilde{z},\tilde{g}))(t))\\
&\hspace*{3cm}+\nu^2 \int_0^T \|(S_{\text{{\tiny $1,\!\delta,\!\nu$}}}(\tilde{z},\tilde{g}))(t)\|_{H^2(\Omega)}^2 dt \le C_5.
\end{align*}

