[Proposition thm:uniquefixed of arXiv:2505.12187, 'Speeding up quantum Markov processes through lifting'] Let $\mathcal{L}_S$ be defined in (equation def:lsbip of the paper), where $\mathcal{L}^A$ is a primitive QMS generator on the subsystem $A$ with invariant state $\sigma^A \in \mathcal{D}_+(\mathcal{M}_A)$. Suppose that (asspA2 of the paper) holds. Then, 
\begin{itemize}
    \item There exists a state $\sigma^B \in \mathcal{D}_+(\mathcal{M}_B)$ such that 
    \begin{align} 
        \sigma = \sigma^A \otimes \sigma^B\,.
    \end{align} 
    Moreover, $\mathcal{L}^A$ is $\sigma^A$-KMS detailed balanced. 
    \item It holds that 
    \begin{align} 
        \left[\sigma^A, H^A \right] = 0\,,\quad \left[\sigma^B, H^B\right] = 0\,,\quad \left[\sigma, H^{AB}\right] = 0\,,
    \end{align}
    where Hamiltonians $H^A$, $H^B$, and $H^{AB}$ are given in (equation eq:hamil of the paper).
\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 15 of arXiv:2607.19873, 'Local limit theorem for the operator norm of products of random matrices'] Let $\mu$ be a Borel probability measure on $G$. 
Assume that the action of $G$ on $B$ satisfies the contraction property \eqref{contraction-property-on-B}.
Then, the operator $P_{\mu}$ admits a unique invariant Borel probability measure $\nu$ on $B$, and 
for any continuous function $\varphi$ on $B$, we have, uniformly in $b \in B$, 
\begin{align*}
 P_{\mu}^n \varphi(b) 
=    \bb E \varphi(g_n \cdots g_1 b) 
\xrightarrow[n\to\infty]{}  \int_{B} \varphi(b')  \nu(d b'). 
\end{align*}

