[Lemma 23 of arXiv:2605.09706, 'A dyadic construction of a three-dimensional attractive point interaction Markov family'] Fix \(T,\beta,\varepsilon>0\). Then there exist constants \(C,c>0\),
depending only on \((T,\beta,\varepsilon)\), such that for every
\(0\le s<t\le T\), every \(R\ge \varepsilon\) and every \(x\in E_\varepsilon\) with $|x| \le R$, we have
\begin{align}
\int_{\{|y|>R\}}
p^{T,\beta}_{s,t}(x,y)\,dy
\;\le\;
C\,
\exp\!\Bigl(
-\frac{c\,(R-|x|)^2}{t-s}
\Bigr).
\end{align}

