[Proposition 23 of arXiv:2609.01362, '{Double cluster swapping for spin models: \\Pfaffian relations and sharpness}'] Let $G = (V,E)$ be a finite graph and $S \subset V$. If $P \in \Ec$, then
	\[
		\left< \vp_o \vp_x \right>_{G,\beta,h} \leq \beta \sum_{\substack{u \in S \\ v \in G \setminus S}} J_{uv} \left< \vp_o \vp_u \right>_{S,\beta,0} \left< \vp_v \vp_x \right>_{G,\beta,h} + h \sum_{u \in S} \left< \vp_o \vp_u \right>_{S,\beta,0} \left< \vp_x \right>_{G,\beta,h} 
	\] 
	for any $o \in S$ and $x \in V \setminus S$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

