[Theorem 5 of arXiv:2609.01485, 'On the Ramification of Quadratic Fields where the Torsion of a Rational Elliptic Curve Gro'] Let $E/\mathbb{Q}$ be a rational elliptic curve and $\ell$ a prime such that there exists a point $P\in E(K)[\ell]\setminus E(\mathbb{Q})$, where $K = \mathbb{Q}(\sqrt{d})$ and $\ell\geq 3$. Let us consider another prime integer $0<p\in \mathbb{Z}$, we have
    \begin{itemize}
        \item If $\ell\in\{5,7\}$ the following conditions determine the primes that divide $d_K$ in terms of invariants of $E$:
        \begin{itemize}
            \item If  $p\neq \ell$, $p|d_K$ if and only if $E$ has additive reduction at $p$.
            \item If $p=\ell = 5$,  $p|d_K$ if and only if $E$ has additive reduction and the Kodaira symbol at $p$ is different from $II$ and $III$.
            \item If $p=\ell = 7$,  $p|d_K$ if and only if $E$ has additive reduction and the Kodaira symbol at $p$ is different from $II$.
        \end{itemize}
        \item If $p\neq \ell = 3$,   $p|d_K$ if and only if $E$ has additive reduction and the Kodaira symbol at $p$ is different from $IV^*$ and $IV$.
    \end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Corollary 4 of arXiv:2609.02703, 'A choice-free proof of the Erd\"os--Dushnik--Miller theorem'] Let $\kappa$ be an aleph, let $P\subseteq\kappa$ with $|P|=\kappa$, and let $f:P\to\kappa$.
Then there exists $Q\subseteq P$ with $|Q|=\kappa$ on which $f$ is monotonic;
that is, for all $\alpha,\beta\in Q$, if $\alpha<\beta$, then $f(\alpha)\leqslant f(\beta)$.

[Theorem of arXiv:2601.21762, 'Navier-Stokes with a fractional transport noise as a limit of multi-scale dynamics'] Let $M$ and $Q$ satisfy Assumption (assumption of the paper), $H\in \left(\frac{1}{3}, \frac{1}{2}\right)$, and
    \begin{equation*}
        X_{s,t}^\epsilon=\epsilon^{H-1} \int_s^t  w_r^\epsilon dr, \quad \mathbb{X}_{s,t}^\epsilon = 
        \int_s^t X_{s,r}^\epsilon \otimes dX_{r}^\epsilon
    \end{equation*}
    Then $(X^{\epsilon}_{\cdot}, \mathbb{X}^{\epsilon}_{ \cdot\cdot})$ converges in $L^{q}(\Omega;\mathcal{C}^{\alpha}
    ([0,T];H^{\sigma}))$ to $(B,\mathbb{B})$ for all $1<q<\infty$ and $\frac{1}{3}<\alpha< H$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition 40 of arXiv:2609.03875, 'Measure theory without infinities'] Let $\mf A$ be a sequentially complete HTG and $\mu$ be an $\mf A$-valued premeasure. Then
  \begin{multline}
    \Sigma_{\mf A}(\mu) =  \sett{A}{A\in \q\mu \mbox{ and the family $\mu\circ \mb A$ is summable in $\mf A$}}{\mbox{for every countable partition $\mb A$ of $A$ into elements of $D_\mu$}}.
  \end{multline}

