body:
[Proposition prop:ito-defect of arXiv:2606.28869, '\bfseries A General Theory of Paths:\\ \large Signatures, Jump Lifts, and Expected Signatu'] Let $X$ be a finite-variation c\`adl\`ag{} path in $\mathbb{R}^d$, and let $\mathrm{Sig}^I$ denote its forward lift. For all letters $i,j$,
\begin{equation}
\inner{\mathrm{Sig}^I}{i}\inner{\mathrm{Sig}^I}{j}
-\big(\inner{\mathrm{Sig}^I}{ij}+\inner{\mathrm{Sig}^I}{ji}\big)
=\sum_{0<u\le T}\Delta X_u^i\Delta X_u^j
=:[X^i,X^j]^{\mathrm d}_T.

\end{equation}
Thus the forward lift fails the shuffle relation exactly by the discrete jump quadratic covariation. In particular, unless this bracket vanishes, $\mathrm{Sig}^I$ is not a character on the shuffle Hopf algebra.

