[Definition def:MP_lin of arXiv:2608.30493, '\bf McKean-Vlasov Differential Equations:\\ {An introduction and a focus on some kinetic m'] Let $s\in [0,T)$ and $\nu\in\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^d)$. A probability measure $\mathbb{P}=\mathbb{P}_{s,\nu}$, on $(C_{[s,T)},\mathcal{B})$, is a solution to MP$(b,\sigma;s,\nu)$ if: 

\begin{itemize}
\item[(i)] $x_{s} \sim  \nu$ under $\mathbb{P}$;
\item[(ii)] for any $\varphi\in C_0^{\infty}(\mathbb{R}^d)$, the process defined by 
\begin{equation}
M_t : =\varphi(x_{t}) - \varphi(x_{s}) - \int_{s}^t \Big(   \langle  b(r, x_r) , \nabla \varphi(x_{r})  \rangle + \frac{1}{2}\text{tr}\big(\sigma \sigma^\top (r , x_r)  \nabla^2 \varphi(x_r)  \big) \Big) dr , \qquad t\in [s, T),
\end{equation}
is a martingale w.r.t. the natural filtration of $(x_t)_{t\in [s,T)}$.
\end{itemize}

[Theorem 14 of arXiv:2609.03634, 'Joint Laws of Maximum Drawdown and Maximum Drawup for Spectrally Negative L\'{e}vy Process'] Let $u>0$, and let $\varphi:\mathbb{R}_+\to\mathbb{R}_+$ be bounded and measurable. Then
\begin{align*}
