[Prop symmetric-tree-geometry of arXiv:2609.03856, 'Consensus time for asynchronous $\ell^p$ relaxation: graph dependence'] Assume $d_0\ge2$.  Then $o$ minimizes $T_G(r)$.  If
\begin{equation}
 S=\sum_{1\le i\le j\le k-1}
 (d_i d_{i+1}\cdots d_j)^{1/(p-1)},
\end{equation}
where the sum is empty for $k=1$, then
\begin{equation}
 1+S\le T_G\le1+2S.
\end{equation}
The actual maximum degree is
\begin{equation}
 \Delta_G=\max\left\{d_0,\ 1+\max_{1\le i<k}d_i\right\},
\end{equation}
with the second maximum omitted for $k=1$.

