[Lemma 20 of arXiv:2511.09517, 'From Cannings model to Brownian motion conditioned on local time profile'] For any $n\ge 1$ and $1 \le s < h(q_n)$,
\begin{align}
    \e_n[(\nu^s_1)^2(\nu^s_2)^2] \le \frac{q_n(s+1)}{q_n(s)-1}\e_n[(\nu^s_1)^3]
\end{align}
In particular, under conditions \eqref{H1} and \eqref{eq:3rd}, for any $\delta>0$,
\begin{align}
    \lim_{n\to\infty} \sup_{\delta n \le s \le h(q_n)-\delta n} \frac{\mathbb{E}_n[(\nu_1^{s})^2 (\nu_2^{s})^2]}{n} = 0.
\end{align}

