[Theorem thrm:multinorm of arXiv:2606.09386, 'High-degree vertices in uniform recursive directed acyclic graphs with freezing'] Let $(X_n)_{n\in\mathbb{N}}$ and  $(Y_n)_{n\in\mathbb{N}}$ be sequences of real-valued random variables,  and let $(\lambda_n)_{n\in\mathbb{N}}$, $(\mu_n)_{n\in\mathbb{N}}$ sequences of real numbers such that, for any $r,s\in\mathbb{N}$ and any $t\geq r,u\geq s$, 
\begin{equation} 
\mathbb{E}\left[(X_n)_r(Y_n)_s\right]-\lambda_n^r\mu_n^s=o(\lambda_n^{-t}\mu_n^{-u}). 
\end{equation} 
Then, with $Z_1,Z_2$ two independent standard normal random variables, 
\begin{equation} 
\Big(\frac{X_n-\lambda_n}{\sqrt{\lambda_n}},\frac{Y_n-\mu_n}{\sqrt{\mu_n}}\Big)\buildrel {\mathrm{d}}\over{\longrightarrow} (Z_1,Z_2).
\end{equation}

