[Lemma hadamardestimate of arXiv:2608.23765, '\texorpdfstring{Tight Majorizations and Convergence Rates\\ of Nuclear Norm Minimization I'] Let $\mathbf{A}   \in \R^{d \times d} $ be a positive semidefinite matrix and let $\mathbf{B} \in \R^{d \times d} $ be arbitrary. 
Let ${\left\vert\kern-0.25ex\left\vert\kern-0.25ex\left\vert \cdot 
    \right\vert\kern-0.25ex\right\vert\kern-0.25ex\right\vert}$ be any unitarily invariant norm on $\R^{d \times d}$.
Then it holds that
\begin{equation*}
\vertiii{ \mathbf{A}  \circ \mathbf{B} }
\le \underset{i \in \left[d\right]}{\max} \  
\mathbf{A}_{ii}  \  \vertiii{ \mathbf{B} }.
\end{equation*}

