body:
[Lemma 20 of arXiv:2607.27150, 'Modelling Anomalous Diffusion: The Role of CTRWs and Non-Local Dynamics'] Let $r_0>0$. For every multi-index $\beta=(\beta_1,\dots,\beta_d)\ge0$, there exist constants $c_1,c_2,c_3>0$ such that for all $t>0$ and all $x,y\in \mathbb{R}^d$ such that $|x-y|>r_0$ it holds that
		\begin{align}
			|\partial^\beta_x p(t,x,y)|&\le c_1(\beta, r_0),\\
			|\partial^\beta_x p^D(t,x,y)|&\le c_3(\beta, r_0,\de(x)),
		\end{align}
		and for all $t>0$ and $x,y\in D$ it holds that
		\begin{align}
			|\partial^\beta_x \mathds{E}^x\left[p(t-T_D,A({T_D}),y);t>T_D\right]|&\le c_2(\beta, \de(x)). 
		\end{align}
		Moreover, both $x\mapsto p(t,x,y)$, $x\in \mathbb{R}^d$, and $x\mapsto p^D(t,x,y)$, $x\in D$, are infinitely differentiable in $x\ne y$, and for every multi-index $\beta$ it holds that $\lim_{|x|\to\infty}\partial^\beta_x p(t,x,y)=0$.

