[Lemma lem:CMF of arXiv:2606.11951, 'On Skorokhod Problems for Reflected and Singular Stochastic Heat Equations'] (Version of the Cameron--Martin Formula) Let $h \in H_0^1~\cap~H^2$. Then, the measure $T_{+h}(\mu^{\beta})$ is absolutely continuous w.r.t.\ $\mu^{\beta}$, and its Radon--Nikodym density is given by
	\begin{equation}
		\frac{dT_{+h}(\mu^{\beta})}{d\mu^{\beta}} = \exp\left( -(h'', \cdot )_{L} - \frac{1}{2} \| h' \|_{L}^2 \right) \eqqcolon \xi.
	\end{equation}

[Proposition keyprop of arXiv:2603.24499, 'A central limit theorem for connected components of random coverings of manifolds with nil'] Consider the previous random variables $\mathsf{K}_{G,n}$ with distribution determined by the measure $\mathbb{P}_{G,n,x}$. 
Let $(a_n)$ be a sequence of real numbers, and let $(b_n)$ be a sequence of positive real numbers such that, as $n\rightarrow\infty$,
\begin{eqnarray*}
a_n &=& 
x W_{G,-1}\left(
W_{G,0}^{-1}\left(\frac{n}{x}\right)
\right)
+o\left(
n^{\frac{\alpha_G-1}{2\alpha_G}}(\ln n)^{\frac{m_G-1}{2\alpha_G}}
\right)\ ,  \\
b_n & = & 
\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha_G(\alpha_G-1)}}
\times{\alpha_G}^{-\left(\frac{m_G-1}{2\alpha_G}\right)}
\times(x\mathcal{K}_G)^{\frac{1}{2\alpha_G}}
\times n^{\frac{\alpha_G-1}{2\alpha_G}}
\times(\ln n)^{\frac{m_G-1}{2\alpha_G}}
\times (1+o(1))\ .
\end{eqnarray*}
Then, for all $s\in\mathbb{R}$, we have
\[
\lim\limits_{n\rightarrow\infty}
\ln
\mathbb{E}\left[\exp\left(s\left(\frac{\mathsf{K}_{G,n}-a_n}{b_n}\right)\right)\right]
=\frac{s^2}{2}\ .
\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma of arXiv:2608.30493, ' f McKean-Vlasov Differential Equations:\ {An introduction and a focus on some kinetic m'] Let $
u\in\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^d)$. A probability measure $\mathbb{P}_{
u}$, on $(C_T,\mathcal{B})$, is a solution to NL-MP$({ f b}^*,{ oldsymbol\sigma}^*;
u)$ if and only if it is a solution to NL-MP$(\widetilde{ f b},\widetilde{ oldsymbol\sigma};
u)$ for any $\widetilde{ f b},\widetilde{ oldsymbol\sigma}$ as defined in (equation eq:def_b_sig_dens_gen of the paper).

