[Proposition prop:ODE_gen of arXiv:2509.15446, 'On the pair correlation function of the $\Sineb$ process'] Fix $\beta>0, \delta>0$. Let $q_k(\lambda)=E[e^{i k \alpha_{\lambda}(0)}]$ where $\alpha_\lambda(u)$ is the strong solution of (equation eq:alphaSDE of the paper) with initial condition (equation eq:SDE_initial of the paper). Then $q_k(\lambda)$ is differentiable for $\lambda\in {\mathbb R}$, $\lambda\neq 0$, and we have
\begin{align}
     \tfrac{\beta}{4}\lambda q_{1}'(\lambda)&=\tfrac{1}{2}(1+\delta)+(i \lambda \tfrac{\beta}{4}-1) q_{1}(\lambda)+\tfrac{1}{2}(1-\delta)q_{2}(\lambda),\\
   \tfrac{\beta}{4} \lambda q'_{k}(\lambda)&=\tfrac{1}{2} k(k+\delta) q_{k-1}(\lambda)+(i k \lambda \tfrac{\beta}{4}-k^2)q_{k}(\lambda)+\tfrac{1}{2} k (k-\delta )q_{k+1}(\lambda), \qquad 2\le k,\\
    \lim_{\lambda\to 0}q_{k}(\lambda)&=1. 
\end{align}

