[Lemma expintest of arXiv:2511.06321, 'Torus scaling limits and the plateau of the critical weakly coupled $|\varphi|^4$ model in'] For $\beta \in (0,1)$,  $a, c, t,\mu \ge 0$,  there exists $c' > 0$ such that
\begin{align}
	\int_a^{\infty} s^{-\beta} e^{-c ( (\mu + s) t^2 )^{1/4} } {\rm d} s \le O( t^{2\beta -2} ) e^{- c' ( ( \mu + a) t^2 )^{1/4}} .
\end{align}

