[Theorem 2 of arXiv:2604.22257, 'On necessary and sufficient conditions for the local large deviation principle'] {\rm (G\"artner--Ellis)}
Assume that, for any $\mu\in \R^d$, there exists the limit
\begin{align}

\Ao (\mu):=\lim_{T\to\infty}\frac1T \ln \exn e^{T \langle \mu, \ze_T\rangle } \in (-\infty, \infty]
\end{align}
which  is essentially smooth and, moreover,  $0 \in \intr{\doma}$. Then the LDP is satisfied for $\{\ze_T\}$ with the rate function $D=\mathcal L_\Ao$ for which condition~\eqref{GoodRF} is met. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem 17 of arXiv:2512.02538, 'On the spectral geometry of Liouville quantum gravity'] Let $N(\lambda) = \sum_{n=0}^\infty 1_{\{\lambda_n \le \lambda\}}$ denote the eigenvalue counting function. Then 
\begin{equation}
\frac{N(\lambda)}{\lambda} \to c_0 |\Sigma|
\end{equation}
as $\lambda \to \infty$. Here $c_0 = 1/ (2\pi)$ and $|\Sigma|$ denotes the Lebesgue measure of $\Sigma$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

