[Proposition prop:p_moments of arXiv:2606.00325, 'Ergodicity for a class of stochastic Hasegawa-Mima equations with dissipation'] Let $\phi_0 \in L^p_{\mathcal{F}_0}(\Omega;  V)$. The unique solution of (eq:main of the paper) in the sense of (def-sol-H1 of the paper) satisfies, for every $p\ge 1$ 
    \begin{align}
        &\mathbb{E}\left[\sup_{t\in [0, T]} (|\phi(t)|^{2p} + |\nabla\phi(t)|^{2p}) + \left(\int_0^T \|\phi(s)\|_V^2 ds\right)^p \right] \lesssim 1
    \end{align}
    Moreover, for every $\alpha < 1/2$ it holds 
    $$\mathbb{E}\left[ \|(I-\Delta)\phi\|_{W^{\alpha,p}(0, T; W')}\right] \le C$$

[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2608.17562, '2608.17562'] Let $h : \R \to \R$ be a $1$-Lipschitz function and $\alpha$ a positive scalar. Then, for every $x \in \Rp$ we have 
\begin{align}
  xg_{h}'(x) &= -\alpha\int_0^{x}e^{{x^{-\alpha}}-{u^{-\alpha}}}h'(u)\dif u 
  \\
&= -\alpha (h(x) - h(0)) + \alpha^2 \int_0^{x} (h(u) - h(0))
e^{{x^{-\alpha}}- {u^{-\alpha}}  }\frac{\dif u}{u^{\alpha + 1}} .
\end{align} 
Consequently, the function $x \mapsto xg_{h}'(x)$ is $2\alpha$-Lipschitz on $(0,\infty)$.
 Furthermore, if $\alpha < 1$ and $h \in \mathcal{H}_b$ for some $b \in (0,\alpha)$, then the following bounds holds:
\begin{align}
x\vert g'_{h}(x) \vert \leq 2\alpha x^b,\quad x \in \Rp. 
\end{align}

