[Lem 6 of arXiv:2606.07194, 'Survival Probability of Markov Linear Reccurence Sequence in a Random Environment: Subcrit'] i) The process is strongly subcritical iff for some positive $\delta$ and natural $i$
\begin{equation}

\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} {\bf P}(Y_n>0|Y_0=i) s^n = +\infty
\end{equation}
for some $s: s\rho^+<1$. Moreover, $1/\rho$ is the radius of convergence of series~(\ref{ProbPowerSeries}).\\
ii) Let $1/\rho^*(h)$ be the radius of convergence of the series
\begin{equation}

\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} {\bf E}(Y_n^h|Y_0=i) s^{n},\  h\in (0,\widehat{h}).
\end{equation}
Let $h^*_{++}$ be the solution of the equation
$$
R(h) = \rho,\ R'(h)>0,
$$
where if there's no solution, we say that $h^*_{++}=+\infty$. Then
$$\rho^*(h)=\left\{
\begin{array}{cc}
\rho,& h<h^*_{++},\\
R(h),& h\in [h^*_{++},\widehat{h}).
\end{array}
\right.
$$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem:ap1:lyapunov1 of arXiv:2412.07710, 'An H-theorem for a conditional McKean-Vlasov process related to interacting diffusions on '] Suppose $f:[0, T]\times \ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^m \rightarrow \ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^m$  and $\mu_0 \in \mathcal{P}(\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^m)$ satisfy the conditions of Theorem (thm:ap1:wellPosed2 of the paper). Let $g: \ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^m \rightarrow \ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}$ be a $C^1$ function such that $\nabla g$ satisfies a linear growth condition. Let $\{\mu_t\}_{t \in [0, T]}$ be the weak solution to (equation eq:ap1:formalPDE of the paper), which exists by (1) of Theorem (thm:ap1:wellPosed2 of the paper). Then for almost every $0 < r < t < T$, we have
\begin{equation}
    \begin{split}
        \int_{\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^m} \mu_t \big( \log \mu_t + g \big) dx - &\int_{\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^m} \mu_r \big( \log \mu_r + g \big) dx = \\
        & - \int_r^t \int_{\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^m} (\nabla \mu_s + f_s \mu_s) \cdot \bigg(\frac{\nabla \mu_s}{\mu_s}  + \nabla g \bigg) dx ds.
    \end{split}

\end{equation}

