[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2608.23462, '2608.23462'] Suppose that Assumption~\ref{assu:frozenLipschitz} is satisfied, that $(\hat Y^x_t)_{t \geq 0}$ is $2$-dissipative and that $f$ is $L_f$-Lipschitz. Then,
    $\Phi: \R^{d_1+d_2} \to \R^{d_1}$ defined in \eqref{eq:Phiproofs} is well-defined and there exists a constant $C > 0$ such that  
    \begin{align} 
    |\Phi(x,y)| \leq  C(1+|y|) \quad \text{ for all } x\in \R^{d_1}, y \in \R^{d_2}.
    \end{align}
    Moreover, the averaged function $\bar{f}$ is Lipschitz-continuous.

