[Lemma of arXiv:2606.11951, 'On Skorokhod Problems for Reflected and Singular Stochastic Heat Equations'] The process $X^a$ is almost surely greater than or equal to zero at $a$, i.e.\ it holds
	\begin{equation*}
		\mathbb{P}_z[\mkern1.5mu \overline{\mkern-1.5mu X_t^a \mkern-1.5mu}\mkern1.5mu(a) \geq 0 \text{ for a.e. } t\in [0,\infty)] = 1 \quad \text{for all } z\inL.
	\end{equation*}
	Further, in the sense of random measures on $[0,\infty)$, it holds
	\begin{equation*}
		\mathds{1}_{ \{ z\in[C_0] \mid \bar{z}_a=0 \} }(X^a_s) \, dL_{s}^{\var{\sigma^{(a)}}} = dL_{s}^{\var{\sigma^{(a)}}} \quad \text{$P^a_z$-a.s.\ for $\mathcal{E}^a$-q.e.\ } z\inL. 
	\end{equation*}

[Lemma lem:Bounds_on_q of arXiv:2411.10113, 'Long-range one-dimensional\\ internal diffusion-limited aggregation'] Suppose that~(equation ass:irreducible of the paper) holds, and
  that~(equation ass:stable-alpha of the paper) holds with $\alpha \in (1,2)$. Let $q_{\alpha} (y; c)$ be as defined in~(equation eq:q_limit_integral of the paper). 
Then it holds that, for every  $c>0$ and all $0 \leq y < 1$,
  \begin{equation}

      q_\alpha (y ; c) \geq (\alpha -1 ) c^{1-\frac{\alpha}{2}} ( c+y)^{\frac{\alpha}{2} -1} ( 1-y),\end{equation}
      and, moreover, for every $c >0$,
 \begin{equation}

      \lim_{y \to 0} q_\alpha (y ; c)  = 1. \end{equation}
       On the other hand, for every $\delta>0$ it holds that
 \begin{equation}

 \sup_{\delta \leq y \leq 1} q_{\alpha} (y; c) < 1.
 \end{equation}

