body:
[Lemma lem:orderSopen of arXiv:2603.16824, 'Age-dependent random connection models with arc reciprocity: clustering and connectivity'] Consider \(S(t_o)\) as defined in~(equation eq:defS of the paper). Then,
\begin{equation}
\int_{1/(t\log t)}^1 S(t_o)\,\mathrm{d} t_o \asymp    
	\begin{cases}
    	1 & \text{if } \gamma < \tfrac{1}{2},
		\\
		(\log t)^{1+\1{\{\Gamma=0\}}} & \text{if } \gamma = \tfrac{1}{2},
		\\
        (t\log t)^{2\gamma-1}(\log t)^{\1\{\Gamma=0\}} & \text{if } \gamma > \tfrac{1}{2}.
	\end{cases}
\end{equation}
In particular, if \(\gamma<1/2\), then \(\int_{1/(t\log t)}^1 S(t_o) \,\mathrm{d} t_o\) is uniformly bounded in \(t\).

