[Prop 67 (Estimates for moments of the increments of QVF in all dimensions) of arXiv:2510.22155, 'Random walks in space-time random media in all spatial dimensions: the full subcritical fl'] Fix $k\in\mathbb N$, $T>0$, and $F:[0,\infty)\to[0,\infty)$ decreasing and of exponential decay at infinity. Let $f(x):=F(|x|)$. 

If the sequence of initial data $\mathfrak H^N(0,\bullet)$ is a good sequence in the sense of Definition \ref{goodseq}, then we have that there exists $C = C(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{i.c.}},k,d,f)$ such that \begin{align}

			\sup_{N\ge 1}\Ex\big[ (Q_N^f(t,\phi)-Q_N^f(s,\phi))^{k}\big]\leq C\|\phi\|^{k}_{L^\infty(\mathbb R)}\cdot (t-s)^{k\e}.
		\end{align}
        where $\e$ is as in Definition \ref{goodseq}.

