{"artifact_digest":"sha256:b1dac1a103317a67a7a602456620776a891552e68483f26a8e1d8c4c46faa6ff","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/b1/b1dac1a103317a67a7a602456620776a891552e68483f26a8e1d8c4c46faa6ff.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:e176f391ccadc39952381dea62552db5db3c7a781f8e78e5dc00f9094231d39f","bundle_entry_key":"2606-03534-theorem-20-generator-of-snake-with-absorb","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s3_044","claim_kind":"theorem","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-20260907/bundle_s3_044.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2606-03534-proposition-20-generator-of-snake-with-absorb","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: Take any $\omega \in \W$. If $\ell_\omega = 0$ then this remains constant, hence 
    \begin{align*}
        T(t)F(\omega) = \mathbb{E}_\omega \big[ F(\omega_t) \big] = \mathbb{E}_\omega \big[ F(\omega) \big] = F(\omega)
    \end{align*}
    and so the generator is equal to zero.

