[Thm surface sum representation in 't hooft limit of arXiv:2411.11676, 'Surface sums for lattice Yang--Mills in the large-$N$ limit'] There exists a number $\upbeta_0(d)>0$, depending only on the dimension $d$, such that the following is true. Let $\Lambda_1\subseteq\Lambda_2\subseteq\hdots$ be any sequence of finite subsets of the lattice $\mathbb{Z}^d$ such that $\mathbb{Z}^d = \cup_{N=1}^{\infty}\Lambda_N$. If $|\upbeta|\leq \upbeta_0(d)$, then for any string $s=\{\ell_1,\dots,\ell_n\}$,
\begin{align*}
	\lim_{N\to\infty}\phi_{\Lambda_N,N,\upbeta}(s) =
	\prod_{i=1}^n\phi(\ell_i),
\end{align*}
where
\begin{equation*}
	\phi(\ell)=\sum_{K:\mathcal{P}_{\mathbb{Z}^d}\to\mathbb{N}} \phi^K(\ell), \quad\text{with}\quad \phi^K(\ell)=\sum_{M\in\mathcal{N}\mathcal{P}\mathcal{M}(\ell,K)}\upbeta^{\area(M)}w_{\infty}(M),
\end{equation*}
and the infinite sum $\phi(\ell)$ is only over finite plaquette assignments $K:\mathcal{P}_{\mathbb{Z}^d}\to\mathbb{N}$, i.e.\ plaquette assignments such that $\sum_{p\in\mathcal{P}_{\mathbb{Z}^d}}K(p)<\infty$. Moreover, the infinite sum $\phi(\ell)$ is absolutely convergent. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem:on_Yn_Y-infty of arXiv:2607.16911, 'Multipartite random graphs with given degrees: local limit, revisiting the giant, distance'] \begin{itemize}
    \item [(a.)] For all $n$ sufficiently large but fixed, the process $\mathcal Y_n$ survives forever with positive probability. 
    \item [(b.)] The process $\mathcal Y_\infty$ also survives forever with positive probability.
    \item [(c.)] Moreover, denoting by $\chi_n$ the survival probability of $\mathcal Y_n$, we have
    \begin{align*}
        \lim_{n \to \infty} \chi_n=\chi,    \end{align*} where $\chi$ is the survival probability of $\mathcal Y_\infty$.
\end{itemize}

