[Thm cokernel distribution theorem 1_intro of arXiv:2505.11700, 'Distribution of the cokernels of determinantal row-sparse matrices'] (Theorem (thm: cokernel distribution theorem 1 of the paper)) Let $G$ be a finite abelian group and $\mathcal{P}$ be a finite set of primes including those dividing $|G|$. 
Assume that a sequence $(k_n)_{n=1}^{\infty}$ satisfies the following:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item for every prime $p$ in $\mathcal{P}$, $p \nmid k_n$ for all sufficiently large $n$;
    \item for every $\epsilon>0$, $k_n < n^{\epsilon}$ for all sufficiently large $n$;
    \item  if $2 \in \mathcal{P}$, then for every $\delta>0$, $\delta \log\log n < k_n$ for all sufficiently large $n$.
\end{enumerate}
Then
$$
\lim_{n\to \infty} \mathbb{P}\left(\bigoplus_{p \in \mathcal{P}} \mathrm{cok}(A_n)_p \cong G\right) = \frac{1}{|\mathrm{Aut}(G)|}\prod_{p\in \mathcal{P}} \prod_{i=1}^\infty (1-p^{-i})
= \prod_{p \in \mathcal{P}} \nu_{\mathrm{CL}, p}(G_p).
$$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 11 (Normalized Fourier expansion) of arXiv:2606.26065, 'Localized Centered Second-Chaos Operators'] Let $K>4d$.  On the support of the four dyadic cutoffs, every amplitude $m$ with finite norm~\eqref{eq:symbol-norm} admits an expansion
\begin{equation}
 m(\ell,\eta,q,n)
 =\sum_{\nu\in\mathbb Z^{4d}}c_\nu
 e^{i\theta_1\nu_1\cdot\ell/N}
 e^{i\theta_2\nu_2\cdot\eta/N}
 e^{i\theta_3\nu_3\cdot q/Q}
 e^{i\theta_4\nu_4\cdot n/M},
\end{equation}
where the $\theta_j$ depend only on a fixed normalized box and
\begin{equation}
 \sum_\nu|c_\nu|
 \lesssim_{d,K}\norm{m}_{\Mclass^K_{N,Q,M}}.
\end{equation}

