[Lemma lem:mixed_tail_finite_ambient_pointwise of arXiv:2609.01576, '\normalfont Pointwise Majorization for sub-Weibull and Mixed Tail Processes with Applicati'] There exists a finite constant $B_{\alpha_1,\alpha_2}$, depending only
on $\alpha_1$ and $\alpha_2$, such that, for every finite set
$K\subseteq T$ containing $t_0$ and every $u\ge1$, with probability at
least $1-e^{-u}$, simultaneously for every $t\in K$, we have
\begin{align*}
\|Z_t\|
\le
B_{\alpha_1,\alpha_2}
\cbr{
\Phi_1(t)+\Phi_2(t)
+
u^{1/\alpha_1}v_1(t)
+
u^{1/\alpha_2}v_2(t)
}.
\end{align*}

