    where all $(\beta_j,\rho_j)$ satisfy the (sub-)criticality condition $\frac{1}{2}\le \frac{1+\rho_j}{\rho_j}(1-\beta_j)$. Hence, by~\cite[Remark~4.2]{agrestiNonlinearSPDEsMaximal2025} we can conclude that $\|\psi(u,\grad u)\|_{\sL_2(\ell^2,H^1)}$ is in $L^2(0,\sigma_m)$ since $u\in L^2(0,\sigma_m;V)$ by local","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:28e8833aa7752f51030eab78ba30efd4a22fa7224fa325f9dc241937c2707c77","revision_digest":"sha256:3c926a895d647d7ab889946960ccf129711e35bf80ac221c39a78eb43231db09","source_id":"arxiv:2608.21014","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-07","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

