[Lemma qstabilitywedge of arXiv:2507.10545, 'KPZ equation from a class of nonlinear SPDEs in infinite volume'] \fsp Suppose {\small$\wt{\mathbf{Q}}^{N}:[0,\infty)\times\Z\to\R$} satisfies the following \abbr{SDE}, where {\small$\mathscr{T}_{N}$} is from Proposition (prop:s-sde of the paper):

\begin{align}
\d\wt{\mathbf{Q}}^{N}_{\t,\x}=\mathscr{T}_{N}\wt{\mathbf{Q}}^{N}_{\t,\x}\d\t+\sqrt{2}\lambda N^{\frac12}\wt{\mathbf{Q}}^{N}_{\t,\x}\d\mathbf{b}_{\t,\x}.
\end{align}

Suppose also that the initial data is non-negative, possibly random, and satisfies the deterministic bounds

\begin{align}
\sup_{\x\in\Z}\mathrm{e}^{\t\mathscr{T}_{N}}[\wt{\mathbf{Q}}^{N}_{0,\cdot}]_{\x}\lesssim\t^{-1/2}\quad\mathrm{and}\quad N^{-1}\sum_{\x\in\Z}\wt{\mathbf{Q}}^{N}_{0,\x}\lesssim1.
\end{align}

Next, suppose that for any {\small$\t>0$} fixed, the function {\small$\X\mapsto\mathrm{e}^{\t\mathscr{T}_{N}}[\wt{\mathbf{Q}}^{N}_{0,\cdot}]_{N\X}$} converges uniformly in {\small$\X\in\R$} to {\small$\mathbf{H}_{0,\t,\X,0}$}. Then, there exists a coupling between {\small$\wt{\mathbf{Q}}^{N}$} and the narrow-wedge solution {\small$\mathbf{Z}^{\mathrm{nw}}$} to (equation eq:she of the paper) so that for any fixed and small {\small$\tau>0$}, we have {\small$\wt{\mathbf{Q}}^{N}_{\t,N\X}-\mathbf{Z}^{\mathrm{nw}}_{\t,N\X}\to0$} locally uniformly on {\small$[\tau,1]\times\R$} in probability.

[Lem comparison of arXiv:2605.06488, 'Continuous-state branching processes with L\'evy-Khintchine drift-interaction: Laplace dua'] Let $\epsilon\in (0,1)$. Call $X^{\mathrm{m},(\epsilon)}$ the unique strong solution, with $0$ and $\infty$ absorbing, to
   \begin{equation*}
   Z_t=x+\int_{0}^{t}\sqrt{2\mathrm{a}Z_s}\mathrm{d} B_s+\int_{0}^{t}\int_{0}^{Z_{s-}}\int_{(0,\epsilon]}u\bar{\mathcal{N}}(\mathrm{d} s,\mathrm{d} r, \mathrm{d} u)-\gamma_{\epsilon}\int_0^tZ_s\mathrm{d} s-\int_0^{t}\hat{\Psi}(Z_s)\mathrm{d} s,
   \end{equation*}
   with $\gamma_{\epsilon}:=|\gamma|+\int_\epsilon^{1}u\pi(\mathrm{d} u)\in (0,\infty)$ and $B$ and $\mathcal{N}$ are those of Equation (equation SDECBDI of the paper). The process $X^{\mathrm{m},(\epsilon)}$ is a minimal $\mathrm{CBDI}(\Sigma^{\epsilon},\hat{\Psi})$ process with subcritical branching mechanism 
   \begin{equation}\Sigma^{\epsilon}(x):=\mathrm{a}x^2+\gamma_{\epsilon}x+\int_{(0,\epsilon]}(e^{-ux}-1+ux)\pi(\mathrm{d} u), \ \ x\in [0,\infty).\end{equation}
   Moreover, for all $x\in (0,\infty)$,
   \[X^{\mathrm{m},(\epsilon)}_t(x)\leq X^{\mathrm{m}}_t(x),\ \text{ for all } t\geq 0\ \text{ a.s..}\]

