[Definition 7 of arXiv:2608.03273, 'On the Asymptotic of Coupled Spherical Integrals: An Operator-Valued Extension of the Free'] An RV $X$ with mean $\mu=\mathbb E[X]$ is sub-exponential if there are non-negative parameters $(\nu, \chi)$ such that
    \begin{equation*}
        \mathbb E\left[
            \exp \left\{
                \gamma (X-\mu)
            \right\}
        \right]
        \leq
        \mathrm{e}^{\frac{\nu^2\gamma^2}{2}} 
        ~\forall |\gamma|<\frac{1}{\chi}
    \end{equation*}

