[Lemma 13 (Odlyzko for the comparison columns) of arXiv:2606.25204, 'Exponential Rank Bounds for Random Matrices'] For every \(j\in[n]\) and every affine subspace \(W\subseteq\R^n\) of
codimension \(r\),
\begin{equation}
   \PP\{Y_j\in W\}\leq \lambda_{4.1}^r.
\end{equation}

[Proposition prop:turning_point of arXiv:2603.27906, 'Marked GUE-corners process in doubly periodic dimer models'] For~$k=1,\dots,\ell$, set~$a_k=\alpha_k\beta_{k-1}^{-1}$ and~$b_k=\alpha_k^{-1}\beta_k$. Then
\begin{equation}
\tau =
\sum_{k=1}^\ell \frac{1+a_k+a_kb_k+a_kb_ka_{k+1}}
{(1+a_k)(1+b_k)(1+a_{k+1})}
\end{equation}
where~$a_{\ell+1}=a_1$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2608.18075, '2608.18075'] There is a Borel set
$\mathsf Y_*\subset\mathsf G_\vartheta$, where
\begin{align*}
 \mathsf G_\vartheta
 =\{(\zeta,\zeta(\tau)):
       \zeta\in c_0^\vartheta([0,\tau];H^b)\}\subset\mathsf Y,
\end{align*}
such that $\mathbf P_Y(\mathsf Y_*)=1$ and the following statements hold
simultaneously for every $Y\in\mathsf Y_*$ and every $z\in\mathsf X$:
the endpoint $\Phi(z,Y)$ is globally defined, and
\begin{align}
 \overline{\Ran A(z,Y)}=E_{\Phi(z,Y)}.
\end{align}
If $z\in H^b\times\mathcal V_j$ and
$\Phi(z,Y)\in H^b\times\mathcal V_k$, the fixed space representatives
\begin{align*}
 J_{kj}(z,Y)&=\mathfrak T_k(\Phi(z,Y))^{-1}
               J(z,Y)\mathfrak T_j(z),\\
 A_k(z,Y)&=\mathfrak T_k(\Phi(z,Y))^{-1}A(z,Y)
\end{align*}
are continuous in operator norm on their common domain.

