body:
[Theorem of arXiv:2605.18712, 'Faster random walks via infrequent steering'] For all $L$ and $\varepsilon >0$, there is $C$ such that if $G$ is a connected graph with
    \begin{equation}\label{ballbound}\sum_{k=0}^\infty |B^k(v)|(1 - \varepsilon )^{k} < L\end{equation}
    for every $v \in V(G)$,
    then
    \[T(G,\varepsilon ) < Cn.\]

