[Lemma exponential_bound_Nt of arXiv:2512.06640, 'Existence and sharpness of the phase transition for the frog model on transitive graphs'] Let $S \subset V$ be a finite set containing the origin. For $x \in S$ define $D_x := d_{\vec{G}}(x, S^c).$ We have that for any $t > 0$ and $x\in S:$
\begin{equation}
\mathbb E_x\left[ N(t) \, \big\vert \, \tau_{S^c} \le t \right] \leq \Delta^{D_x} (t + D_x) \, .
\end{equation}

