[Lemma lem:shift_NM of arXiv:2411.14818, 'Scaling limits of solitons in the Box-Ball system'] {Assume that $\eta \in \Omega$.} For any $k, \ell, h \in {\mathbb{N}}$, $i \in {\mathbb{Z}}$ and $n \in {\mathbb{N}}$, we have 
            \begin{align}
                N^{(i)}_{k + h,\ell + h}\left(\eta, n\right) &= N^{(i)}_{k,\ell}\left(\Psi_{h}\left(\eta\right), n\right),  \\
                M^{(i)}_{k+h}\left(\eta, n\right) &= M^{(i)}_{k}\left(\Psi_{h}\left(\eta\right), n\right) .
            \end{align}
        In particular, (equation eq:shift_M_k of the paper) implies 
            \begin{align}
                Y^{\left(i\right)}_{1}\left(\Psi_{k-1}\left(\eta\right), n\right) = n - M^{(i)}_{k}\left(\eta, n\right). 
            \end{align}

