{"artifact_digest":"sha256:7e54d2d9b30625e30ce58f7fd8cae3aee9d753e65bffd262b8954168b70d3801","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/7e/7e54d2d9b30625e30ce58f7fd8cae3aee9d753e65bffd262b8954168b70d3801.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:6d346810bb3d2fd52ec50dcca2507601e38d8b4f9ff15339b8f2c1100d52559f","bundle_entry_key":"2609-02788-lemma-8-parity-weighted-inner-comparis","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s3_154","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-20260907/bundle_s3_154.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2609-02788-lemma-8-parity-weighted-inner-comparis","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: The exact factorization \eqref{eq:oddexact} implies that the odd first-order
system is homogeneous.  In parity-adapted variables it has the form
\begin{equation}
 V_o'=A_o(U_e,V_o)V_o
\end{equation}
for the Ricci-flat equation.  The positive-Einstein equation has the same
Weyl parity and therefore can be written
\begin{equation}
 V_o'=\bigl(A_o(U_e,V_o)+b^2e^{2s}B_o(U_e,V_o;b)\bigr)V_o.
\end{equation}
Here $U_e$ denotes the Weyl-even variables.  Since the odd vector field is
odd under $V_o\mapsto -V_o$, Hadamard's formula gives a smooth factorization
for which the coefficient matrices are even:
