body:
[Theorem t02 of arXiv:2412.04015, 'Linear fluctuation of interfaces in Glauber-Kawasaki dynamics'] Fix a function $G\colon {\mathbb T}^d_N \to {\mathbb R}$, and a finite subset $A$
of ${\mathbb Z}^d$ with at least two elements. Assume that
$\sup_{N\ge 1} K^2_N / \ell^d_N < \infty$. Then, there exists a finite
constant ${\mathfrak c}({\boldsymbol u}^N)$ which depends only on ${\boldsymbol u}^N$, the set
$A$, the dimension $d$, and is uniformly bounded in $N$, such that
\begin{equation*}
K_N\, \int  {\mathcal W}^{G,A}
\, f\; d\nu^N \; \le\;
\delta \, N^2\, I^E_{N}(f;\nu^N)
\;+\; {\mathfrak c}({\boldsymbol u}^N)\, \frac{1}{\delta}\, \{\, 1 + \Vert
G\Vert^2_\infty\,\} \, K^2_N
\, \big\{ H_N(f) \,+\, (N/\ell_N)^d \, \big\} 
\end{equation*}
for all $0<\delta<1$, density $f$ with respect to $\nu^N$ and
$N\ge 1$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

