[Theorem thm:growing-lower of arXiv:2605.16244, 'Analysis of a twisted Bose--Einstein Markov chain with applications to sampling Catalan st'] If $m_*\ge2$, then, for every $t\ge0$,
\begin{equation}
 d(t)
 \ge\overline d(t)
 \ge
 1-\frac{t\mu+\log(2+1/\theta)}{\log m_*}.
\end{equation}
Consequently, for every $0<\varepsilon<1$,
\begin{equation}
 t_{\mathrm{mix}}(\varepsilon)
 \ge\overline t_{\mathrm{mix}}(\varepsilon)
 \ge
 \frac{(1-\varepsilon)\log m_*-\log(2+1/\theta)}
 {\mu}.
\end{equation}

