[Theorem 4 of arXiv:2607.07552, 'Weak convergence rate for the Cox--Ingersoll--Ross process'] Let $2\alpha\geq\theta^2$ and $f\in\mathcal{C}^{(2)}((0,\infty),\mathbb{R})$ be such that $|f^{(2)}(x)|\leq K(1+x^m)$ for some $m\geq 2$. Then
	\begin{equation}
		|\mathbb{E}^x[f(X_T)]-\mathbb{E}^x[f(\hat{X}_T)]|\sim\mathcal{O}\!\left({1\over N}\right).
	\end{equation}

