body:
[Proposition 33 of arXiv:2608.15914, 'Absorption cutoff and stationary singularities for rounded Gaussian random dynamical syste'] Let \cref{ass:gaussian-stable-selected} hold. Let $\nu_{A,N}$ be the unique
  nonzero invariant law of $K_{A,N}$. Then there are constants $C,c>0$ such that
  \begin{equation}
    \nu_{A,N}(I_\ast^c)\leq C e^{-cN}
  \end{equation}
  for all sufficiently large $N$. In particular,
  \begin{equation}
    \nu_{A,N}(I_\ast^c)\leq\frac{C}{N}
  \end{equation}
  after enlarging $C$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Prop comparison-SG-and-ST of arXiv:2411.03065, 'Growing conditioned BGW trees with\\ log-concave offspring distributions'] Let $n\geq1$ and let ${\boldsymbol{\uptheta}}$ be a summable sequence.
	Fix some $\tau\in\mathbbm{t}$ and $(T,{\boldsymbol{S}})\in\trees^{\rm gr}_n[\mathbb{S}]$ such that $\mathfrak{P}(\tau)=(T,{\boldsymbol{S}})$.
	If we write ${\boldsymbol{S}}=(S_\mathtt{u})_{\mathtt{u}\inT}$, then for every $n\geq1$ the following identity holds:
	\begin{align}
	\Sub{{\boldsymbol{\uptheta}}}{n}(\tau)=\SimpGen{{\mathbf{e}}({\boldsymbol{\uptheta}})}{n}(T)\cdot\prod_{\mathtt{u}\in T}\randSubset{{\boldsymbol{\uptheta}}}{k_\mathtt{u}(T)}(S_\mathtt{u}).
	\end{align}

