[Proposition 9 of arXiv:2606.01881, '2606.01881'] There exists a constant $c>0$ such that, for every $j\ge2$,
\begin{equation}
        \Pp(D_j\mid\mathcal F_{T_j})
        \ge 1-\exp(-cL_j)
        \qquad\text{a.s.}
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem:maximal-fluctuation-bound of arXiv:2605.08052, 'Rapid phase ordering of Ising dynamics on $\mathbb Z^2$'] There exists $C$ such that for all $\beta>\beta_0$, as long as $\ell \ge b-a\ge e^{\beta/5}$, one has for all $h$ that  
    \begin{align*}
        \pi_{\bar S}^\eta( \sigma: \lambda(\sigma) \text{ reaches } H^*_{h}) \le C (b-a)^{C}\exp( - \kappa_\beta (\tfrac{h^2}{b-a-1}\wedge h )) \qquad \text{for all }h
    \end{align*}

