[Definition nonlinear log sobolev of arXiv:2511.05223, 'Kac's Program and Relative Entropy Decay for Nonlinear Spin-Exchange Dynamics'] We say the reversible quadratic system associated to \(\ensuremath{\mathcal Q}_J^{\ensuremath{\mathcal K}}\) satisfies a \textbf{Nonlinear-Modified Log-Sobolev Inequality} of rate \(\alpha\), abbreviated as \(NMLSI(\alpha)\), if  for all 
 \(\mu'\in\ensuremath{\mathcal P}_J^\ensuremath{\mathcal A}(\Omega)\)
\begin{equation}
    \inf_{f}\frac{\mathcal{D}_{\mu'}(f, f)}{{\rm Ent}_{\mu'}F} \ge \alpha, 
\end{equation}
    where the \(\inf\) runs over all \(f:\Omega\to R_+\) such that \(f\mu'\) is a probability measure with \(\rho^\ensuremath{\mathcal A}(f\mu')=\rho^\ensuremath{\mathcal A}(\mu')\).

