[Prop 16 of arXiv:2604.12233, 'An upper bound on the smallest singular value of dense random combinatorial matrices'] \cite[Proposition 2.2]{rudelson2008least}
Let $Z_k$ be non-negative random variables for $k\in [n]$. Then for every $\varepsilon>0$, 
\begin{equation*}
    \P\lr{\frac{1}{n}\sum_{k=1}^nZ_k\le \varepsilon}\le \frac{2}{n}\sum_{k=1}^n\P(Z_k\le 2\varepsilon).
\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

