[Theorem Theo1 of arXiv:2511.19391, 'Central limit theorem for supercritical Crump-Mode-Jagers processes counted with non-indiv'] Suppose that assumptions (A1 of the paper)-(A7 of the paper) hold and  let $\varphi$ be an $h$-dependent descendant characteristic, for some $h \in \mathbb{N}_{0}$, satisfying (C1 of the paper)-(C5 of the paper). Then, as $t \rightarrow \infty$, $t \in \mathbb{G}$, 
\begin{align}
 e^{-\frac{\alpha}{2}t} \mathcal{Z}_{t}^{\varphi-\mathbb{E}[\varphi]} \xrightarrow[]{\rm st} \left( \frac{W}{\beta} \int_{\mathbb{G}} \mathbb{E}[(\chi^{(\varphi,h)}(s))^{2}] e^{-\alpha s} \ell( {\rm d} s) \right)^{1/2} \mathcal{N},
\end{align}
\noindent where $\beta \in (0, \infty)$ is defined in (equation eq3 of the paper), $W$ is the limit of Nerman's martingale and $\mathcal{N}$ is a standard normal random variable independent of $\mathcal{F}$ (and thus of $W$). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

