[Proposition 14 of arXiv:2604.19308, '\textbf{On McKean--Vlasov SDEs with polynomial drifts for SIS epidemic models}'] Assume that~\eqref{co:3},~\eqref{co:6} and~\eqref{co:7} are satisfied. Then
\begin{equation*}
\E\big[|\hat{I}_{t}^{(n)}|^{p}\big] \leq e^{k_{p,j,n}t}\E\big[\xi_{0}^{p}\big] + e^{l_{p,j,n}t}t\max_{i=0,\dots,j}\hat{b}_{0}(t_{i,n},N(t_{i,n}))
\end{equation*}
for all $n\in\N$, $j\in\{0,\dots,k_{n}-1\}$ and $t\in [t_{j,n},t_{j+1,n}]$ with the two non-negative constants
\begin{align*}
k_{p,j,n} &:= \max_{i=0,\dots,j} \big((p-1)\hat{b}_{0} + p(\hat{b}_{k+3} + c_{p}l^{2})\big)(t_{i,n},N(t_{i,n})),
\\
l_{p,j,n} &:= \max_{i=0,\dots,j} \big(2(p-1)\big(\hat{b}_{0} + c_{p}l^{2}\big) + (2p-1)\hat{b}_{k+3}\big)(t_{i,n},N(t_{i,n})).
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition eq:mu-mixture of arXiv:2607.27613, 'Regularized Bulk Universality versus Bounded-Disorder Nonuniversality\\for Annealed Comple'] \label[proposition]{prop:moment-law}
Fix an integer \(q\ge1\) and \(\sigma>1\).  There exists \(\varepsilon_0>0\) such that, for every \(0<\varepsilon<\varepsilon_0\), one can find a symmetric compactly supported \(C^\infty\) density \(\nu\) for which
\begin{equation}
 \mu=\varepsilon\mathcal N(0,\sigma^2)+(1-\varepsilon)\nu
\end{equation}
has the same moments as \(\mathcal N(0,1)\) through order \(2q\).  The density of \(\mu\) is strictly positive and \(C^\infty\), and \(\mu\) is sub-Gaussian.

