[Theorem 5 (Finite-time convergence of the unnormalized latent recursion) of arXiv:2608.22636, 'Q-Learning with Stable Infinite-Dimensional \\Linear Function Approximation'] Suppose Assumptions~\ref{assump:mdp}, \ref{assump:mix},
\ref{assump:stable_kernels}, and \ref{assump:stepsizes} hold. Moreover, choose $\alpha_{\mrm U}c_\wedge(1-\gamma)=:\lambda_\mrm U>1$ and set 
\begin{equation}
        \epsilon_n^{\mrm U}
        := \sqbk{(n+n_0^\mrm U)\crbk{ 2L_{0,\rho} + 5L_{\kappa,\rho}} \log\!\crbk{
        \frac{5 (n+n_0^{\mrm U})}{n_0^{\mrm U} }}}\inv.

\end{equation}
Then, for every $\delta\in(0,1)$,  with probability at least $1-\delta$, 
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
        \norm{\theta_n^{\mrm U}-\theta^*}&\le
        \frac{3}{1-\gamma}
        \sqbk{\frac{17 n_0^{\mrm U}}{n+n_0^{\mrm U}}}^{\lambda_{\mrm U}} +
        \frac{328\tmix}{c_\wedge (1-\gamma)^2}
        \sqbk{
        \sqrt{\frac{\alpha_\mrm U(\cL_n^\mrm U(\delta) + \log\cN_\rho(\epsilon_n^\mrm U))}{n+n_0^{\mrm U}}}
        +
        \frac{\alpha_{\mrm U}^{2}}{(\lambda_{\mrm U}-1)(n+n_0^{\mrm U})}}
\end{aligned}

\end{equation}
simultaneously for all $n\ge 16\alpha_\mrm U$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 12 (Endpoint estimates in the low-parameter rectangle) of arXiv:2608.30304, '2608.30304'] Let $n\ge1$ and $\alpha,\beta\in[-\tfrac12,A_0]$. If
