[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2609.02711, 'Differentiability of the Leading Lyapunov Exponent \\ of a linear differential equation wi'] Let $f:\R_+\to \R_+$ measurable such that for some $\ee>0$, the
  following limit exist and is finite
  \begin{equation}
    \lim_{t\to +\infty} \unsur{t} \intot f(s)^{1+\ee}\, ds =: m \in
    \R_+\,.
  \end{equation}

  Then, for any $\alpha>0$,
  \begin{equation}
    \lim_{t\to +\infty} \unsur{t} \intot e^{-\alpha s} f(s)\, ds = 0\,.
  \end{equation}

