[Lemma lem:finitecollision of arXiv:2601.10624, 'Source localisation in simple random walks'] Suppose $\mathbb{H}$ is an infinite, connected, vertex-transitive, recurrent graph of finite degree. Further, let $a$, $b \in \mathbb{H}$ be such that the transition probability $p_{2j}(a, b)$ is positive for some $j \geqslant 0$, and consider two independent simple random walks $X_t$, $Y_t$ on $\mathbb{H}$. Then, we have
    \begin{equation*}
        \mathbb{P}(\exists t > 0 \colon X_t = Y_t \mid X_0 = a, Y_0 = b) = 1.
    \end{equation*}

[Teorema 23 of arXiv:2506.11937, 'Random rotational invariance of integration by parts formulas within a Bismut-type approac'] A stochastic symmetry $\ T=(\Phi, B,\eta,h) \in S_m(M)$ is a $\mathcal{G}-$weak symmetry of $\ SDE_{\mu,\sigma}$ if and only if
    \begin{equation}
        \mu=\Big(\frac{1}{\eta}[L(\Phi)+D(\Phi)\sigma h]\Big)\circ\Phi^{-1}, \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \sigma \sigma^T=\Big(\frac{1}{\eta} D(\Phi) \sigma \sigma^T D(\Phi)^T\Big) \circ \Phi^{-1}.
    \end{equation}

