body:
[Lemma lem: X^p space of arXiv:2604.05941, 'Banach spaces of continuous paths with finite $p$-th variation'] [Dyadic case of Theorem 4.3 of [das-kim2024]]    
    For $x \in C([0, 1])$ with the Faber-Schauder representation (equation Eq: Schauder representation of the paper), we denote for any $p > 1$
    \begin{equation}    
        \xi^{(p)}_m := 2^{-\frac{mp}{2}} \Big( \sum_{k \in I_m} |\theta^x_{m, k}|^p \Big), \qquad m \ge 0.
    \end{equation}
    Then,
    \begin{equation*}
        x \in \mathcal{X}^p_{\mathbb{T}} \quad \text{if and only if} \quad \limsup_{m \to \infty} \, \xi^{(p)}_m < \infty.
    \end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem thm_main_dim of arXiv:2607.04002, 'Collisions of random walks in unimodular random graphs: applications to the random geometr'] Let~$G \in \{ \mathcal G_\mathrm{SGil},\mathcal G_\mathrm{Del}, \mathcal G_\mathrm{Gab} \}$. Then,
\begin{enumerate}
    \item for~$d=2$, the graph~$G$ has the discrete and continuous infinite collision property almost surely;
    \item for~$d \ge 3$, the graph~$G$ has the discrete and continuous finite collision property almost surely;
    \item for~$d \ge 2$, the tail~$\sigma$-algebra~$\mathcal T_\mathrm{rw}(G)$ is trivial almost surely. 
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem thm:vd-l2-wedge-free of arXiv:2609.00698, 'Kinetic Wedge Layers and Diffusive Limit of Neutron Transport in Polygonal Domains'] Let $\Omega$ satisfy (equation eq:vd-l2-angle-assumption of the paper), and suppose Assumption~(ass:vd-l2-data of the paper) holds. The unique bounded mild solution $u^\varepsilon$ of (equation eq:physical-model of the paper) belongs to the kinetic graph space $\mathscr W_{\rm kin}^2$ defined at (equation graph space of the paper). There is a constant $C_\Omega$, independent of $0<\varepsilon\leq1$, such that, with the endpoint-truncated leading side layer $\mathcal U_{\rm sl,0}^\varepsilon$ constructed in Section~(subsec:vd-l2-side-localization of the paper),
\begin{align}
 \nm{u^\varepsilon-\rho_0}_{L^2(\Omega\times\mathbb S^1)}
 +
 \nm{\pku^\varepsilon-\rho_0}_{L^2(\Omega)}
 &\leq
 C_\Omega\mathcal G_{\rm vd}\varepsilon^{\frac12},
 \\
 \nm{\mathcal U_{\rm sl,0}^\varepsilon}_{L^2(\Omega\times\mathbb S^1)}
 &\leq
 C_\Omega\mathcal G_{\rm vd}\varepsilon^{\frac12},
 \\
 \nm{u^\varepsilon-\rho_0-\mathcal U_{\rm sl,0}^\varepsilon}
 _{L^2(\Omega\times\mathbb S^1)}
 &\leq
 C_\Omega\mathcal G_{\rm vd}\varepsilon^{\frac12},
 \\
 \nm{\mathbf Q(u^\varepsilon-\rho_0-\mathcal U_{\rm sl,0}^\varepsilon)}
 _{L^2(\Omega\times\mathbb S^1)}
 &\leq
 C_\Omega\mathcal G_{\rm vd}\varepsilon,
 \\
 \abs{u^\varepsilon-\rho_0-\mathcal U_{\rm sl,0}^\varepsilon}_{2,+}
 &\leq
 C_\Omega\mathcal G_{\rm vd}\varepsilon^{\frac12}.

\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

