[Theorem 2 of arXiv:2604.11385, 'Quantitative large population limit for non exchangeable diffusions in Fisher information'] Let $T>0$ and $G_{1}, G_{2}$ two bounded graphons. Consider 
For $i \in \{1,2\}$ and $u \in [0,1]$, the two associated graphon particle systems
\begin{align*}
dX_{u}^{i}(t)=\int_{0}^{1} \int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}} b(X_{u}^{i}(s),x) G_{i}(u,v) P_{t}^{i,v}(dx)dvdt+  dB_{u}(t) 
          \quad \text{where} \quad     P_{t}^{i,v}=\text{Law}(X_{u}^{i}(t)).
\end{align*}
Let, for $u \in [0,1]$: $P_{[t]}^{i,u}=\text{Law}(X_{s}^{i,u}, s \in [0,t])$ and $H_{t}^{u}=H\left(P_{[t]}^{1,u}|P_{[t]}^{2,u}\right)$. Suppose 
\begin{itemize}
    \item b is bounded,
    \item $\displaystyle \forall u \in [0,1], \ H_{0}^{u} \leq C \left(\underset{u\in [0,1]}{\sup} \int_{0}^{1} \left| G_{1}(u,v)-G_{2}(u,v) \right| dv \right)^{2}.$
\end{itemize}
Then, there exists a constant $M_{T}$ (that does not depend on $u$) such that, for all $u \in [0,1]$,
\begin{equation*}
H_{T}^{u} \leq M_{T}  \left(\underset{u\in [0,1]}{\sup} \int_{0}^{1} \lvert G_{1}(u,v)-G_{2}(u,v) \rvert dv \right)^{2}.
\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

