    Let the probability measure $\nu$ on $\R^n$ have density $\nu(x) \propto \exp(-V(x))$ for all $x \in \R^n$. Suppose there is $\alpha > 0$ \st{} $\nabla^2 V(x) \succeq \alpha I_n$ for all $x \in \R^n$. Then, the following holds: 
    \begin{align*}
        \ent[\nu]{f^2} 
        \leq \frac 2 \alpha \cdot \E[\twonorm{\nabla f(X)}^2]
        \quad \text{and} \quad 
        \var[\nu]{f} 
        \leq \frac 2 \alpha \cdot \E[\twonorm{\nabla f(X)}^2].
    \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma diag:laxify of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] Let $T$ be a small $\infty$-category with a terminal object $1$, and let ${\mathcal{C}}$ be a small $T$-$\infty$-category such that for every $p\colon A\to1$ the functor $p^*\colon{\mathcal{C}}(1)\to{\mathcal{C}}(A)$ is fully faithful and admits a right adjoint $p_*$. Moreover, let ${\mathcal{E}}$ be any presentable (non-parametrized) $\infty$-category and denote by $\ul{\mathcal{E}}_T$ the category of $T$-objects in ${\mathcal{E}}$ (Example~(ex:T-objects of the paper)). Then a $T$-functor $F\colon{\mathcal{C}}\to\ul{\mathcal{E}}_T$ is left Kan extended from $\textup{const}\,{\mathcal{C}}(1)$ if and only if for every $A\in T$ and $X\in{\mathcal{C}}(A)$ the map $F(\varepsilon\colon p^*p_*X\to X)$ in $\ul{\mathcal{E}}_T(A)={\textup{Fun}}(T_{/A}^{\textup{op}},{\mathcal{E}})$ induced by the counit becomes an equivalence after evaluation at $\textup{id}_A$.
    \begin{proof}
        Write $\pi\colon\textup{const}\,{\mathcal{E}}\to\ul{\mathcal{E}}_T$ for the unique $T$-functor extending $\textup{const}\colon{\mathcal{E}}\to\ul{\mathcal{E}}_T(1)={\textup{Fun}}(T^{\textup{op}},{\mathcal{E}})$. By [LLP]*{Theorem~6.9} (for $M=\core T$), the individual right adjoints $\ul{\mathcal{E}}_T(A)\to{\mathcal{E}}$ (evaluating at $\textup{id}_A\in T_{/A}^{\textup{op}}$) assemble into a right adjoint $\rho\colon\textup{Un}^\text{cc}(\ul{\mathcal{E}}_T)\to\textup{Un}^\text{cc}(\textup{const}\,{\mathcal{E}})={\mathcal{E}}\times T^{\textup{op}}$ over $T^{\textup{op}}$ such that the composite
        \[
            {\textup{Fun}}_T({\mathcal{D}},\ul{\mathcal{E}}_T)\xrightarrow{\;\textup{Un}^\text{cc}\;}
            {\textup{Fun}}_{/T^{\textup{op}}}(\textup{Un}^\text{cc}({\mathcal{D}}),\textup{Un}^\text{cc}(\ul{\mathcal{E}}_T))\xrightarrow{\;\rho\circ{-}\;}
            {\textup{Fun}}_{/T^{\textup{op}}}(\textup{Un}^\text{cc}({\mathcal{D}}),{\mathcal{E}}\times T^{\textup{op}})
        \]        
        is an equivalence for every $T$-$\infty$-category ${\mathcal{D}}$. Applying this for ${\mathcal{D}}={\mathcal{C}}$ and ${\mathcal{D}}=\textup{const}\,{\mathcal{C}}(1)$ yields a commutative square
        \begin{equation}
            \begin{tikzcd}[cramped]
                {\textup{Fun}}_T({\mathcal{C}},\ul{\mathcal{E}}_T)\arrow[r,"\sim"]\arrow[d,"\textup{res}"'] & {\textup{Fun}}_{/T^{\textup{op}}}(\textup{Un}^\text{cc}({\mathcal{C}}),{\mathcal{E}}\times T^{\textup{op}})\arrow[d,"\textup{res}"]\\
                {\textup{Fun}}_T(\textup{const}\,{\mathcal{C}}(1),\ul{\mathcal{E}}_T)\arrow[r,"\sim"'] & {\textup{Fun}}_{/T^{\textup{op}}}({\mathcal{C}}(1)\times T^{\textup{op}},{\mathcal{E}}\times T^{\textup{op}})\rlap.
            \end{tikzcd}
        \end{equation}
        By [HA]*{Proposition 7.3.2.6${}^{\textup{op}}$}, the individual right adjoints $p_*\colon{\mathcal{C}}(A)\to{\mathcal{C}}(1)$ assemble into a right adjoint $\gamma\colon\textup{Un}^\text{cc}({\mathcal{C}})\to{\mathcal{C}}(1)\times T^{\textup{op}}$ over $T^{\textup{op}}$, so that the right-hand vertical arrow in $((diag:laxify of the paper))$ admits a \emph{left} adjoint given by precomposing with $\gamma$. On the other hand, the left-hand vertical arrow admits a left adjoint given by parametrized left Kan extension, and it follows formally that also the square where we pass to left adjoints vertically commutes.

        As we assumed each $p^*\colon{\mathcal{C}}(1)\to{\mathcal{C}}(A)$ to be fully faithful, the right adjoint $\gamma$ is a localization at the images of the counits $\varepsilon\colon p^*p_*X\to X$ for all $A\in T$ and $X\in{\mathcal{C}}(A)$. Thus, $F\colon{\mathcal{C}}\to\ul{\mathcal{E}}_T$ is in the image of the left adjoint of the left-hand vertical map (i.e., $F$ is left Kan extended) if and only if $\rho\circ\textup{Un}^\text{cc}(F)$ inverts the above counit maps. By the explicit fiberwise description of $\rho$, this is precisely demanding that each $F(\varepsilon)$ become an equivalence after evaluation at $\textup{id}_A\in T_{/A}^{\textup{op}}$.
    \end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

