[Prop 37 of arXiv:2507.08909, 'Annealed almost periodic entropy'] Let $\phi \in \B(\A,\rmM_k)_+$ be $\l$-normal, and form this $k$-tuple in $H_\l^{\oplus k}$:
	\begin{equation}
	\xi_i = [0,\dots,0,\xi,0,\dots,0]^\rm{T} \qquad (i=1,2,\dots,k),
	\end{equation}
	where only the $i^\rm{th}$ coordinate of $\xi_i$ is nonzero. Then there is a unique non-negative operator $T$ affiliated to $\l^{\oplus k}(\A)'$ such that $\xi_i \in \rm{dom}\,T$ for each $i$ and $\phi$ is associated to $\l^{\oplus k}$ by $T\xi_1$, \dots, $T\xi_k$. \qed (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

