[Corollary of arXiv:2603.12774, 'Synchronization by noise for stochastic differential equations driven by fractional Browni'] For every \( x \in \mathbb{R}^d \), we can find the measurable decomposition (up to null sets) \( \tilde{\mathcal{B}}  = \bigcup_{1\leq i\leq \tilde{N}} \mathcal{B}_{i,x} \) such that for each \( i \), \( \mathbf{P}(\mathcal{B}_{i,x}) = \frac{1}{\tilde{N}} \), and the following convergence holds in probability on \( \mathcal{B}_{i,x} \):
		\begin{align*}
			\lim_{t \to \infty} \left\Vert \phi^{t}_{\omega^-}(x) - b_{i}(\omega^-) \right\Vert = 0.
		\end{align*}
		\noindent{\bf Proof.\, }
		Set
		\begin{align*}
			\mathcal{B}_{i,x} := \left\{ \omega^- \in \mathcal{B} : \lim_{t \to \infty} \left\Vert \phi^{t}_{\omega^-}(x) - b_{i}(\omega^-) \right\Vert = 0  \text{(in probability)}\right\} \quad .
		\end{align*}
		\hfill $\Box$\smallskip\newline (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem thm:G-monotonicity of arXiv:2605.17082, 'Spectral Purification in Reversible Markov Chains: Hidden Parameters, Observable Equivalen'] For every relaxation trajectory with $g_0 \perp \mathbf{1}$,
\begin{equation}
G(k+1) \le G(k), \qquad \forall\, k \ge 0.
\end{equation}
Equality holds if and only if all active modes at step $k$ have the same $\lambda_i^2$. Under $\lambda_2 > \lambda_3$, equality occurs iff $\alpha_2(k) = 1$.

