[Proposition prop:delocwithdiagonal of arXiv:2604.24743, 'The impact of disorder and non-convex interactions on delocalisation of height functions'] There exist a probability $p_0 \in (0,1)$, an inverse temperature $\beta_{\mathrm{Deloc}, \times} \in (0 , \infty)$ and a constant $c_0 \in (0, \infty)$ such that, for any $p \geq p_0$, any $\beta \geq \beta_{\mathrm{Deloc}, \times}$ and any $L \in \ensuremath{\mathbb{N}}^*$,
\begin{equation*}
    \mathbb{E}_p^{\mathrm{site}} \left[ \mathrm{Var}^{\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}-\mathrm{GFF}, \times}_{L , \beta, r} \left[ \varphi(0) \right] \right] \geq c_0 \ln L.
