[Lem ;lpre1 of arXiv:2604.12462, 'Stochastic analysis of Beckner's and related functional inequalities'] Let $\vp \colon (0,\infty )\to \mathbb{R} $ be a $C^{2}$-function. Then, for every 
$0\le t\le 1$, it holds that 
\begin{align*}
 \ex [\vp (M_{t})]-\vp (M_{0})
 =\frac{1}{2}\int _{0}^{t}ds\,\ex \!\left[ 
 \vp ''(M_{s})|\dv _{s}|^{2}
 \right] .
\end{align*}

