\[
  Y_t = \sigma'\eta^{t}
      = \sigma \circ \tau_{ij}\eta^{t}
      = \sigma\eta^{m}\eta^{t}
      = \sigma\eta^{t+m}
      = X_{t+m},
\]
for all $t\in\mathbb{Z}$. Thus $\{Y_t\}$ is just the cyclic shift of
$\{X_t\}$ by $m$. Given any index window $W\subset\{0,\dots,2m-1\}$, set
$T$ with law proportional to $w(X_t)$ on $W$, and define $T' = T+m \pmod{2m}$.
