[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2609.04143, 'The Geometry of Real Anisotropic Bohnenblust--Hille Constants'] If $\sigma(\mathbf q)=0$, then $C_{\mathbf q}^{(m)}=1$. If $\sigma(\mathbf q)>0$, then
\begin{equation}
 C_{\mathbf q}^{(m)}
 \ge 2^{\frac{\sigma(\mathbf q)}{2}\left(1+(m-2)Y_1(\mathbf q)\right)}.
\end{equation}

[Prop condldpdef of arXiv:2609.02682, 'LDP for tensor forms'] Assume $Q_n$ is a sequence of random symmetric zero-diagonal $v$-tensors (independent of $\mathbf{X}$) such that
\begin{align}
\|W_{Q_n}-W_\infty\|_{\square^*}=o_{\mathbb P}(1),

\end{align}
for some deterministic $W_\infty\in\mathcal W_v$.

Then $N_n(Q_n,\phi,{{\bf X}})$ satisfies a conditional LDP (see~(cor:conditional-ldp of the paper)) with speed $n$ and the deterministic good rate function $J_{W_\infty}(\cdot)$ as in (NewLDP of the paper) (i). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lem l:300.3.10 of arXiv:2602.21277, 'A Limit in Law for the Cover Time and Last Visited Vertex of Wired Planar Domains'] For any fixed $u \geq 0$, 
	\begin{equation}
		\frac{|{\mathbf W}_n(u) \setminus {\mathbf W}_n^{k,\epsilon}(u)|}{\sqrt{n}} \overset{\mathbb{P}}{\longrightarrow}0,  
	\end{equation}
	in the limit as $n \to \infty$, followed by $k \to \infty$ and finally $\epsilon \to 0$.

